window.__DOC_SEARCH_INDEX=[{"u":"docs/changelog/","ti":"Changelog","c":"","s":[{"h":"Version 1.0.0 - 27 November 2026","a":"version-100---27-november-2026","t":"First release. Shop admin panel and POS POS terminal with hold and resume, split payments, returns from the till and receipts with a QR code. Sales, refunds, shifts and cash, and quotations. Products with variants, categories, brands and units, and bulk barcode label printing. Stock levels, batches with expiry, adjustments, transfers and stock takes. Tax rates, price lists, customer groups, discount rules, coupons and gift cards. Suppliers, purchase orders, reorder suggestions and purchase returns. Expenses, branches, customers, loyalty points, team, roles and permissions. Reports, an owner summary, backups, data export and an audit log. Payment methods, email and SMS settings, and multiple languages. Super admin panel Businesses, impersonation and feature rollout. Plans, payment gateways (Stripe, Razorpay, PayPal, Flutterwave), invoices and reports. Support inbox and announcements. Platform settings, legal pages, mail templates, languages, backups, file storage and system updates. Admins, roles and permissions, and an audit log, with two-factor sign-in. Platform Public website with an editor for sections, design, text, pictures and questions. Pricing page, sign-up, onboarding and a setup wizard. Demo mode with one-click demo logins. Browser-based installer with purchase code check. Scheduler for loyalty, subscriptions, summaries and backups."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Updating Previous FAQs Version 1.0.0 - 27 November 2026 Related"}]},{"u":"docs/faqs/","ti":"FAQs","c":"","s":[{"h":"The page has no CSS and looks like plain HTML","a":"the-page-has-no-css-and-looks-like-plain-html","t":"A leftover public/hot file makes the app load assets from a development server that is not running. Delete public/hot. If public/build is missing, run npm run build."},{"h":"I am redirected to /install","a":"i-am-redirected-to-install","t":"The database has no tables, or .env points at the wrong or an empty database. Check the DB_* values in .env. For a new site, run the web installer. For development, run php artisan migrate --seed."},{"h":"I get a 404 on /install","a":"i-get-a-404-on-install","t":"That is expected once installation finishes. The installer locks itself by writing storage/installed."},{"h":"My .env or config changes are ignored","a":"my-env-or-config-changes-are-ignored","t":"Run php artisan optimize:clear."},{"h":"Class or route not found after an update","a":"class-or-route-not-found-after-an-update","t":"Run composer install, php artisan migrate, npm install, npm run build, then php artisan optimize:clear. See Updating."},{"h":"The installer says the validation server cannot be reached","a":"the-installer-says-the-validation-server-cannot-be-reached","t":"Your host blocks outbound HTTPS (port 443) or DNS fails. Ask your host to allow it."},{"h":"The Scheduler shows \"Not running\" in Settings > System","a":"the-scheduler-shows-not-running-in-settings--system","t":"The cron entry is missing or failing. See Cron jobs."},{"h":"Do I need a queue worker?","a":"do-i-need-a-queue-worker","t":"No. See Queue worker."},{"h":"Uploads fail or show \"Upload too large\"","a":"uploads-fail-or-show-upload-too-large","t":"Raise upload_max_filesize and post_max_size. See PHP ini settings."},{"h":"Emails are not arriving","a":"emails-are-not-arriving","t":"With the default log mailer emails are only written to the log. Enter SMTP details under Settings > System email in the Super admin panel and send a test email."},{"h":"A business can only view data and cannot add or edit","a":"a-business-can-only-view-data-and-cannot-add-or-edit","t":"A business becomes read-only when its trial or grace period has ended. The owner needs to subscribe or renew. See Billing and plans. Run the scheduler so statuses stay up to date."},{"h":"Backups fail","a":"backups-fail","t":"mysqldump must be installed and reachable. Set BACKUP_MYSQLDUMP_PATH in .env if it is not on the PATH. See Backups."},{"h":"I locked myself out of the Super admin panel","a":"i-locked-myself-out-of-the-super-admin-panel","t":"Create another admin with php artisan platform:make-admin you@example.com --name=\"Your Name\" --role=\"Super admin\"."},{"h":"Do I need node_modules on the server?","a":"do-i-need-node_modules-on-the-server","t":"No. It is only used to build the CSS and JavaScript. Build on your computer with npm run build and upload the whole public/build folder. You need node_modules only if you build on the server, and you can delete it afterwards. See Deployment."},{"h":"A new menu item, such as Website, does not appear","a":"a-new-menu-item-such-as-website-does-not-appear","t":"Run php artisan optimize:clear. Then check that your role has the permission; Website needs settings.manage. See Website."},{"h":"How do I change the text or pictures of the home page?","a":"how-do-i-change-the-text-or-pictures-of-the-home-page","t":"In the Super admin panel under Website."},{"h":"How do I run a public demo?","a":"how-do-i-run-a-public-demo","t":"See Demo mode."},{"h":"What are the demo login details?","a":"what-are-the-demo-login-details","t":"On a demo site the login page shows three buttons that sign in with one click: Platform admin (admin@example.com), Business partner (owner@example.com) and Cashier (cashier@example.com), all with the password Demo@2026. You can change them with DEMO_ADMIN_EMAIL, DEMO_PARTNER_EMAIL, DEMO_CASHIER_EMAIL and the matching ..._PASSWORD values in .env. See Demo mode."},{"h":"The login page shows demo buttons on my live site","a":"the-login-page-shows-demo-buttons-on-my-live-site","t":"Set DEMO_MODE=false and DEMO_LOGIN_CARDS=false in .env, then run php artisan optimize:clear. Never leave demo logins on for a real site, and change or remove the sample accounts."},{"h":"I was sent to the login page with \"Your session expired and nothing was saved\"","a":"i-was-sent-to-the-login-page-with-your-session-expired-and-nothing-was-saved","t":"You sent a form after your session had ended, for example after leaving a page open for a long time. Sign in again; you return to the page you were on. Enter the change again, because it was not saved. On the sign-up and password pages the message is \"The page was open too long, so nothing was sent. Please try again.\""},{"h":"How do I change the picture behind the login page?","a":"how-do-i-change-the-picture-behind-the-login-page","t":"Upload a Login background under the Super admin panel's General settings. Without one, public/images/auth-bg.jpg is used (or a .jpeg, .png or .webp file with that name)."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Support Installation overview Previous Support Next Changelog The page has no CSS and looks like plain HTML I am redirected to /install I get a 404 on /install My .env or config changes are ignored Class or route not found after an update The installer says the validation server cannot be reached The Scheduler shows \"Not running\" in Settings > System Do I need a queue worker? Uploads fail or show \"Upload too large\" Emails are not arriving A business can only view data and cannot add or edit Backups fail I locked myself out of the Super admin panel Do I need node_modules on the server? A new menu item, such as Website, does not appear How do I change the text or pictures of the home page? How do I run a public demo? What are the demo login details? The login page shows demo buttons on my live site I was sent to the login page with \"Your session expired and nothing was saved\" How do I change the picture behind the login page? Related"}]},{"u":"docs/installation/cron-jobs/","ti":"Cron jobs","c":"","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The application relies on the Laravel scheduler. You add one cron entry that runs every minute, and the application decides which tasks are due. Where to find it: your server's crontab."},{"h":"Add the cron entry","a":"add-the-cron-entry","t":"* * * * * php /path/to/project/artisan schedule:run >> /dev/null 2>&1 Use the full path to your project, and the PHP 8.3 binary if your server has several versions."},{"h":"What the scheduler runs","a":"what-the-scheduler-runs","t":"Command When What it does loyalty:expire Daily 00:10 Tidies expired loyalty point lots. loyalty:remind Daily 09:00 Sends loyalty-expiry reminders. summary:send Every 10 minutes Sends each business its owner summary once its local send time passes. payments:sweep-pending Every 5 minutes Settles or releases online payments whose customer never came back. backup:run Daily 02:00 Nightly database backup for businesses with automatic backup on. subscriptions:advance Daily 00:20 Moves ended trials, periods and grace to expired or cancelled. subscriptions:remind Daily 09:00 Sends trial and renewal reminder emails. platform:digest Mondays 08:00 Weekly platform summary to admins, if switched on. A heartbeat task runs every minute to prove the scheduler is working. note Times follow the server's configured timezone."},{"h":"Check it works","a":"check-it-works","t":"In the Super admin panel open Settings > System. Under System health, Scheduler shows Running. If it shows Not running (check the cron job) or No heartbeat yet, the cron entry is missing or failing. It counts as stale after 5 minutes without a heartbeat. Without the cron, trials and subscriptions are not advanced, reminders and summaries are not sent, and no nightly backups are made."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Queue worker Backups FAQs Previous PHP ini settings Next Queue worker Add the cron entry What the scheduler runs Check it works Related"}]},{"u":"docs/installation/demo-mode/","ti":"Demo mode","c":"","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Demo mode lets visitors try every panel while the important settings stay protected. Where to find it: the .env file in the project root. danger Never turn on demo mode or the demo login buttons (DEMO_MODE, DEMO_LOGIN_CARDS) on a real live site. Anyone who opens the login page could then sign in with one click, including as a platform admin. Keep both set to false on a site with real businesses and customers."},{"h":"Turn it on","a":"turn-it-on","t":"DEMO_MODE=true DEMO_BYPASS_EMAILS=you@yourcompany.com Then run php artisan optimize:clear. Variable What it does DEMO_MODE true turns demo mode on DEMO_LOGIN_CARDS Shows the demo login buttons on the sign-in page. Follows DEMO_MODE when not set DEMO_BYPASS_EMAILS Emails, separated by commas, that skip every demo restriction DEMO_PURCHASE_URL Where the Buy now button goes. Default: the POS SaaS page on the WRTeam marketplace DEMO_ADMIN_EMAIL, DEMO_PARTNER_EMAIL, DEMO_CASHIER_EMAIL Change the accounts behind the demo login buttons. Each has a matching ..._PASSWORD variable"},{"h":"Demo logins","a":"demo-logins","t":"When demo logins are on, the sign-in page (/login) shows Or try a demo account under the form, with three buttons. One click on a button signs the visitor in as that account straight away. There is nothing to copy or type. Button Opens Email Password Change with Platform admin The Super admin panel admin@example.com Demo@2026 DEMO_ADMIN_EMAIL, DEMO_ADMIN_PASSWORD Business partner The shop panel as the store owner owner@example.com Demo@2026 DEMO_PARTNER_EMAIL, DEMO_PARTNER_PASSWORD Cashier The shop panel as a cashier cashier@example.com Demo@2026 DEMO_CASHIER_EMAIL, DEMO_CASHIER_PASSWORD The buttons are shown when DEMO_LOGIN_CARDS=true, or when DEMO_MODE=true and DEMO_LOGIN_CARDS is not set. To show demo mode without the buttons, set DEMO_LOGIN_CARDS=false. Run php artisan optimize:clear after any change. The buttons only fill in and send the details above. The accounts must exist with that email and password. The demo seeder and demo:accounts below create or fix the default ones; if you change the emails or passwords with the variables, change the accounts to match. If you set ADMIN_DOMAIN, the Platform admin button sends the visitor to the admin sign-in page on that domain, where they sign in again. The full demo data, with three shops and months of sales, is created with: php artisan db:seed --class=LaunchDemoSeeder On a demo site that was seeded earlier with other emails, this renames the sample accounts and sets the password. It refuses to run on a live site. php artisan demo:accounts If the sample Super admin has two-factor on, visitors still need its code to sign in."},{"h":"What visitors cannot do","a":"what-visitors-cannot-do","t":"Super admin panel: save, change or delete anything. Reading is open, except downloading backups and opening the server logs. Shop panel: change settings, email and SMS settings, templates, gift card and loyalty settings, profile, password, roles, team and billing, or export and import data. Everyday work stays open: selling, products, stock, customers and purchasing. A Demo badge is shown in the header and a Buy now button in the bottom corner (on the POS terminal both are in the header). note Demo data is not reset automatically. Visitors can add and delete products, customers and sales."},{"h":"Your own unrestricted Super admin","a":"your-own-unrestricted-super-admin","t":"Create the account first. The password needs at least 12 characters: php artisan platform:make-admin you@yourcompany.com --name=\"Owner\" --role=\"Super admin\" Add the same email to DEMO_BYPASS_EMAILS and run php artisan optimize:clear. Sign in. You change the password and, when it is required, set up two-factor. This account is never shown on the demo login buttons."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Environment configuration Login and two-factor Previous Updating Turn it on Demo logins What visitors cannot do Your own unrestricted Super admin Related"}]},{"u":"docs/installation/deployment/","ti":"Deployment","c":"","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Put the application on your server and make the public folder the web root. Where to find it: Installation > Deployment."},{"h":"Steps","a":"steps","t":"Create an empty MySQL database and a database user. Upload the application files to your server (for example /var/www/pos). Set the document root of your domain to the public folder, not the project root. Make storage and bootstrap/cache writable by the web server user. Open your domain in a browser. You are redirected to /install. Continue with the web installer. warning Never expose the project root to the web. Only public should be reachable, otherwise your .env file can be downloaded."},{"h":"Dependencies and assets","a":"dependencies-and-assets","t":"The package you receive should include the vendor folder and the built assets in public/build. If either is missing, run these on the server (or locally, then upload): composer install --no-dev --optimize-autoloader npm install npm run build Folder or file Needed on the server? vendor, public/build Yes .env Yes, the server's own file. Never replace it with a local one node_modules No, unless you build on the server resources/js, resources/css Only if you build on the server public/hot Never upload it. It makes the site look for a development server tests, .git No"},{"h":"Separate admin domain","a":"separate-admin-domain","t":"By default the Super admin panel is at /admin. To serve it on its own host, set ADMIN_DOMAIN in .env (for example admin.example.com) and point that host at the same public folder. See Environment configuration."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Server requirements Web installer Cron jobs Previous Server requirements Next Web installer Steps Dependencies and assets Separate admin domain Related"}]},{"u":"docs/installation/environment-configuration/","ti":"Environment configuration","c":"","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The installer writes your .env file. You rarely need to touch it, but these are the values that matter. Most business settings live inside the panels, not in .env. Where to find it: the .env file in the project root."},{"h":"Key values","a":"key-values","t":"Variable What it does APP_NAME The application name. Set by the installer. APP_URL Your site's full address, for example https://example.com. APP_ENV production on a live site. APP_DEBUG Must be false on a live site. APP_KEY The encryption key. Never change it on a live site. DB_HOST, DB_PORT, DB_DATABASE, DB_USERNAME, DB_PASSWORD Database connection. ADMIN_DOMAIN Serve the Super admin panel on its own host (for example admin.example.com) instead of /admin. Leave empty to use /admin. BACKUP_MYSQLDUMP_PATH Path to mysqldump if it is not on the PATH. Used by backups. INSTALLER_VALIDATOR_URL Purchase code validator used by the installer. Leave the default. DEMO_MODE, DEMO_BYPASS_EMAILS and other DEMO_* values For a public demo site only. See Demo mode. LANDING_DEMO_URL The Live demo button's link until you save one under Website. SESSION_DRIVER, CACHE_STORE, QUEUE_CONNECTION Default to database. warning Changing APP_KEY makes saved encrypted values unreadable, such as gateway keys and SMS secrets. Back it up."},{"h":"Email","a":"email","t":"The .env mail values default to the log mailer, which only writes emails to the log. For real email, enter your SMTP details in the Super admin panel under Settings > System email, then use Send test email. Businesses can also use their own mail account in their email settings."},{"h":"After changing .env","a":"after-changing-env","t":"Clear cached configuration so the new values are read: php artisan optimize:clear"},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Web installer Cron jobs FAQs Previous Web installer Next PHP ini settings Key values Email After changing .env Related"}]},{"u":"docs/installation/first-login/","ti":"First login","c":"","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"After the installer finishes, you sign in with the Super admin account you created. Where to find it: /admin/login, or your ADMIN_DOMAIN host if you set one."},{"h":"Steps","a":"steps","t":"Open /admin/login and sign in with the admin email and password from the installer. Set up two-factor authentication when asked. See Login and two-factor. Open the dashboard. See Dashboard. Go to the platform settings and fill in the platform details, system email, plans and payment gateways."},{"h":"Businesses sign in elsewhere","a":"businesses-sign-in-elsewhere","t":"Shop owners and staff use /login, not /admin/login. If you installed demo data, a \"Demo Store\" business exists with sample products and customers. Its owner is owner@example.com and its cashier cashier@example.com, both with the password Demo@2026. Change these passwords or remove the store before you go live."},{"h":"Demo login buttons","a":"demo-login-buttons","t":"On a demo site the /login page shows three buttons under the form: Platform admin, Business partner and Cashier. One click signs in as that account. They appear only when DEMO_MODE or DEMO_LOGIN_CARDS is true in .env. Button Email Password Platform admin admin@example.com Demo@2026 Business partner owner@example.com Demo@2026 Cashier cashier@example.com Demo@2026 warning Keep demo mode and the demo login buttons off on a real live site. See Demo mode. tip If you lose access, create another admin from the server with php artisan platform:make-admin you@example.com --name=\"Your Name\" --role=\"Super admin\". It asks for a temporary password of at least 12 characters, which must be changed at first sign-in."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Platform overview Platform admins Cron jobs Previous Queue worker Next Localhost setup Steps Businesses sign in elsewhere Demo login buttons Related"}]},{"u":"docs/installation/localhost-setup/","ti":"Localhost setup","c":"","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"For development you set up the database with commands instead of the web installer. Where to find it: a terminal in the project folder."},{"h":"Requirements","a":"requirements","t":"PHP 8.3+, Composer 2, Node.js 20+ with npm, and MySQL 8 or MariaDB 10.6+. With XAMPP on macOS, use XAMPP's MySQL and make sure php -v shows 8.3 or newer."},{"h":"Steps","a":"steps","t":"Install dependencies and create the environment file: composer install cp .env.example .env php artisan key:generate Create an empty database (for example pos) and set APP_URL, DB_DATABASE, DB_USERNAME and DB_PASSWORD in .env. Create the tables and demo shop: php artisan migrate --seed php artisan storage:link npm install npm run build Start the app with php artisan serve and open http://127.0.0.1:8000. Create a Super admin: php artisan platform:make-admin you@example.com --name=\"Your Name\"."},{"h":"Logging in","a":"logging-in","t":"Where URL Login Shop owner /login owner@example.com / Demo@2026 Cashier /login cashier@example.com / Demo@2026 Super admin /admin/login The account you created in step 5 warning Never run php artisan db:seed on a live site. It creates the owner@example.com and cashier@example.com demo logins. note Open the site only after migrating. With no tables the app redirects to /install."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Environment configuration FAQs Previous First login Next Updating Requirements Steps Logging in Related"}]},{"u":"docs/installation/overview/","ti":"Installation overview","c":"","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"You install the application by uploading the files to your server, pointing the web server at the public folder, and running the web installer in your browser. Where to find it: Installation, the first page."},{"h":"The steps","a":"the-steps","t":"Check your server requirements. Deploy the files and set the document root to public. Open your site. It redirects to /install, the web installer. Finish the installer and create your Super admin account. Add the cron job. Sign in at /admin/login."},{"h":"Good to know","a":"good-to-know","t":"The installer needs an empty database. It never wipes an existing one. Once installation finishes, /install returns a 404 and cannot be run again. No default admin exists after installing. You create your own in the last installer step. There is no queue worker to configure. See Queue worker. Developers who want to run the code locally should read Localhost setup."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Environment configuration PHP ini settings Updating Next Server requirements The steps Good to know Related"}]},{"u":"docs/installation/php-ini-settings/","ti":"PHP ini settings","c":"","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The defaults of most hosts work. Adjust these only if you hit the problems described. Where to find it: your host's PHP settings, or php.ini."},{"h":"Uploads","a":"uploads","t":"Setting Why it matters upload_max_filesize The largest single file you can upload (product pictures, logos, expense receipts). post_max_size The largest total request. Keep it at or above upload_max_filesize. If a request is bigger than post_max_size, the application shows an Upload too large page: \"The upload was too large for the server, so nothing was saved. Use smaller pictures and try again.\" Raise both values or upload smaller files. Expense receipts that exceed the limit show a message asking for a smaller photo or PDF."},{"h":"Time and memory","a":"time-and-memory","t":"Setting Why it matters max_execution_time The Migrations installer step and backups can take a while. memory_limit Raise it if large reports or exports run out of memory."},{"h":"Required functions","a":"required-functions","t":"Keep symlink and proc_open enabled (not in disable_functions) and leave open_basedir unset. The installer checks them. See Server requirements."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Server requirements FAQs Previous Environment configuration Next Cron jobs Uploads Time and memory Required functions Related"}]},{"u":"docs/installation/queue-worker/","ti":"Queue worker","c":"","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"You do not need to run a queue worker. The application code does not queue jobs for emails, SMS or payments; they are handled in the request or by the scheduler. Where to find it: Installation > Queue worker."},{"h":"Configuration","a":"configuration","t":"QUEUE_CONNECTION defaults to database in .env. The Super admin panel shows Queued jobs and Failed jobs counts under Settings > System > System health. Both normally stay at 0."},{"h":"If you add a worker anyway","a":"if-you-add-a-worker-anyway","t":"If you customise the application to queue work, run a worker under a process manager such as Supervisor: php artisan queue:work --tries=3 Restart it after each update with php artisan queue:restart."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Cron jobs Environment configuration Previous Cron jobs Next First login Configuration If you add a worker anyway Related"}]},{"u":"docs/installation/server-requirements/","ti":"Server requirements","c":"","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The installer checks these automatically on its Server requirements and Folder permissions screens. Check them first to avoid surprises. Where to find it: Installation > Server requirements."},{"h":"PHP","a":"php","t":"PHP 8.3.0 or newer is required. These extensions must be loaded: Extension Extension pdo_mysql mbstring fileinfo openssl tokenizer json curl bcmath ctype dom gd xml zip"},{"h":"PHP functions and settings","a":"php-functions-and-settings","t":"The installer has a PHP functions step. These must be satisfied: The symlink function is enabled (used for storage:link). The proc_open function is enabled. open_basedir is not set."},{"h":"Folders","a":"folders","t":"These must be writable by the web server: storage/framework storage/logs bootstrap/cache Other folders under storage also need to be writable, since uploads and backups are stored there."},{"h":"Database","a":"database","t":"MySQL 8 or MariaDB 10.6+. An empty database and a user with full rights on it."},{"h":"Other","a":"other","t":"Outbound HTTPS (port 443) so the installer can validate your purchase code, and for payment gateways and email. mysqldump on the server's PATH, only for backups. If it lives elsewhere, set BACKUP_MYSQLDUMP_PATH in .env. Cron access, to run the scheduler every minute. Node.js 20+ and npm, only if you build assets yourself. The built assets are what you deploy."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Deployment PHP ini settings Web installer Previous Installation overview Next Deployment PHP PHP functions and settings Folders Database Other Related"}]},{"u":"docs/installation/updating/","ti":"Updating","c":"","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Back up first, replace the code, then run the database migrations. With an update package (ZIP) you can do it from the panel instead: see System updates. Where to find it: a terminal on your server."},{"h":"Steps","a":"steps","t":"Back up your database and the storage folder. See Backups. Upload the new files over the old ones. Keep your .env file and the storage folder. Install dependencies and build assets if your package does not include them: composer install --no-dev --optimize-autoloader npm install npm run build If you build on your computer, replace the whole public/build folder on the server. node_modules is not needed there. Run the migrations: php artisan migrate --force Clear caches: php artisan optimize:clear Check the site and Settings > System > System health. warning Do not run db:seed or migrate:fresh on a live site."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Cron jobs Changelog FAQs Previous Localhost setup Next Demo mode Steps Related"}]},{"u":"docs/installation/web-installer/","ti":"Web installer","c":"","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The installer sets up the database and creates your Super admin account. It opens automatically when you visit an uninstalled site. Where to find it: Open your domain, or go to /install. Installer welcome screen"},{"h":"The screens","a":"the-screens","t":"Welcome. Lists what you need: app URL and database host, port, name, username and password. Click Next step. Server requirements. Shows each PHP version and extension as passed or failed. Fix failures and click Reload. See Server requirements. Folder permissions. Checks /storage/framework, /storage/logs and /bootstrap/cache. Purchase code. Enter your purchase code. It is verified against the WRTeam validator for your domain. There is no way to skip it. PHP functions. Confirms symlink and proc_open are enabled and open_basedir is off. Database. Enter Database host, Database port, Database name, Database user, Database password and Database prefix. The database must be empty. Migrations. Creates all tables and loads the base data. This can take a while, so do not close the page. Site and admin. See below. Finish. Shows your website address and admin login link. Site and admin step of the installer"},{"h":"Site and admin","a":"site-and-admin","t":"Field What it does Platform name The name of your platform, saved as the application name. App url Your site's address. Admin name Name of your Super admin account. Admin email The email you sign in with. Admin password At least 8 characters. Confirm admin password Repeat the password. Install demo data Optional. Adds a \"Demo Store\" business with sample products and customers, an owner owner@example.com and a cashier cashier@example.com (password Demo@2026 for both). Not for a live site. This step also generates the encryption key, writes the settings to .env (production mode, debug off) and creates the storage link."},{"h":"After installing","a":"after-installing","t":"On finish the installer locks itself and /install becomes a 404. Your first sign-in at /admin/login asks you to set up two-factor authentication. See First login."},{"h":"Troubleshooting","a":"troubleshooting","t":"Validation server could not be reached. Your host blocks outbound HTTPS on port 443 or DNS fails. Ask the host to allow it. Purchase code not valid for this site. If it is registered to another domain, reset it from your purchase account first. Database step fails. Check host, port, name, user and password, and that pdo_mysql is installed. The database must have no tables. Redirected to /install on an installed site. The database has no tables, or .env points to the wrong database. See FAQs."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Environment configuration Cron jobs First login Previous Deployment Next Environment configuration The screens Site and admin After installing Troubleshooting Related"}]},{"u":"docs/intro/","ti":"Introduction","c":"","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The application is a multi-tenant (SaaS) point-of-sale and back-office system. Shops sign up, pick a plan and run their business from one admin panel; you, the platform owner, manage everything from a separate Super admin panel."},{"h":"What is included","a":"what-is-included","t":"Part What it is Shop admin panel The back office each business uses: products, stock, purchasing, customers, expenses, reports and settings. POS terminal The checkout screen cashiers use to ring up sales, take payments and print receipts. Super admin panel Your own panel at /admin (or on its own domain). Manage businesses, plans, payment gateways, invoices, support, languages and backups. Public pages A landing page and a pricing page, plus sign-up for new businesses. Edit the landing page under Website."},{"h":"Recommended setup order","a":"recommended-setup-order","t":"Check the server requirements and deploy the files. Run the web installer and create your Super admin account. Add the cron job so scheduled tasks run. Sign in to the Super admin panel and set up the platform: general settings, website, system email, plans and payment gateways. Create a shop (or sign up as a business) and follow the setup wizard."},{"h":"Requirements at a glance","a":"requirements-at-a-glance","t":"PHP 8.3 or newer with the extensions listed in Server requirements. MySQL 8 or MariaDB 10.6+. The application targets MySQL. Node.js 20+ and npm, only if you build the front-end assets yourself. mysqldump available on the server, only for the backup feature. A cron job that runs the Laravel scheduler every minute. note The application does not need a queue worker to run, because it sends emails and SMS during the request. See Queue worker."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Installation overview Third-party costs Shop admin panel Super admin panel Next Third-party costs What is included Recommended setup order Requirements at a glance Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/admins/","ti":"Admins","c":"Admins & Audit","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Admins are the people who can sign in to the platform panel. Each admin has one role, and the role decides what they can open. Where to find it: sidebar, Admins. Needs admins.manage. Admins list with role, two-factor and last sign-in"},{"h":"The list","a":"the-list","t":"Columns: name and email, role, two-factor state (2FA on or 2FA not set up), Must change password, and Last sign-in (or Never). Your own row is marked You."},{"h":"Add an admin","a":"add-an-admin","t":"Click Add admin. Enter Name, Email and a Temporary password: at least 8 characters with letters and numbers. Choose a Role. You can only give a role that has no more access than you do. Only a Super admin can give the Super admin role. Click Save. Share the password securely. The new admin must change it, and set up two-factor, at first sign-in. See Login and two-factor. The password is never written to the audit log. You can also create an admin from the server with php artisan platform:make-admin (name the role with --role). See Login and two-factor."},{"h":"Change a role","a":"change-a-role","t":"Pick a new role in the admin's row. You cannot change your own role, and only a Super admin can change another Super admin. There must always be at least one Super admin."},{"h":"Reset two-factor","a":"reset-two-factor","t":"Reset 2FA clears the authenticator and recovery codes. The admin sets up two-factor again at their next sign-in. Use it when someone loses their phone and recovery codes. You cannot reset your own two-factor here. Use My account, which asks for a current code. Only a Super admin can reset another Super admin."},{"h":"Remove an admin","a":"remove-an-admin","t":"Remove deletes the account. It cannot be undone. You cannot remove yourself. The last admin cannot be removed, and neither can the last Super admin. Only a Super admin can remove another Super admin. The audit log keeps the removed admin's email."},{"h":"Security emails","a":"security-emails","t":"With Email admins about security events on (Settings, Security), all admins are emailed when an admin is added or removed, when two-factor is reset or locked after failed codes, and the admin concerned is emailed about a sign-in from a new address."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Roles and permissions Audit log Login and two-factor Previous System updates Next Roles and permissions The list Add an admin Change a role Reset two-factor Remove an admin Security emails Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/admins/audit-log/","ti":"Audit log","c":"Admins & Audit","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The audit log records who did what, to which business, and when. Entries cannot be edited or deleted: there are no such screens or routes. Where to find it: sidebar, Audit log. Needs audit.view. Audit log table with filters"},{"h":"Filter","a":"filter","t":"Filter What it does Admin One admin, by email. Removed admins stay in the list Event One kind of event From, To A date range Columns: When, Admin, Event, Business, Subject, Details, IP address. Hover over Details to see the full change (old and new values)."},{"h":"What is recorded","a":"what-is-recorded","t":"Area Events Sign-in Admin signed in, two-factor code failed, two-factor locked after failed codes, admin password changed Admins Admin added, admin removed, admin two-factor reset, admin role changed, role saved, role deleted Businesses Business updated, suspended, reactivated, trial extended, note added, feature rolled out Billing Plan created, plan updated, manual payment recorded, invoice voided, payment gateway settings updated Support and notices Support request status changed, announcement saved or deleted, weekly summary emailed Impersonation Opened a business as its owner, stopped viewing as the owner Settings Settings updated, email template updated, legal pages updated, website updated, language added, translations updated, default language changed, language turned on or off, language deleted Backups Backup created, backup failed, backup downloaded, automatic backup setting changed Secrets are never stored. Gateway keys, SMTP passwords and temporary passwords are masked or left out, and legal text is recorded only as \"which texts changed\". note Shop-side changes made by business users are in each business's own audit log. See Business audit log."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Admins Roles and permissions Impersonation Previous Roles and permissions Filter What is recorded Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/admins/roles-and-permissions/","ti":"Roles and permissions","c":"Admins & Audit","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"A role is a name and a set of permissions. Each admin has exactly one role. Platform roles are separate from the roles inside a business. Where to find it: sidebar, Admins, then Roles. Needs admins.manage. Platform roles list"},{"h":"Super admin","a":"super-admin","t":"Super admin is built in. It holds every permission, including future ones, and it cannot be edited or deleted. It is the only role that can open pages not listed in the tables below: a new page is closed to everyone but Super admins until it is added to config/platform_permissions.php. Only a Super admin can give the Super admin role, and only a Super admin can change, reset or remove another Super admin. At least one Super admin must always exist."},{"h":"Custom roles","a":"custom-roles","t":"Open Roles and click New role. Enter a Name (unique, up to 60 characters) and an optional Description. Tick the Permissions. Click Save. Rules: You can only give permissions you have yourself. Super admins can give any. You can only assign a role that has no more access than you. A role that still has admins cannot be deleted. Move them to another role first. Every admin can open the dashboard, their own My account page, and sign out, whatever their role. Saving and deleting are written to the Audit log."},{"h":"Permissions","a":"permissions","t":"Group Permission Label on the role form Businesses businesses.view See businesses Businesses businesses.manage Change businesses (suspend, plans, notes, tags) Businesses businesses.impersonate Open a business as its owner Money reports.view See reports and the weekly summary Money billing.view See invoices and plans Money billing.manage Record payments, void invoices, edit plans Customers support.manage Answer support requests Customers announcements.manage Send announcements Customers features.manage Roll features out System audit.view See the audit log System settings.manage Change settings, payments, languages System backups.manage Run and download backups System admins.manage Manage admins and roles"},{"h":"What each page needs","a":"what-each-page-needs","t":"Some areas need one permission to read and another to change. Reading means opening a list or a report. Opening an add or edit form counts as changing. Area Read Change Dashboard, My account, two-factor setup, language switch, sign out Any signed-in admin Any signed-in admin Search businesses.view Businesses list and data businesses.view businesses.manage (edit, status, bulk, notes, tags) Open as owner businesses.impersonate Record manual payment on a business billing.manage Reports (business, revenue, retention, summary email) reports.view reports.view Invoices list billing.view Void an invoice billing.manage Plans billing.view billing.manage Support inbox support.manage support.manage Announcements announcements.manage announcements.manage Features (rollout) features.manage features.manage Audit log audit.view Backups (downloading one is Super admin only) backups.manage backups.manage File storage, System updates Super admin only Super admin only Website, Settings, Payments, Legal pages, Languages, Email templates settings.manage settings.manage Admins and Roles admins.manage admins.manage An admin without the needed permission sees \"Your role does not allow this.\" (HTTP 403). tip A support agent role could have businesses.view, support.manage and reports.view. A finance role could have billing.view, billing.manage and reports.view."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Admins Audit log Login and two-factor Previous Admins Next Audit log Super admin Custom roles Permissions What each page needs Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/businesses/","ti":"Businesses","c":"Businesses","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"A business is one shop account (a tenant). This page covers finding a business, changing its subscription, recording a manual payment, suspending it, and keeping private notes and tags. Where to find it: sidebar, Businesses. Needs businesses.view. Changes need businesses.manage; recording a payment needs billing.manage. Businesses list with plan, status and health columns"},{"h":"The list","a":"the-list","t":"Search by name. Columns: Column Meaning Name, Plan The business and its current plan Status Trial, Active, Payment overdue, Read-only, or No plan Sales (30d), Last sale Completed sales in the last 30 days, and the date of the latest one Health Score and level (Healthy, At risk, Critical). See Dashboard Renews on Period end, or trial end while on trial Each row has Report (opens the business report) and, with businesses.manage, Manage."},{"h":"Subscription states","a":"subscription-states","t":"State What the business can do Trial Full access until the trial end date Active Full access until the period end Payment overdue Full access during the grace period (default 7 days, set under Settings, Billing) Read-only Can view and export data. Cannot add or change anything, except paying, leaving and exporting The nightly job subscriptions:advance stores these changes: an ended trial becomes expired, an unpaid active period becomes past due with a grace end date, and an ended grace becomes expired. If the owner chose not to renew, the subscription becomes cancelled at period end. The state shown to the business is always worked out from the dates."},{"h":"Manage a business","a":"manage-a-business","t":"Click Manage. The form has these fields. Field What it does Plan The plan the business is on Status Trialing, Active, Past due, Cancelled or Expired Billing interval Monthly or yearly, or empty Trial ends Required when status is Trialing Renews on End of the paid period Grace ends Required when status is Past due I won't renew Cancel at period end warning You are editing the subscription directly. Setting Trialing with no end date, or Past due with no grace date, is refused because the business would become read-only at once."},{"h":"Special limits for this business","a":"special-limits-for-this-business","t":"Under Special limits for this business, give one business its own value for each plan feature. Leave a box empty to use the plan value. Limits (branches, team members, products): type a number, or unlimited. Yes/no features: Use plan value, On or Off. To switch one feature for many businesses at once, use Feature rollout."},{"h":"Record manual payment","a":"record-manual-payment","t":"Use this for a bank transfer or cash payment. It needs billing.manage. In Record manual payment, pick the Plan (not the trial plan) and the billing interval. Enter the Amount and an optional note, such as the transfer reference. Click Record manual payment. The payment is saved as a paid invoice with the gateway \"Manual payment\", and the subscription becomes Active. Paying again for the plan that is still running adds time after the current period. A different plan starts now."},{"h":"Invoices and voiding","a":"invoices-and-voiding","t":"The page lists the last 30 invoices of the business. Void keeps an invoice on record but it can no longer be paid. Voiding a paid invoice does not shorten the subscription. Voiding needs billing.manage."},{"h":"Open as owner","a":"open-as-owner","t":"See Impersonation."},{"h":"Suspend, reactivate, extend a trial","a":"suspend-reactivate-extend-a-trial","t":"These actions are on the Business report (Reports in the sidebar), for one business or a ticked selection (up to 200 at a time). Action Effect Suspend Sets the business to suspended. Its members cannot work in it. Reactivate Sets it back to active Extend trial Adds 1 to 90 days (default 7) to the trial end. Only for businesses that are trialing Businesses already in the target state are skipped. Each change is written to the Audit log."},{"h":"Notes and tags","a":"notes-and-tags","t":"Open a business from Report. There you can add: Notes: free text up to 2000 characters, visible only to admins. Tags: short labels such as vip or churn risk. Up to 10 per business. Tags can be used to filter the business report. Adding or removing notes and tags needs businesses.manage."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Reports Plans Invoices Feature rollout Business billing and plans Previous Website Next Impersonation The list Subscription states Manage a businessSpecial limits for this business Record manual payment Invoices and voiding Open as owner Suspend, reactivate, extend a trial Notes and tags Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/businesses/feature-rollout/","ti":"Feature rollout","c":"Businesses","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Plans decide which yes/no features a business has. Feature rollout lets you override that for selected businesses: a beta, a gift, or a fix. Where to find it: sidebar, Features. Needs features.manage. Features list with forced on and forced off counts"},{"h":"The features","a":"the-features","t":"The list shows each yes/no feature, the plans that include it (Included in plans), and how many businesses are Forced on and Forced off. Limits such as branches or products are not listed here; set those per business under Businesses. Feature What it controls in a business Loyalty points Loyalty settings and customer points Batch and expiry tracking Batch and expiry screens and the expiry report Stock take Stock takes Quotations Quotations Daily owner summary The owner summary settings SMS SMS settings and templates"},{"h":"Roll a feature out","a":"roll-a-feature-out","t":"Open Features and click a feature. The table shows, for each business, By plan, Override and Effective. Tick the businesses (up to 500). Choose Force on, Force off or Follow the plan. Choice Result Force on The business has the feature, whatever its plan says Force off The business does not have it Follow the plan Removes the override, so the plan decides again The change applies at once. Each rollout is one entry in the Audit log. note The same override can be set per business on the Manage page, under \"Special limits for this business\". Rollout is the bulk way to do it."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Plans Businesses Audit log Previous Impersonation Next Plans The features Roll a feature out Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/businesses/impersonation/","ti":"Impersonation","c":"Businesses","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"\"Open as owner\" signs you in to a business as its owner so you can see what they see. It is meant for support. It is time-limited, restricted and always recorded. Where to find it: Businesses, Manage, then the Open as owner card. Needs businesses.impersonate. Open as owner card on the business page"},{"h":"Open a business as its owner","a":"open-a-business-as-its-owner","t":"Open the business with Manage. The Open as owner card shows the owner you will be signed in as, with their name and email. Enter a Reason, for example a support ticket number. It is required and is saved in the audit log. Click Open as owner and confirm. The note under the box reminds you how long the session lasts and what is blocked. You are sent to the shop and signed in as the oldest active member who holds the Owner role. While you are in, a banner reads \"Viewing as (name) ((business))\" with an Exit button. When the business is suspended or has no active owner, the card shows \"This business has no active owner to open as.\" and the button is disabled. The card is shown only to admins with businesses.impersonate."},{"h":"Limits","a":"limits","t":"The session lasts at most 60 minutes (impersonation_minutes in config/platform.php). Then you are signed out of the owner view. Password and email changes are blocked. Sign-out is blocked. Use Exit instead, so the end is recorded. Inviting team members, resending or cancelling invitations, and switching business are blocked. Exporting business data is blocked. Everything else works as the owner would. Treat it as editing the real business. The hand-off uses a one-time link valid for 60 seconds, so it works when the panel and the shop are on different hosts."},{"h":"Audit","a":"audit","t":"Two entries are written to the Audit log: \"Opened a business as its owner\" (with your reason and the owner's email) and \"Stopped viewing as the owner\" (how long and why it ended, for example expired). warning Everything you do is done as the real owner. Use impersonation only when needed, and write a reason."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Businesses Audit log Roles and permissions Previous Businesses Next Feature rollout Open a business as its owner Limits Audit Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/care/announcements/","ti":"Announcements","c":"Customer Care","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"An announcement is a notice shown to businesses at the top of their app. Use it for maintenance, new features or billing news. Where to find it: sidebar, Announcements. Needs announcements.manage. Announcements list with live status"},{"h":"Create an announcement","a":"create-an-announcement","t":"Click New announcement. Fill in the fields below. Click Save. Field What it does Title Up to 120 characters. Required Message Optional text, up to 1000 characters Style Info, Warning or Urgent Audience Every business, or Only businesses on one plan From, To Optional dates. Empty means no start or no end. The end date includes that whole day Show to businesses The on/off switch The list shows each announcement's title, audience, window and a Live or Not live badge. An announcement is live when it is switched on and today is inside its window."},{"h":"Edit and delete","a":"edit-and-delete","t":"Click Edit to change an announcement, or Delete to remove it. To hide one without losing it, switch Show to businesses off. Saving and deleting are written to the Audit log. tip A plan audience reaches only businesses currently on that plan. To reach everyone, choose Every business."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Plans Support inbox Audit log Previous Support inbox Next General settings Create an announcement Edit and delete Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/care/support-inbox/","ti":"Support inbox","c":"Customer Care","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Businesses send questions and problems from their own panel. All requests from all businesses arrive in one inbox. Where to find it: sidebar, Support. Needs support.manage. Support inbox with status tabs"},{"h":"Find a request","a":"find-a-request","t":"Tabs show how many requests are in each state: Tab Meaning Needs reply The business wrote last Answered You replied last Closed Finished All Everything Search matches the subject, the business name, the text of any message, the opener's email, or the request number (for example #12). Columns: number, subject and opener, business, type, status, time of the last message. Request types a business can choose: Question, Billing, Something is broken, Feature request."},{"h":"Reply","a":"reply","t":"Click a subject to open the conversation. Type in the reply box. Enter sends; Shift+Enter starts a new line. Send. The status becomes Answered and the person who opened the request gets an email with your message and a link to it. Replies are 2 to 5000 characters."},{"h":"Internal notes","a":"internal-notes","t":"Tick Internal note before sending to leave a note only admins can see. The business is not emailed and the status does not change."},{"h":"Close and reopen","a":"close-and-reopen","t":"Close request marks it Closed. The opener is emailed. A closed request cannot take new messages. Reopen brings it back. The status returns to Answered if your reply was the last visible message, otherwise Needs reply. The opener is emailed. Status changes are written to the Audit log."},{"h":"Email notices","a":"email-notices","t":"When a business opens or answers a request, the Support email (Settings, Platform) is emailed. If none is set, every platform admin is emailed. Emails need a working system email. See General settings. A mail problem never stops a reply from being saved. Open requests also appear on the Dashboard under Needs attention."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Business support Dashboard Businesses Previous Reports Next Announcements Find a request ReplyInternal notes Close and reopen Email notices Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/dashboard/","ti":"Dashboard","c":"","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The dashboard shows how the platform is doing across every business: growth, recurring revenue, problem payments and businesses that need attention. Where to find it: sidebar, Dashboard. Every signed-in admin can open it. Platform dashboard with KPI cards and charts"},{"h":"Date range","a":"date-range","t":"The Date range control sets the window for the KPI tiles, the sign-up chart and Top businesses by sales: 7 days, 30 days (default), 90 days or 1 year. Each KPI is compared with the period just before it (vs previous period). KPI What it counts New businesses Businesses created in the range Active businesses Businesses with at least one completed sale in the range Sales Completed sales across all businesses Sales value Total of those sales"},{"h":"Summary cards","a":"summary-cards","t":"Card What it shows Businesses Total, with how many are active and suspended Subscriptions Trialing, Active, Past due and Expired counts Monthly recurring revenue Active paid plans; a yearly plan counts as a twelfth. Each currency is shown on its own line Revenue this month Live payments and manual payments only. Test-mode payments are excluded Failed and pending payments Counts, plus a list of recent ones and See all invoices New businesses (30 days) Sign-ups, with how many trials end within 7 days note Money is never converted between currencies. If plans use different currencies you see one line per currency. Subscription counts are worked out from dates, not from the stored status. They match what each business sees even if the nightly job has not run yet. See Businesses for the states. Each card has an icon in a fixed colour that does not change with the accent colour. Red (failed payments) and orange (open support requests) appear only when there is something to deal with; at zero the icon is grey. Cards with history show a small trend line. The cards also include Support requests waiting, the number of open requests."},{"h":"Needs attention","a":"needs-attention","t":"Needs attention lists what to act on, most urgent first: Alert When it appears Suspended The business is suspended Read-only Its subscription has ended In grace period A renewal failed and the grace period is running Trial ending The trial ends within 3 days Cancels at period end The owner chose not to renew Near plan limit Usage is at 90% or more of a plan limit Payment failed A failed invoice in the last 14 days Payment mismatch A payment did not match its invoice (see Invoices) Support requests waiting Open tickets in the Support inbox"},{"h":"Business health","a":"business-health","t":"Each business gets a score from 0 to 100, based on recent sales (the most weight), subscription state, and how set up it is. A suspended business scores 0. Level Score Healthy 70 or more At risk 40 to 69 Critical below 40 The dashboard shows how many businesses fall in each level. The score is also shown for each row in Businesses."},{"h":"Other panels","a":"other-panels","t":"Platform revenue and Growth: revenue and new businesses for the last 12 months. Subscriptions by plan and Sales across all businesses. Top businesses by sales for the chosen range. Quiet businesses: active businesses at least 7 days old with no sale in the last 14 days. Trials ending within 7 days. Recent sign-ups. Recent admin activity: the latest entries of the Audit log."},{"h":"System health","a":"system-health","t":"The scheduler heartbeat and queue counts are not on the dashboard. They are on Settings, System. See General settings."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Reports Businesses Support inbox Previous Login and two-factor Next Website Date range Summary cards Needs attention Business health Other panels System health Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/login-and-two-factor/","ti":"Login and two-factor","c":"","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Platform admins sign in with an email and password, then a six-digit code from an authenticator app. Where to find it: /admin/login (or your ADMIN_DOMAIN). Account page: My account. No permission needed. Platform admin sign in page"},{"h":"Create the first admin","a":"create-the-first-admin","t":"The web installer creates the first admin. To add one from the server: php artisan platform:make-admin you@example.com --name=\"Your Name\" Once an admin exists, name the role too, for example --role=\"Super admin\". The command asks for a password (at least 12 characters) and confirms it. The new admin must change that password and set up two-factor at first sign-in. Once you are in, add more people under Admins."},{"h":"Sign in","a":"sign-in","t":"Open the login page and enter your email and password. If two-factor is set up, enter the six-digit code from your app. You can switch to Use a recovery code instead. You land on the dashboard, or on the page you were trying to open. Limits that protect the login: After 5 wrong passwords for the same email and address, sign-in is blocked for a short time. After 5 wrong authenticator or recovery codes for one admin, that admin is locked for 15 minutes. One address is also limited to 5 wrong codes a minute. You have 5 minutes between the password step and the code step. You are signed out after 30 minutes without activity. Change this under Settings, Security (Admin idle timeout (minutes), 5 to 240). Changing your password signs out your other sessions. Signing out of the panel does not sign you out of a shop in the same browser. You can also sign in from the shop sign-in page (/login). When the email belongs to a platform admin, you are taken on to the panel and asked for your code there. If you set ADMIN_DOMAIN, you are sent to the admin sign-in page on that domain instead. If you send a form after your session has ended, nothing is saved. You are taken to the login page with \"Your session expired and nothing was saved. Please sign in again.\" After signing in you return to the page you were on. The picture behind the sign-in and sign-up pages is the Login background under General settings. With none uploaded, the built-in picture is used. On a demo site two-factor is not forced on the shared sample admin. Admins listed in DEMO_BYPASS_EMAILS keep the normal rule. A demo site also shows demo login buttons on /login: one click on Platform admin signs in as admin@example.com (password Demo@2026). Never turn these on for a live site."},{"h":"Set up two-factor","a":"set-up-two-factor","t":"Two-factor is required by default (Settings, Security, Require two-factor authentication for admins). Until you set it up, every page sends you to the setup screen. Install Google Authenticator, Microsoft Authenticator or Authy on your phone. In the app, scan the QR code. If you cannot scan, enter the key by hand: account name, key, type \"time based\". Enter the six-digit code and click Turn on two-factor authentication. Save the 8 recovery codes shown on the next screen. They are shown once, and each works once. tip If a code is rejected, check that your phone's date and time are set to automatic. When the setting is turned off, admins who have not set up an authenticator sign in with email and password only. Admins who already have one are still asked for a code. Turning it off lowers the security of the panel."},{"h":"My account","a":"my-account","t":"Action What it does Change password Needs your current password. At least 8 characters. Get new recovery codes Asks for a current authenticator code, then replaces all 8 codes. The old ones stop working. If your password is temporary (a new admin, or one made with platform:make-admin), you must change it before anything else."},{"h":"Lost phone or codes","a":"lost-phone-or-codes","t":"Ask a Super admin to open Admins and use Reset 2FA on your row. You set up an authenticator again at your next sign-in. You cannot reset your own two-factor there."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Admins Roles and permissions General settings First login Previous Platform overview Next Dashboard Create the first admin Sign in Set up two-factor My account Lost phone or codes Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/money/invoices/","ti":"Invoices","c":"Plans & Money","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Each time a business pays for a plan, or you record a manual payment, an invoice is created. This page lists them all. Where to find it: sidebar, Invoices. Needs billing.view. Voiding needs billing.manage. Invoices list with status tabs and filters"},{"h":"Filter the list","a":"filter-the-list","t":"Filter Options Status tabs All statuses, Pending, Paid, Failed, Void Search Business name Gateway Stripe, Razorpay, Flutterwave, PayPal, Manual payment Mode Live or Test From, To Created date range Columns: Invoice number, Business, Plan, Amount, Status, Gateway, Paid on."},{"h":"Invoice statuses","a":"invoice-statuses","t":"Status Meaning Pending Checkout started, not paid yet Paid Payment confirmed and the subscription extended Failed Checkout could not start, or was abandoned Void Cancelled by an admin. Kept on record, cannot be paid Pending invoices older than one day are marked Failed by the nightly job. If the money arrives later, it is still applied. Invoice numbers use a prefix, INV- by default. Change it under Settings, Billing. Existing invoices keep their numbers."},{"h":"Mismatch","a":"mismatch","t":"An invoice shows a red Mismatch badge when the gateway reported a different amount or currency from the invoice. The invoice stays Pending and nothing is applied. The owner is told to contact support, and the reason is saved on the invoice. Check the payment in the gateway, then either record a manual payment or void the invoice. Mismatches also appear on the dashboard under Needs attention."},{"h":"Void an invoice","a":"void-an-invoice","t":"Click Void on a row, or on the business page. Confirm. Voiding a paid invoice does not shorten the subscription: the paid period stays. A void invoice that is later paid at the gateway is not applied; it is logged as an error."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Businesses Payment gateways Reports General settings Previous Payment gateways Next Reports Filter the list Invoice statuses Mismatch Void an invoice Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/money/payment-gateways/","ti":"Payment gateways","c":"Plans & Money","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"These are your gateways: the ones businesses use to pay you for a plan. Each business also sets up its own gateways to take payments from its customers. Those are separate. See Payment methods. Where to find it: sidebar, Settings, Payments. Needs settings.manage. Payment gateways page with Stripe selected"},{"h":"Set up a gateway","a":"set-up-a-gateway","t":"Open Payments and pick a gateway in the Gateways list: Stripe, Razorpay, Flutterwave or PayPal. Choose the Mode: Live or Test. The selected mode is the one used for real payments. Fill in the credentials for that mode. Copy the Webhook URL and add it in the gateway's dashboard (see below). Turn on Enabled and click Save. Live and Test credentials are stored separately, so you can switch modes without retyping keys. The status line under the gateway name shows Not enabled, Configured or Credentials missing. A gateway is only offered to businesses when it is enabled and has every required credential for its mode."},{"h":"Credentials","a":"credentials","t":"Secret fields are stored encrypted and never shown again. Leave a secret box blank to keep the saved value, click Replace to change it, or tick Clear the saved value. Gateway Fields Required Stripe Publishable Key, Secret Key, Webhook Secret Secret Key Razorpay Key Id, Key Secret, Webhook Secret Key Id, Key Secret Flutterwave Public Key, Secret Key, Webhook Secret Public Key, Secret Key PayPal Client Id, Client Secret, Webhook Id Client Id, Client Secret For PayPal, use the Sandbox app's credentials in Test mode and the Live app's in Live mode."},{"h":"Webhooks","a":"webhooks","t":"Webhooks let a payment complete even if the customer closes the browser tab. Each gateway has its own URL: Gateway Webhook URL Event to send Secret to copy back Stripe https://your-domain/webhooks/platform/stripe checkout.session.completed (also checkout.session.async_payment_succeeded) Signing secret into Webhook Secret Razorpay https://your-domain/webhooks/platform/razorpay payment_link.paid The secret you typed into Webhook Secret Flutterwave https://your-domain/webhooks/platform/flutterwave charge.completed The \"Secret hash\" into Webhook Secret PayPal https://your-domain/webhooks/platform/paypal CHECKOUT.ORDER.APPROVED and PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED The Webhook ID into Webhook Id The page shows the exact URL with a Copy button. The gateway must be able to reach it from the internet, so it cannot be a localhost address. When a webhook arrives its signature is verified, then the payment is re-checked with the gateway before anything is applied. Without a webhook, a payment only completes when the customer returns to the app after paying."},{"h":"Currencies","a":"currencies","t":"Each plan has one currency, and a gateway must accept it. The page warns \"This gateway cannot take these plan currencies\" when an active plan uses a currency a gateway rejects. Stripe and Razorpay accept any three-letter currency code (the gateway account itself must support it). Flutterwave: NGN, GHS, KES, UGX, TZS, ZAR, RWF, XAF, XOF, USD, EUR, GBP. PayPal: AUD, BRL, CAD, CNY, CZK, DKK, EUR, GBP, HKD, HUF, ILS, JPY, MXN, MYR, NOK, NZD, PHP, PLN, SEK, SGD, THB, TWD, USD, CHF."},{"h":"Test mode","a":"test-mode","t":"Every invoice records the mode it was created in. Test-mode invoices show a Test badge, and are never counted in revenue or monthly recurring revenue. warning If you switch the mode while a payment is waiting, that invoice is not re-checked. The mode on the invoice must match the gateway's current mode."},{"h":"Audit","a":"audit","t":"Saving writes \"Payment gateway settings updated\" to the Audit log. It records which gateways are on, their mode, and the names of the settings that changed. Values are never logged."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Plans Invoices General settings Business billing and plans Previous Plans Next Invoices Set up a gateway Credentials Webhooks Currencies Test mode Audit Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/money/plans/","ti":"Plans","c":"Plans & Money","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"A plan is what a business subscribes to: a price, a trial length, and a set of limits and features. You can edit the default plans or add your own. Where to find it: sidebar, Plans. Viewing needs billing.view; creating and editing need billing.manage. Plans list with prices and status"},{"h":"Default plans","a":"default-plans","t":"A fresh install creates four plans in USD. They are only created when no plan exists, so your edits are never overwritten. Treat these values as a starting point. Plan Monthly Yearly Branches Team members Products Trial (14 trial days, not public) 0 0 3 5 Unlimited Starter 19.00 190.00 1 2 500 Growth 49.00 490.00 3 10 5000 Pro 99.00 990.00 Unlimited Unlimited Unlimited Trial includes every yes/no feature. Starter includes only Coupons and Gift cards. Growth includes all except SMS. Pro includes all."},{"h":"Create or edit a plan","a":"create-or-edit-a-plan","t":"Click New plan, or Edit on a row. Field What it does Name Shown to businesses Code Short id: lowercase letters, numbers, - and _. Set once; cannot be changed later Currency The plan's currency. Payments are never converted Monthly price, Yearly price Prices in that currency, up to 2 decimals Trial days Length of the trial for the trial plan Sort order Lower numbers are shown first Status Active or Archived Show on the Billing page Whether businesses can pick this plan themselves Under What this plan includes: Limits (branches, team members, products): a number, or empty for Unlimited. Yes/no features: tick to include. These are Loyalty points, Batch and expiry tracking, Stock take, Quotations, Daily owner summary, SMS, Coupons and Gift cards. Changes take effect at once for every business on the plan. Saving writes \"Plan created\" or \"Plan updated\" to the Audit log."},{"h":"The trial plan","a":"the-trial-plan","t":"One plan is the trial plan. New sign-ups start on it. It cannot be archived. It needs at least 1 trial day. With 0 days, new sign-ups would be read-only at once. It cannot be bought. Businesses choose a paid plan before or after the trial ends."},{"h":"What a business can buy","a":"what-a-business-can-buy","t":"A business can only start a checkout for a plan that is Active, shown on the Billing page, not the trial plan, and has a price above zero. The gateway must be enabled and accept the plan currency. See Payment gateways. When a business moves to a different plan, it must be within that plan's limits. Otherwise checkout is refused with a message naming the limits it exceeds. Renewing the same plan is never refused. Archiving a plan hides it from new purchases. It does not move businesses already on it."},{"h":"Overrides","a":"overrides","t":"A business can have its own limits or feature values, set on its Manage page or through Feature rollout. An override wins over the plan."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Businesses Payment gateways Invoices Business billing and plans Previous Feature rollout Next Payment gateways Default plans Create or edit a plan The trial plan What a business can buy Overrides Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/money/reports/","ti":"Reports","c":"Plans & Money","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Three reports cover how businesses use the platform and how much recurring revenue it makes. Where to find it: sidebar, Reports, then the tabs Business report, Revenue & subscriptions and Retention. Needs reports.view. Business report table with filters"},{"h":"Business report","a":"business-report","t":"Sales, customers and billing for every business, side by side. Filters: Date range (7 days, 30 days, 90 days, 1 year) or a custom from and to (up to five years), Plan, Status (Active or Suspended), Tag, and a name search. Click Apply, or Reset. Summary tiles show the number of businesses (and how many have sales), sales, sales value, customers and products. Column Meaning Name, Plan, Joined The business, its plan and sign-up date Sales, Sales value Completed sales in the window Customers, Products, Branches, Users All-time counts Last sale Date of the latest completed sale Paid to platform Live payments the business made to you, per currency Click a column heading to sort. Export CSV downloads the filtered rows. With businesses.manage you can tick businesses and apply Suspend, Reactivate or Extend trial (with a number of days). See Businesses."},{"h":"One business","a":"one-business","t":"Click a business name or Report in the Businesses list. The page shows: Sales by month for the last 12 months, and Top products in this period. Plan usage against each limit (users, branches, products), and the Health score. Team: members with their roles. Subscription payments: the last 10 invoices. Admin actions on this business. Notes and Tags."},{"h":"Revenue & subscriptions","a":"revenue--subscriptions","t":"Recurring revenue, churn, conversion and renewals. Figure How it is worked out Monthly recurring revenue Active paid plans; yearly plans counted as a twelfth ARR Monthly recurring revenue times 12 Revenue per paying business Monthly recurring revenue divided by paying businesses Paying businesses Active subscriptions on a paid plan Churn (30 days) Paid subscriptions that ended in the last 30 days, over the paying base at the start of that period Trial to paid Businesses that ever paid with a live payment, out of all that signed up Other sections: subscriptions by state (Trial, Active, Past due, Expired, Cancelling), Recurring revenue by plan, Renewals in the next 14 days, and Revenue by gateway. Money is shown per currency and never converted. Test-mode payments are excluded. Export CSV downloads the last 12 months: month, platform revenue, new businesses, sales and sales value."},{"h":"Email summary now","a":"email-summary-now","t":"Email summary now sends the weekly summary to every platform admin immediately. It covers the last 7 days against the 7 before: sign-ups, sales, revenue, active businesses, recurring revenue, top businesses and alerts. Tick Email a weekly summary to platform admins under Settings, Platform to also send it every Monday at 08:00. That needs the scheduler cron job and a working system email. See General settings."},{"h":"Retention","a":"retention","t":"Of the businesses that joined in each month, how many were still selling later. Each cell is the share of that month's sign-ups with at least one completed sale in the month shown. Month 0 is the sign-up month. A blank cell means that month has not happened yet."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Dashboard Businesses Invoices Previous Invoices Next Support inbox Business reportOne business Revenue & subscriptionsEmail summary now Retention Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/overview/","ti":"Platform overview","c":"","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The platform panel is where you, the owner of the installation, run the whole SaaS: businesses, plans, payments, support and system settings. Businesses never see it. Where to find it: /admin, or the host set in ADMIN_DOMAIN in your .env file. Sign in at /admin/login. Without ADMIN_DOMAIN this opens the shared sign-in page at /login, which signs in platform admins too. Platform panel with the sidebar open"},{"h":"Panel versus shop","a":"panel-versus-shop","t":"Platform panel Shop (business) panel Who uses it Platform admins Business owners and staff Sign in /admin/login /login Accounts Platform admins and platform roles Users, with per-business roles Sees Every business Only its own business If you set ADMIN_DOMAIN, the panel is served only on that host and the public site pages return a 404 there. ADMIN_DOMAIN is an .env value on purpose, so a wrong value in a screen can never lock you out. See Environment configuration."},{"h":"Sidebar","a":"sidebar","t":"Each item is shown only if its route exists. What you can open also depends on your role. Menu item What it is for Permission Dashboard Headline numbers and alerts Every admin Businesses Every business and its subscription businesses.view Reports Business report, revenue, retention reports.view Features Turn a feature on or off per business features.manage Support Support requests from businesses support.manage Announcements Banners shown to businesses announcements.manage Invoices Subscription invoices billing.view Plans Plans and what they include billing.view Website Text, pictures and design of the public home page settings.manage Settings Platform settings, payments, legal, languages, backups settings.manage Admins Admins and roles admins.manage Audit log Everything admins did audit.view A search box finds a business by name, a person by name or email, or an invoice by number. It needs businesses.view and at least two characters. Every admin also has My account (change password, two-factor, recovery codes). See Login and two-factor."},{"h":"How the SaaS fits together","a":"how-the-saas-fits-together","t":"A new business signs up and starts on the trial plan. Its subscription moves through trial, active, payment overdue (grace) and read-only. Plans decide limits (branches, team members, products) and yes/no features. You can override both per business. Businesses pay for plans through the gateways you configure under Payment gateways. You can also record a manual payment. Everything you change in the panel is written to the Audit log. note Several features depend on the scheduler cron job (subscription changes, reminders, backups, the weekly summary). Check it under Settings, System. See Cron jobs."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Login and two-factor Dashboard Website Businesses Roles and permissions Next Login and two-factor Panel versus shop Sidebar How the SaaS fits together Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/settings/backups/","ti":"Backups","c":"Settings","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"A backup is a compressed dump of the whole database, so it contains every business. Only platform admins can reach it. Where to find it: sidebar, Settings, Backups. Needs backups.manage. Backups page with the file list"},{"h":"Automatic backup","a":"automatic-backup","t":"Turn on Automatic nightly backup to back up every night at 02:00. The newest 14 are kept by default. Change that with Backups to keep (3 to 90) and click Save changes. Automatic backups are on by default and need the scheduler cron job. See Cron jobs. If a nightly backup fails, every platform admin is emailed."},{"h":"Back up now","a":"back-up-now","t":"Click Back up now to create a backup straight away. The page reports the file name. Only one backup runs at a time; a second attempt says another backup is already running."},{"h":"Status banners","a":"status-banners","t":"Banner Meaning The last automatic backup failed Check the message and the server log No backup has been made in the last 36 hours Check that the scheduler is running There is no backup yet The first one is made tonight, or use Back up now Automatic backups are off Back up now and Download still work"},{"h":"Download and restore","a":"download-and-restore","t":"The list shows each file, its size and date. Click Download to save one. Files are named backup-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.sql.gz, and are stored privately on the server outside the web root. To restore, run this on the server. It replaces the current data: gunzip < backup-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.sql.gz | mysql -u USER -p DATABASE"},{"h":"Requirements","a":"requirements","t":"Backups work with MySQL, MariaDB and SQLite. For MySQL the mysqldump program must be available. If it is not on the server path, set BACKUP_MYSQLDUMP_PATH in .env. Use BACKUP_DB_CONNECTION to back up a different connection. warning Only a Super admin can download a backup. A backup holds every business's data and password hashes. Download it over a secure connection and store it safely. Running, failing, downloading and changing the automatic setting are written to the Audit log."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Cron jobs General settings Business backups Previous Languages Next File storage Automatic backup Back up now Status banners Download and restore Requirements Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/settings/file-storage/","ti":"File storage","c":"Settings","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Choose where uploaded pictures and receipts are kept: on this server or in an S3 bucket. Businesses never see this setting. Where to find it: sidebar, Settings, File storage. Super admins only. File storage page with the S3 bucket fields"},{"h":"Use an S3 bucket","a":"use-an-s3-bucket","t":"Fill in the bucket details and click Save. Click Test connection. It writes, reads and deletes a small test file. Switch to Amazon S3 (or S3-compatible) and confirm. Field What it does Access key ID, Secret access key The bucket's keys. Leave blank to keep the saved ones Bucket The bucket's name Region For example us-east-1. Use auto for Cloudflare R2 Endpoint Only for S3-compatible services such as MinIO, DigitalOcean Spaces or Cloudflare R2 Use path-style URLs Turn on for MinIO and similar services"},{"h":"What happens when you switch","a":"what-happens-when-you-switch","t":"New uploads go to the new place at once. Existing files are moved in the background and stay visible meanwhile. The page shows how many have moved. Files that could not be moved are counted. Click Retry to queue them again. You can switch back to the local disk in the same way. One switch must finish before the next starts. note Moving files needs the scheduler. If the page says it does not seem to be running, see Cron jobs."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Backups General settings Previous Backups Next System updates Use an S3 bucket What happens when you switch Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/settings/general-settings/","ti":"General settings","c":"Settings","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Platform-wide settings live in one place, with a menu on the left. Settings are saved in the database and take effect at once. Where to find it: sidebar, Settings. Needs settings.manage. Platform settings page with the settings menu The settings menu groups pages like this: Group Pages General Platform, Appearance, New business defaults Sign-up and billing Sign-up, Billing, Payments Messaging System email, Email templates Security and system Security, Legal pages, Languages, Backups, File storage, System updates, System Changes that alter a value are written to the Audit log as \"Settings updated\" (secrets are masked)."},{"h":"Platform","a":"platform","t":"Field What it does Platform name Shown in the panel, emails and the authenticator app. Empty uses the name from the server configuration Support email Receives new support requests. Empty means every admin is emailed Company name, Company address Your company details Email a weekly summary to platform admins Sent Mondays at 08:00. Needs the scheduler cron job Logo (light theme), Logo (dark theme) Wide logo with your name, for the sidebar, sign-in pages and website header. The dark one falls back to the light one. PNG, JPG or WebP, up to 1 MB. Empty space around the logo is trimmed and a very large logo is scaled down when you upload it, so there is no need to crop or resize it first Short logo (light theme), Short logo (dark theme) Square icon for the collapsed sidebar. PNG, JPG or WebP, up to 1 MB. Trimmed and scaled the same way Login background Shown behind the sign-in and sign-up pages. PNG, JPG or WebP, up to 4 MB. Large pictures are saved as a screen-sized WebP (up to 1920 px wide) so the page loads fast. With none uploaded, the built-in picture public/images/auth-bg.jpg is used (a .jpeg, .png or .webp file with the same name also works) Favicon PNG, ICO, JPG or WebP, up to 512 KB"},{"h":"Appearance","a":"appearance","t":"The look of the admin panel. Field What it does Accent colour Fixes the panel colour for everyone. When none is set, each admin picks a palette from the header Text on the accent colour Auto, White or Dark. Auto picks the most readable Default theme Light, Dark or System, until an admin chooses Font The font used across the panel"},{"h":"New business defaults","a":"new-business-defaults","t":"Starting values for a business created at sign-up. Field What it does Default currency Currency of new businesses Default timezone Used when the visitor's browser does not report one"},{"h":"Sign-up","a":"sign-up","t":"Field What it does Allow new sign-ups When off, nobody can create a new business. Existing businesses are not affected Require email verification at signup New businesses must verify their email before they can invite team members or take online payments Blocked email domains One per line, for example mailinator.com. Subdomains are blocked too Invitations per business per hour / per day Limits how fast a business can send team invitations (1 to 1000 per hour, 1 to 5000 per day) Invitations per person per hour / per day The same limits for each person who invites"},{"h":"Billing","a":"billing","t":"Field What it does Grace period (days) How long a business keeps full access after a failed renewal. 0 to 60. Default 7 Trial ending reminder (days before) When the trial reminder email is sent. 1 to 14. Default 4 Renewal reminders (days before) Comma separated whole numbers from 1 to 60, for example 7, 3, 1. Up to 5 values. Only the nearest threshold is sent Invoice number prefix Letters, numbers and dashes, up to 10 characters. Default INV-. Existing invoices keep their numbers Reminder emails are sent by the daily job subscriptions:remind at 09:00. They go to the business owner."},{"h":"System email","a":"system-email","t":"The mail server used for verification, password reset, invitations and billing emails. Field What it does Mail server, Port, Username, Password SMTP details. The default port is 587. Leave the server empty to use the .env mail configuration. Leave the password blank to keep the saved one Encryption TLS (default), SSL or None From address, From name The sender shown on emails Use Send test email to send one message to your own address with the saved settings. A server address that is private or local is refused for the test."},{"h":"Security","a":"security","t":"Field What it does Email admins about security events Sign-in from a new address, 2FA lockouts, admins added or removed, 2FA resets Require two-factor authentication for admins See Login and two-factor Admin idle timeout (minutes) 5 to 240. Default 30 Shop session lifetime (minutes) How long a business user stays signed in. 15 to 1440 Minimum password length (shop) 8 to 64 Failed sign-ins before lockout (shop) 3 to 20 The shop fields apply to businesses. The admin sign-in throttle and admin password rule are fixed in code."},{"h":"System","a":"system","t":"Field What it does Show a maintenance notice on every shop page Turn on to show a notice to businesses Notice text Up to 300 characters. Empty shows \"The system is under maintenance. Some features may be unavailable.\" The System health card on this page shows: Row Meaning Scheduler Running, Not running (check the cron job), or No heartbeat yet. A heartbeat is written every minute; it is stale after 5 minutes without one Queued jobs, Failed jobs Counts from the queue tables PHP version, Framework version What the server is running If the scheduler is not running, subscriptions do not advance, reminders and backups do not run, and the weekly summary is not sent. See Cron jobs and Queue worker."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Payment gateways Email templates Backups Login and two-factor Previous Announcements Next Legal pages Platform Appearance New business defaults Sign-up Billing System email Security System Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/settings/languages/","ti":"Languages","c":"Settings","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The interface of both the platform panel and the shop panels is translated through language files. You manage them here once, and every business shares them. Where to find it: sidebar, Settings, Languages. Needs settings.manage. Languages list with translation progress"},{"h":"The list","a":"the-list","t":"Each row shows the language, Default badge, how many texts are translated (for example \"120 of 800 translated\"), whether it is right-to-left, and its status. Actions: Edit translations, Make default, Disable or Enable, Delete. Users switch language from the language menu in the top bar. Only enabled languages are offered."},{"h":"Add a language","a":"add-a-language","t":"Click Add language (or New language). Fill in the fields, then click Create language. Field What it does Name The name in English, for example Arabic Native name How speakers write it Code Short code such as ar, hi or pt-BR. Cannot be changed later Right-to-left Turn on for Arabic, Hebrew or Urdu. The whole layout flips A new language starts as a copy of the English file, so nothing is blank. You land on its translation editor."},{"h":"Translate","a":"translate","t":"Click Edit translations. Search by key or text, and use the filter to show only texts that need translation. Edit the Translation column. Leave a box as it is to keep the English wording. Click Save translations. A blank box falls back to English. Only keys that exist in English can be edited. Unsaved changes trigger a warning if you leave the page."},{"h":"Default, enable, disable, delete","a":"default-enable-disable-delete","t":"Make default: only an enabled language can become the default. Disable: the default language cannot be disabled. Choose another default first. Delete: English and the default language cannot be deleted. Deleting removes the language file. Every change is written to the Audit log. note Texts you add for a new feature in code appear in English until you translate them. Languages also drive the tabs in Legal pages and Email templates."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Website Legal pages Email templates Business languages Previous Email templates Next Backups The list Add a language Translate Default, enable, disable, delete Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/settings/legal-pages/","ti":"Legal pages","c":"Settings","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The Terms of Service and Privacy Policy are shown on the public site and linked from the sign-up form. You write them here, one text per language. Where to find it: sidebar, Settings, Legal pages. Needs settings.manage. Legal pages editor with a tab for each language"},{"h":"Edit the texts","a":"edit-the-texts","t":"Open Legal pages. There is one card for Terms of Service and one for Privacy Policy. Each card shows its public link, /terms and /privacy. Pick the language tab. Tabs are the active languages from Languages. Type the text. Use plain text and leave a blank line between paragraphs. Up to 50000 characters. Click Save. Details: A blank box falls back to English, then to the built-in placeholder text. A blank box clears the saved text for that language. The text is stored as typed and escaped when shown, so HTML does not work. A language the form did not send keeps its text. warning The built-in placeholder text is generic. Replace it with text approved for your business before you open sign-ups. The audit log records that the legal pages changed and which languages, never the text itself."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Website Languages General settings Audit log Previous General settings Next Email templates Edit the texts Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/settings/mail-templates/","ti":"Email templates","c":"Settings","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The platform sends a few emails of its own. You can change their subject and message for each language. Where to find it: sidebar, Settings, Email templates. Needs settings.manage. Email templates page with placeholders"},{"h":"Templates","a":"templates","t":"Template Sent when Placeholders Email verification A new owner must verify their email {name}, {app} Password reset Someone asks to reset a password {name}, {app} Team invitation A business invites a team member {inviter}, {business}, {app}, {role}"},{"h":"Edit a template","a":"edit-a-template","t":"Open Email templates. Each template has a card with a tab per active language. Pick a language. Edit the Subject (up to 200 characters) and Message (up to 5000). Click Save. Each language is saved on its own. Rules: Write plain text. Leave a blank line between paragraphs. HTML is removed. Put a placeholder in curly braces where the value should appear. Leave a box empty to use the built-in text. note Emails are sent through the mail server set under System email. See General settings. Other platform emails are not editable here."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"General settings Languages Previous Legal pages Next Languages Templates Edit a template Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/settings/system-updates/","ti":"System updates","c":"Settings","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Install a new version of the software from an update package, without a terminal. Where to find it: sidebar, Settings, System updates. Super admins only. System updates page with the installed version and update history"},{"h":"Install an update","a":"install-an-update","t":"Check the Installed version shown on the page. Choose the Update package (.zip). Enter your password and click Install update, then confirm. What happens: A database backup is made first. If it fails, nothing is changed. The site goes into maintenance mode while files are replaced and database changes run. If anything goes wrong, the replaced files are put back and the version stays as it was. If the failure happens during the database changes, the message says so and names the database backup made in step 1. Some database changes may already be in place, so download that backup from Backups, import it with your database tool, then try again. Rules for the package: It must hold a VERSION file with a version newer than the installed one. Up to 300 MB unpacked. The server's upload limits must allow the file; see PHP ini settings. Your .env file and the storage folder are never touched. Update history lists each update with its date, version and result."},{"h":"If an update stops halfway","a":"if-an-update-stops-halfway","t":"If the server stops the update partway through, for example on a time limit or a memory error, the site can stay in maintenance mode. Run php artisan up on the server to open the site again. Check storage/logs for the error. The files that were replaced are copied to storage/app/updates/<date>-<old>-to-<new>/files. Put them back if the site does not work. If database changes were made, download the backup from Backups and import it with your database tool, such as phpMyAdmin or the mysql command. Install the package again once the cause is fixed."},{"h":"Make an update package (developers)","a":"make-an-update-package-developers","t":"Build the package on your development copy with: php artisan update:package 1.1.0 --since=v1.0.0 --since is the git tag or commit of the version your customers run. Every file changed since then goes in. When CSS or JavaScript changed, the compiled public/build folder is added by itself. Run npm run build first. When composer.json or composer.lock changed, the whole vendor folder is added by itself. Run composer install --no-dev --optimize-autoloader first so no development tools ship. Add --with-build or --with-vendor to include them anyway. Deleted files are listed as a warning. An update only adds and replaces files, so they stay on the server. The package is saved to storage/app/packages/update-<version>.zip."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Updating by hand Backups Previous File storage Next Admins Install an update If an update stops halfway Make an update package (developers) Related"}]},{"u":"docs/platform/website/","ti":"Website","c":"","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The Website page controls everything visitors see on your public home page. You can change text, pictures, colours and the order of the sections without touching any code. Where to find it: sidebar, Website (below Plans). Needs settings.manage; Super admins always have it. Website editor with the list of sections"},{"h":"How it works","a":"how-it-works","t":"Open Website and choose a tab at the top. With more than one active language, pick the language you are writing in under Editing language. Text is saved separately for each language. Make your changes and click Save. They appear on the home page at once. Click View site to see the result in a new tab. You start from the built-in page. Boxes already show the text in use. Text you do not change keeps the built-in wording, so wording fixes and translations in later updates still reach it. To go back, clear the box. Emptying a box and saving restores the built-in text for that language. One Save stores every tab. If something is wrong, the page opens on the tab with the problem and lists it. Pictures chosen before the error must be chosen again."},{"h":"Sections","a":"sections","t":"Eight sections make up the home page: Hero, Product showcase, Screenshot tour, Fast checkout, Pricing, FAQ, Contact and Closing call to action. The Hero also holds the feature cards and the How it works steps. Control What it does Grip (dots) Drag a section up or down. With the keyboard, focus the grip and use the arrow keys Background As designed, Plain, Soft tint, Accent tint or Dark brand. Each section has its own choice Switch Shows or hides the section The page header shows your logo, menu links (Features, Screenshots, FAQ and Pricing), a language menu when more than one language is active, Log in and, while sign-up is open, Get started. On a phone the links move into a menu button. Some sections hide themselves when they have nothing to show: Pricing without a public plan, Contact without a phone or WhatsApp number, Screenshot tour without slides and FAQ without questions. The menu links to hidden sections disappear too. The older Languages section (\"Your shop, in your language\") has been removed. Visitors still change the language from the globe menu in the page header. If you saved a section order before, Fast checkout is placed after Screenshot tour; drag it elsewhere if you like."},{"h":"Design","a":"design","t":"The preview on the right changes as you choose. Design tab with colours, headings, shapes and a live preview Option Choices Brand colour Buttons, icons and highlights. Empty uses the panel's accent colour Accent colour Dots, underlines and markers Heading colour Empty follows the light and dark theme Heading font Any font of the panel, or the same as the rest of the site Highlighted words in headings Colour, Underline, Marker, Gradient or None. It applies to the last words of a heading Button shape Pill, Rounded or Square Card corners Round, Soft or Sharp Space between sections Normal, Compact or Airy Page width Normal, Narrow or Wide Hero picture side Right or Left Page background Gradient, Plain or Tinted Animations On or Off Custom CSS For anything else. Up to 20,000 characters, used on the home page only. Landing page classes start with .lp- Colours are hex codes such as #8a1538. The reset button beside a colour goes back to automatic."},{"h":"Content tabs","a":"content-tabs","t":"Tab What you edit Hero Label, main heading, text, note, hero picture, How it works heading, and the lists Feature cards (up to 9), How it works steps (5) and Benefits strip (8) Product showcase Heading and text, the light and dark screen pictures, the banner text and Highlights (6) Screenshot tour Heading and text, and up to 8 slides Fast checkout Small label, heading, text, Checkout screenshot and Checkout points (6). Two or four points look best Pricing Heading and text. Plans, prices and the comparison table come from Plans FAQ Heading, text and up to 30 questions Closing call to action Label, heading, text and picture Buttons & badges Button labels, the trial line, and the badges under the plans (6) and in the closing banner (4)"},{"h":"Lists","a":"lists","t":"Feature cards, steps, benefits, highlights, checkout points, questions and badges work the same way: Add creates an item. Choose an icon, then write a title and a short text. Drag the grip to reorder, and use the bin to remove an item. An item you add needs a title in at least one language. A question needs a title and an answer. If an item you added has no text in a language, the English text is shown there. An empty list hides that block."},{"h":"Screenshot slides","a":"screenshot-slides","t":"Each slide has a picture, an icon, a tab label, a title, a short text and key points (one per line). A new slide must have a picture; the recommended size is 1800 × 880 px. On a built-in slide, Use the built-in picture removes your upload."},{"h":"Trial length in text","a":"trial-length-in-text","t":"Write :days in the trial line or in a badge to show the length of the trial. A badge that uses :days is hidden when there is no trial."},{"h":"Pictures","a":"pictures","t":"PNG, JPG or WebP, up to 4 MB. Each box shows the recommended size, for example 1800 × 1200 px for the checkout screenshot. Tick remove on an uploaded picture to go back to the built-in one. Files are kept in the place set under File storage."},{"h":"Contact & demo","a":"contact--demo","t":"Field What it does WhatsApp number With the country code. Adds a WhatsApp button and a floating chat button Phone number Adds a call button Contact name Shown above the buttons, for example \"Sales team\" Live demo link Where the Live demo button goes. Empty hides the button Until you save this page, the demo link comes from LANDING_DEMO_URL in .env. The contact box heading and text are on this tab too."},{"h":"Search & sharing","a":"search--sharing","t":"Field What it does Page title The title in the browser tab and in search results Description The short text under the title in search results Share picture Shown when the link is shared on social media. Recommended 1200 × 630 px"},{"h":"What is edited somewhere else","a":"what-is-edited-somewhere-else","t":"On the home page Edit it under Logo, favicon and platform name General settings Plans and prices Plans Start trial buttons (hidden while sign-up is closed) General settings, Sign-up Terms and Privacy Legal pages Languages in the header language menu Languages Menu and footer labels Languages, translations"},{"h":"Good to know","a":"good-to-know","t":"A fresh install needs no setup: the home page shows the built-in content until you change it. Saving writes \"Website updated\" to the Audit log, with which parts changed. The page content is cached for up to 5 minutes; saving clears it."},{"h":"Website is missing from the sidebar","a":"website-is-missing-from-the-sidebar","t":"Make sure your role has settings.manage, or is Super admin. Run php artisan optimize:clear on the server. Old cached config or routes hide new menu items."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"General settings Languages Plans Previous Dashboard Next Businesses How it works Sections Design Content tabsLists Screenshot slides Trial length in text Pictures Contact & demo Search & sharing What is edited somewhere else Good to know Website is missing from the sidebar Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/account/audit-log/","ti":"Audit Log","c":"Account & Billing","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The audit log records who changed what in your business, and when. Entries cannot be edited or deleted. Where to find it: sidebar > System > Audit log. Requires audit.view. Audit log table with user and event filters"},{"h":"Filters","a":"filters","t":"Field What it does Search Searches the entries. User Show one team member's actions (All users by default). Event Show one kind of event (All events). From (UTC) / To (UTC) Date range, as calendar days in UTC. To cannot be before From."},{"h":"Columns","a":"columns","t":"No., ID, When (UTC), User, Event, Record (what was changed, with its name or number), and Changes (each changed field, old value struck through beside the new one). Entries made by the system itself show System as the user."},{"h":"Events you can filter by","a":"events-you-can-filter-by","t":"created, updated, deleted, restored, permanently_deleted, batch_override, batch_expiry_corrected, password_changed, invitation_sent, invitation_resent, invitation_revoked, invitation_accepted and data_exported. The filter list also contains backup_created, backup_failed, backup_downloaded and backup_setting_changed. note Times are shown in UTC, not your business time zone, so they match what is stored."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Data Export Team Roles & Permissions Previous Support Next Notifications Filters Columns Events you can filter by Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/account/billing-and-plans/","ti":"Billing and Plans","c":"Account & Billing","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Billing shows your current plan, how much of its limits you have used, the plans you can switch to, and your invoices. You pay online through a gateway the platform has switched on. Where to find it: sidebar > System > Billing. Requires billing.manage, which only the Owner has. Billing page with current plan, usage bars and plan cards"},{"h":"Plans and the trial","a":"plans-and-the-trial","t":"New businesses start on a free Trial plan. The number of trial days is set by the platform administrator. The platform also sets every plan's name, price, currency, limits and features, so what you see on the Billing page is your platform's own catalogue. A plan controls two things: What Examples Limits Number of branches, team members (including pending invitations) and products. A limit can be unlimited. Features Loyalty points, Batch and expiry tracking, Stock take, Quotations, Daily owner summary, SMS. If a feature is not in your plan, its menu item is hidden and its pages say \"This feature is not included in your plan.\" The platform can also grant a business extra features or limits individually."},{"h":"Current plan","a":"current-plan","t":"The top card shows the plan name, its monthly and yearly price, your Billing cycle, and Trial ends or Renews on with the days left. Usage and limits shows bars for branches, team members and products against your plan limits. Banners warn you as time runs out: a trial reminder, and Payment overdue during the grace period."},{"h":"Pay or change plan","a":"pay-or-change-plan","t":"Under Available plans, choose Monthly or Yearly under Billing interval. On the plan you want, pick Pay with a gateway if more than one is offered. Click Subscribe, or Renew now for your current plan. Complete payment on the gateway's page. You return to the Billing page with a confirmation. Gateways are the ones the platform enabled: Stripe, Razorpay, Flutterwave or PayPal. Only gateways that accept the plan's currency are offered. If none are available you see \"Online payment is not available yet. Please contact us to activate your plan.\" A banner says \"Test mode: payments made now are not real.\" when a gateway is in test mode. Each payment covers one period. Renewal is manual: you pay again before the end date, and a reminder email is sent before it ends. Your current plan offers Renew now only in its last 7 days. Paying again for the same plan adds a new period after the one you already paid for. Switching to a different plan starts it today. The days left on your old plan are lost, not refunded and not carried over. A warning shows how many days before you confirm. If the payment page does not return you, open Billing again. A payment that is still processing shows \"We have not received your payment yet\" and confirms automatically."},{"h":"Stop renewal reminders","a":"stop-renewal-reminders","t":"On an active plan, click I won't renew to say you do not plan to continue. The plan stays active to the end of the paid period, then the shop becomes read-only and reminder emails stop. Click I'll renew to turn reminders back on."},{"h":"What happens when it lapses","a":"what-happens-when-it-lapses","t":"State What you can do Trial Full use until the trial ends. Active Full use. Payment overdue (grace) Full use for 7 days after the period ends. Renew to avoid read-only. Read-only You can view data, run reports and export. You cannot add or change anything, except pay, record refunds, update your profile, and export your data. warning In read-only mode every save is refused with \"Your subscription is not active, so changes are turned off.\" Support tickets still work so you can ask for help."},{"h":"Invoices","a":"invoices","t":"The Invoices table lists your latest invoices with Invoice number, Plan, Period, Amount and Status (Pending, Paid, Failed or Void). Click View receipt to open a printable receipt."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Support Data Export Team Branches Previous Data Export Next Profile Plans and the trial Current plan Pay or change planStop renewal reminders What happens when it lapses Invoices Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/account/notifications/","ti":"Notifications","c":"Account & Billing","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Notifications show what needs your attention right now. Nothing is stored: each alert is a live count and disappears when the count reaches zero. Where to find it: the bell in the top bar, which opens Notifications. No dedicated permission, but each alert depends on what you may see. Notifications page with alert cards"},{"h":"Alerts","a":"alerts","t":"Alert Shown when Needs Products low or out of stock Products are at or below their low-stock threshold in your branches. inventory.view Batches expired or expiring soon You track batches and some are expired or inside the expiry warning window. inventory.view and reports.inventory Customers with dues older than 30 days Customers have an open sale with a balance older than 30 days. customers.view Each alert is a card with a count. Click it to open the matching report or customer list. Without access to that screen, the alert still shows but does not link. When nothing is wrong you see \"You are all caught up.\" Counts are limited to the branches you work in."},{"h":"Announcements","a":"announcements","t":"The platform team can post an announcement banner at the top of the panel. Dismiss one to hide it for the rest of your browser session."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Inventory & Expiry reports Customers General Settings Previous Audit Log Alerts Announcements Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/account/profile/","ti":"Profile","c":"Account & Billing","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Your profile holds your own name, photo and password. Everyone in the business can open it. Where to find it: your name or avatar in the top bar > My Profile. No special permission needed. My Profile page with member details and change password"},{"h":"Member details","a":"member-details","t":"Field What it does Profile photo Optional. JPG, PNG or WebP, up to 2 MB. You can also remove the current photo. Name Your display name. Email Your login email. Read-only here. Role Your role in this business. Read-only. Branches The branches you are assigned to. Read-only. Click Save changes. Only an owner or manager can change your role or assigned branches. See Team."},{"h":"Change password","a":"change-password","t":"Enter your Current password. Enter a New password and Confirm password. It must differ from the current one and follow the password rules the platform sets. Click Change password. Changing your password signs you out of all your other devices. note Your profile still saves when the subscription is read-only."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Team Roles & Permissions Languages Previous Billing and Plans Next Support Member details Change password Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/account/support/","ti":"Support","c":"Account & Billing","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Support is a ticket inbox between your business and the platform team. Replies appear in the thread and are emailed to you. Where to find it: sidebar > Support, or the Support button in the top bar. Open to every team member, with no permission or plan needed. It keeps working even when the subscription is read-only. Support requests list with status column"},{"h":"Send a request","a":"send-a-request","t":"Click New request. Enter a Subject (4 to 120 characters). Pick a Type: Question, Billing, Something is broken or Feature request. Describe the problem under How can we help? (5 to 5,000 characters). Click Send. You can send up to 10 new requests per hour."},{"h":"Follow the conversation","a":"follow-the-conversation","t":"Tabs filter the list: all, Waiting for us, Answered and Closed, each with its count. Search by subject or request number (for example #12). The list shows Subject, Type, Status and Last update. Open requests stay on top. Status Meaning Waiting for us The team has not answered yet. Answered The team replied. Closed The request is finished. Open a request to see the Conversation. Type under Your reply and send with Enter (Shift+Enter for a new line). Any reply puts the request back in front of the team."},{"h":"Close a request","a":"close-a-request","t":"Click Close request and confirm. You can reopen it by replying. Once closed, a request cannot take new messages from you. Open a new request instead."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Billing & Plans Notifications Profile Previous Profile Next Audit Log Send a request Follow the conversation Close a request Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/branches/","ti":"Branches","c":"Branches","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"A branch is a location your team sells from and holds stock in. Stock, sales, shifts, transfers and purchase orders belong to a branch. Where to find it: Branches > Branches. Needs settings.manage. The number of active branches is limited by your plan. Branches list with the default branch marked"},{"h":"The branches list","a":"the-branches-list","t":"Tabs filter by status. Search by name or code. Columns: Name, Branch Code and Status. The default branch is marked Default. Row actions: Edit, Make default, and Activate or Deactivate."},{"h":"Add a branch","a":"add-a-branch","t":"Click New Branch. Enter a Name. It appears in the branch switcher and reports. Optionally enter a Branch Code. Leave it blank to auto-generate one like BR-0001. Set Status and click Save Branch. Only an active branch counts against your plan's branch limit. Adding or reactivating a branch stops with a message once the limit is reached. The new branch is assigned automatically to you and to every Owner of the business. Give other people access in Team."},{"h":"Default, deactivate","a":"default-deactivate","t":"Make default sets the branch used by default. Only an active branch can be the default. The default branch must stay active, so it cannot be deactivated. Deactivate hides the branch from the branch switcher and team assignment. If some people work only in that branch, you are warned that they will not be able to sign in until they are given another branch, and must confirm."},{"h":"Switch branch","a":"switch-branch","t":"If you have access to more than one active branch, a branch selector appears in the top bar. Choose a branch and the page reloads in that branch. You can only switch to active branches assigned to you. What follows the current branch: Stock quantities and low-stock badges in Stock levels and on the products list. New sales at the POS and the register shift you open. Reorder suggestions and the default From branch on a stock transfer. Starting quantities entered when you add a product."},{"h":"Who can see what","a":"who-can-see-what","t":"Each team member is assigned the branches they can work in (Branches on the team member form, see Team). Lists such as stock adjustments, transfers, purchase orders, purchase returns, stock takes and expenses only show records from your branches, and opening a record from another branch returns not found. Stock transfers are the way to move stock between branches. Products, categories, suppliers and price lists are shared across the business; a price list or discount rule can be limited to one branch."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Stock transfers Team Roles and permissions Previous Expenses Next Customers The branches list Add a branch Default, deactivate Switch branch Who can see what Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/catalogue/categories-brands-units/","ti":"Categories, Brands and Units","c":"Catalogue","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Categories, brands and units group your products and decide how quantities are counted. All three work the same way: create, edit, switch active/inactive, archive, restore, delete permanently. Where to find it: Inventory > Catalogue > Categories, Brands, Units. Permissions are categories.*, brands.* and units.* (view, create, update, delete). Categories list"},{"h":"Categories","a":"categories","t":"Categories organise the catalogue and the POS category list. They have two levels: a top-level category and its sub categories. Click New category (or the add-sub-category action on a row). Enter the Name. Choose a Parent category, or leave None (top level). Upload an Image (required, JPG, PNG or WebP, up to 2 MB). Set Active and click Save category. Notes: A category that has sub categories cannot be moved under another category. Archiving is refused while the category has sub categories or products. Delete permanently only works for an archived category never used by a product or sub category. Restoring fails if the parent is archived or the name is already taken. Import categories: CSV with columns name (required), parent (the parent category name; blank for top level) and status (active or inactive, default active). Use Download template for the exact header."},{"h":"Brands","a":"brands","t":"Brands let you filter and report by who makes a product. Field What it does Name Brand name, unique. Logo Optional. JPG, PNG or WebP, up to 1 MB. Active Off hides the brand from the product form without deleting it. Brands can also be imported from CSV (name, status) and are deleted permanently only when no product (archived ones included) uses them."},{"h":"Units","a":"units","t":"Units say how a product is counted or sold. Field What it does Name Full name, for example Kilogram. Unique. Short name Shown next to quantities, for example kg. Unique. Type Count, Weight, Volume or Length. Allows decimals On lets quantities such as 1.25 be sold. Weight, volume and length units default to decimals; count units do not. Active Off hides the unit from the product form. warning You cannot switch a unit to whole numbers while fractional stock, held sales or open purchase orders still use it with decimals. The units list can be filtered by type. Units can be imported from CSV (name and short_name required; type and status optional)."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Products Variants and attributes Previous Variants and Attributes Next Print Labels Categories Brands Units Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/catalogue/print-labels/","ti":"Print Labels","c":"Catalogue","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Generate a print-ready sheet of labels with barcodes for any active product or variant. Where to find it: Inventory > Catalogue > Print Labels. Needs products.view. Print labels builder with sheet options"},{"h":"Print a sheet","a":"print-a-sheet","t":"Add the products you need. There are three ways, and you can mix them: Search: type a name, SKU or barcode in the search box and click a result. Press Enter on an exact code to add it at once. Scan: scan a barcode at any time, wherever the cursor is. Each scan adds one more label for that item. Select products: opens a pop-up where you can pick many items at once (see below). Only active products and variants appear. Each line shows the SKU, price and stock in the current branch. Clicking or scanning an item that is already in the list adds one to its quantity. Set the quantity for each line (0 to 500 labels). A line set to 0 stays in the list but is marked Not printed. Under Sheet options, choose Paper / label size: 24 per sheet, 63.5 x 33.9 mm (A4) 58 mm thermal roll 80 mm thermal roll Tick what to Show on each label: Product name, SKU, Price, Barcode. At least one is required. Check the totals under the options: Products, Labels and, for A4, Sheets. Click Generate sheet. A print-ready page opens in a new tab. Click Print. The price printed is the variant's current selling price. If a variant has no barcode, its SKU is used to draw the barcode."},{"h":"Select many products at once","a":"select-many-products-at-once","t":"Click Select products to open the pop-up. Narrow the list with the search box, a category (sub-categories are listed under their parent) and a brand. Tick the items you want. Click Show more to load the next page of results. Select all ticks every item that matches the filters, up to 1,000. If more match, only the first 1,000 are ticked and a message asks you to use the filters for the rest. Clear all unticks everything. Click Add selected. Each new item is added with a quantity of 1. Items already in your list are marked Added and cannot be ticked again."},{"h":"Change many quantities at once","a":"change-many-quantities-at-once","t":"Once the list has items, a bar above it offers: Control What it does Quantity for all Type a number and click Apply to give every line that quantity Match stock Sets each line to the stock in this branch, so you print one label per piece. Items with no stock are set to 0, and no line goes above 500 Clear all Empties the list Use the cross on a line to remove just that item."},{"h":"Limits","a":"limits","t":"You can print at most 1,000 labels at a time. The running total turns into a warning above that, and Generate sheet stays off until you lower the quantities. Barcodes are drawn at their true size so scanners can read them. If a code is too long to fit on the chosen label, it is printed as text instead, and a note at the top of the print page lists those codes. On a thermal roll a long barcode may be turned to run along the roll."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Products Previous Categories, Brands and Units Next Stock Levels Print a sheet Select many products at once Change many quantities at once Limits Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/catalogue/products/","ti":"Products","c":"Catalogue","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Products are the items you sell. Each product has a price, a category, a unit and stock per branch. Where to find it: Inventory > Catalogue > Products. Needs products.view to see the list, products.create to add or import, products.update to edit, and products.delete to archive or delete. Products list with status tabs and filters"},{"h":"The products list","a":"the-products-list","t":"Tabs at the top filter by status, each with a count: All, Active, Draft and Archived. Use the search box to find a product by name, SKU or barcode. The toolbar also filters by category, brand, unit, type (Simple or Variable) and stock (In stock or Out of stock). The stock figure and the stock filter use the branch you are currently working in. Row actions: Action What it does View Opens the product page (Overview, Variants, Inventory and Activity tabs). Edit Opens the edit form. Move to draft / Activate Switches the product between draft and active. Duplicate Makes a copy and opens it in the editor. Archive Hides the product. It can be restored from the Archived tab. Restore Brings an archived product back. Delete permanently Removes an archived product for good. note Draft products are hidden from the POS register. A product with sales or stock history cannot be deleted permanently and can stay archived."},{"h":"Add a product","a":"add-a-product","t":"Click New product. Fill in Product info, Pricing, Status and Organization (below). Click Save product, or Save as draft to keep it hidden for now. Add product form If you save a product with no stock, the confirmation tells you so, because a product with no stock cannot be rung up."},{"h":"Product info","a":"product-info","t":"Field What it does Thumbnail Main picture shown in the catalogue, POS grid and receipts. JPG, PNG or WebP, up to 5 MB. Name Display name. Required, up to 255 characters. Product Type Simple (one SKU) or Variable (one SKU per combination of attributes such as size or colour). See Variants and attributes. SKU Unique code for the product. Required for simple products; leave it blank and one is generated. The sparkle button generates one for you. Barcode Optional scannable code. The sparkle button generates a valid EAN-13. Must be unique. Cost Price What you paid. Used in profit reports, never shown to customers. Starting quantity Only when adding. Sets the opening stock in your current branch. Whole numbers unless the unit allows decimals. Tax Group Which tax group applies. No tax by default. A live preview shows the tax on the price. Description Up to 5000 characters."},{"h":"Media","a":"media","t":"Add up to 5 extra pictures (JPG, PNG or WebP, 5 MB each). When editing, tick Remove under a saved picture to delete it on save."},{"h":"Pricing","a":"pricing","t":"Field What it does Base price The regular selling price. Required. Discounted price Optional sale price. Leave empty to sell at the base price. Alert quantity Low-stock threshold for this product. Leave empty to use the default from Settings. In stock Turn off to keep the product visible but unavailable."},{"h":"Batches & expiry","a":"batches--expiry","t":"Field What it does Track batches / lot numbers Keeps stock per lot. See Batches and expiry. Track expiry dates Each lot has an expiry date. The earliest expiry is sold first and expired stock cannot be sold. Default expiry date Pre-filled when receiving stock. Cannot be in the past. When you switch tracking on for a product that already has stock, that stock moves into an Opening batch. You cannot switch tracking off while stock still sits in batches, and you cannot switch it on while any stock is negative."},{"h":"Status and organization","a":"status-and-organization","t":"Status: on means active, off saves a draft. Brand (optional), Unit (required), Category (required), Sub category (optional) and Tags (comma separated). Only active brands, units and categories are offered. See Categories, brands and units. warning You cannot change a product from a decimal unit (such as kg) to a whole-number unit while fractional stock, held carts or open purchase orders still use it."},{"h":"Edit, duplicate, archive","a":"edit-duplicate-archive","t":"Edit opens the same form without the starting quantity. Change stock with Stock adjustments instead. Duplicate copies the product and opens the copy. Archive hides it. Restoring needs the category, brand and unit to still be available. Your plan may limit the number of products. Adding, duplicating or restoring a product stops with a message once you reach the limit."},{"h":"Import products from CSV","a":"import-products-from-csv","t":"Click Import products, then Download template. Fill in the file and upload it (comma-separated, up to 2 MB). Click Import products and read the results table. Rows with a problem are skipped and listed with the reason. Required columns: name, sku, description, category, brand, unit, base_price. Category, brand and unit are matched by name against active records (the unit by its full name, not the short name). Optional columns: discounted_price, charge_tax, in_stock, barcode, tags, alert_quantity, track_batches, track_expiry, default_expiry_date, starting_quantity, batch_number, expiry_date. note Imported products have no picture and land as drafts. Add a photo and activate each one from the editor."},{"h":"Product page","a":"product-page","t":"Click View on a product to see: Overview: product profile, pricing breakdown and stock summary. Variants: the variants, their prices, and a form to add more. Inventory: stock by branch, plus batches for tracked products. Activity: every stock change with date, reason, quantity, balance and who made it."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Variants and attributes Categories, brands and units Print labels Stock levels Tax rates and groups Previous Quotations Next Variants and Attributes The products list Add a productProduct info Media Pricing Batches & expiry Status and organization Edit, duplicate, archive Import products from CSV Product page Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/catalogue/variants-and-attributes/","ti":"Variants and Attributes","c":"Catalogue","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"An attribute is a characteristic such as Color or Size, with a list of values (Black, White, Red). A variable product has one variant per combination of values, and each variant has its own SKU, barcode, cost and stock. Where to find it: Inventory > Catalogue > Attributes (attributes.view, attributes.create, attributes.update). Variants are managed on the product form and on the product page (products.update). Attribute form with values and category limits"},{"h":"Create an attribute","a":"create-an-attribute","t":"Click New Attribute. Enter a Name, for example Size. Set Status. Inactive hides the attribute from the variant builder without deleting it. Under Values, type each value and click Add Value. Under Applies to categories, untick the categories that should not offer this attribute. With everything ticked it is available for every category. Use the search box, Select all and Clear all to speed this up. Click Save Attribute. When editing an attribute you add new values with New Value and Add Value, and switch a value on or off with its Activate or Deactivate button. Names are unique, and a value can only appear once per attribute. You can also create an attribute while building a product: click Add Attribute in the Variants section and type the name and comma separated values (for example Red, Blue, Green). This needs attributes.create."},{"h":"Make a variable product","a":"make-a-variable-product","t":"On the product form choose Variable as the Product Type. In Variants, tick the attribute values you want (for example Size: Small, Medium and Color: Red, Blue). Click Generate Variants. Rows also update automatically as you tick values. Optionally use Fill all rows to set the same Cost Price and Starting quantity on every row, then click Fill all. Edit each row: SKU, Barcode, Cost Price, Starting quantity (new products only), Status (Active or Inactive) and Tax Group. Use the remove button to drop a row. Save the product. Variant grid on the product form Rules: A variable product needs at least one variant, and up to 100 are allowed. SKUs and barcodes must be unique. A combination cannot appear twice. Only attributes that apply to the product's category can be used."},{"h":"Manage variants on the product page","a":"manage-variants-on-the-product-page","t":"Open a product and go to the Variants tab. Add variant: pick one value per attribute, then enter SKU, Barcode, Cost Price, optionally a Base price and Discounted price, and the Starting quantity. Adding a variant to a simple product turns it into a variable product. Edit prices: change a variant's Cost Price, Base price and Discounted price. Leave the base price empty to use the product's price (shown as Same as product). A discounted price must be lower than the base price. Remove: deletes a variant. You cannot remove the last variant of a variable product. The table shows each variant's selling price after any price list or discount rule, and its current stock in your branch."},{"h":"Stock on the Base product","a":"stock-on-the-base-product","t":"A simple product keeps a hidden Base product that holds its stock. Once real variants exist, the Base product is no longer sold. If it still holds stock, a Stock on the Base product card appears: choose the Branch, the variant to Move to, and the Quantity, then click Move stock. You can move part of it and repeat. This is not available for products that track batches."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Products Categories, brands and units Stock adjustments Previous Products Next Categories, Brands and Units Create an attribute Make a variable product Manage variants on the product pageStock on the Base product Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/expenses/","ti":"Expenses","c":"Expenses","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Expenses record money the business spent, such as rent, utilities or salaries. They feed your net profit figures, and an expense paid in cash can also come out of an open register shift. Where to find it: Expenses > Expenses and Expenses > Expense categories. Permissions: expenses.view, expenses.create, expenses.update, expenses.delete. Managing categories needs expenses.update. Expenses list with filters and total"},{"h":"The expenses list","a":"the-expenses-list","t":"Filter by date range, branch, category and payment method, or search by expense number or payee. Total of these expenses shows the sum of everything matching the filters. Export CSV downloads the filtered list (Number, Date, Branch, Category, Payee, Method, Reference, Amount, Note). Columns: Expense no. (starting EXP-), Date, Branch, Category, Paid to, Payment Method and Amount. Row actions let you view the receipt, edit, and delete. You only see branches you have access to."},{"h":"Add an expense","a":"add-an-expense","t":"Click New expense. Fill in the form and click Save expense. Field What it does Expense date The day the money was spent. It cannot be in the future. Amount More than zero, up to 2 decimals. Category The kind of cost. Reports group expenses by category. Branch The branch the cost belongs to, used for profit per branch. Payment Method How it was paid. Gateway, credit and loyalty methods are not offered. Reference A cheque, transaction or invoice number. Required for payment methods that need one, such as card or bank transfer. Paid to Who you paid, for example the landlord. Note Optional detail, such as the period covered. Paid from the till See below. Receipt Photo or PDF of the bill, up to 5 MB. Kept privately; only people who can view expenses can open it. note You need at least one active expense category and one active payment method before an expense can be saved."},{"h":"Paid from the till","a":"paid-from-the-till","t":"Turn on Paid from the till when the cash came out of your drawer. It is only available for a cash payment method, on a branch where you have an open shift. Saving then also records a cash-out on your open shift, so the expected cash goes down and the drawer still balances. Leave it off for cash paid from somewhere else, such as the safe. See Shifts and cash."},{"h":"Edit and delete","a":"edit-and-delete","t":"Editing an expense paid from a still-open shift keeps its branch fixed, and updates or removes the till cash-out if you change the amount or untick the option. Once that shift is closed, the amount, payment method and branch are locked and the expense cannot be deleted. Other details can still be edited. Delete asks for confirmation and removes the expense (and its till cash-out when the shift is open)."},{"h":"Expense categories","a":"expense-categories","t":"Categories group expenses (for example Rent, Utilities, Salaries). Open Expense categories and click New category. Enter a Name (unique) and set Active. Click Save category. Switch a category on or off from the list. A category that already has expenses cannot be deleted; deactivate it instead. An expense keeps working with a category that was deactivated later."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Shifts and cash Branches Purchase orders Previous Purchase Returns Next Branches The expenses list Add an expensePaid from the till Edit and delete Expense categories Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/getting-started/dashboard/","ti":"Dashboard","c":"Getting Started","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The Dashboard summarises how the business is doing for a period you choose. What you see depends on your permissions: figures about takings need report access, stock widgets need inventory access. Where to find it: Dashboard (top of the sidebar). Every signed-in member can open it. Dashboard with key number cards and sales trend chart"},{"h":"Period and branch","a":"period-and-branch","t":"Choose Today, 7 days, 30 days or 90 days at the top. The default is 7 days. If you work in more than one branch, pick one in the Branch filter or leave All branches. Numbers are compared with the previous period of the same length."},{"h":"Get started checklist","a":"get-started-checklist","t":"A new business that has not yet completed a sale sees a Get started card with up to three steps, each shown only if you can do it: Add your first product (products.create), Add some stock (inventory.adjust) and Make your first sale (sales.create). The card disappears after the first completed sale."},{"h":"Key numbers","a":"key-numbers","t":"Needs reports.sales. Each card shows the figure, a small trend line and the change against the previous period. The icon colours are fixed and do not follow the accent colour; Refunds turns red only when there are refunds. Card What it shows Revenue Completed sales total, before refunds and including tax. Gross profit Net sales minus cost price, with the margin. Needs reports.financial. If some items sold have no cost price the margin is hidden. Orders Number of completed sales. Average basket Revenue divided by orders. Items sold Total quantity sold. Refunds Amount refunded, by the day each refund was issued."},{"h":"Charts and boards","a":"charts-and-boards","t":"Needs reports.sales unless noted. Widget What it shows Sales trend This period against the previous period, day by day. Sales by Payment Method How takings split across payment methods. Busiest hours Orders by hour of the day. Sales by category Which categories sell most. Customer insights New and returning customers, top customers, and loyalty points issued and redeemed when loyalty is on. Needs customers.view too. Sales breakdown Subtotal, discounts given, tax collected, refunded, unpaid balance and total sales. Branch comparison Takings per branch. Shown when you work in several branches and have All branches selected."},{"h":"Stock and operations","a":"stock-and-operations","t":"Widget Needs What it shows Inventory health reports.inventory Stock value, low stock, out of stock and slow movers (no sales in the last days shown). Expiry watch reports.inventory, tracked batches and a plan that includes batch expiry Expired and soon-to-expire stock. Open shifts shifts.view Cashiers with an open register: opening time, opening cash and expected cash, with a badge when a shift has been open too long. Up to 6 are listed; select a row to open the shift, or more open shifts for the rest. Top Products reports.sales Best sellers for the period. Recent Sales reports.sales The latest sales, with a link to all sales. Low stock inventory.view Products running low, or \"Nothing is running low.\" tip Open the bell in the header for alerts about low stock, expiring batches and overdue customer dues. See Navigating the Panel."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Reports Shifts and Cash Stock Adjustments Previous Navigating the Panel Next POS Terminal Period and branch Get started checklist Key numbers Charts and boards Stock and operations Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/getting-started/navigating-the-panel/","ti":"Navigating the Panel","c":"Getting Started","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The panel has a sidebar for pages and a header for tools you use everywhere: search, notifications, switching business or branch, language, colours and your account menu. Header with search, notifications, branch switch, language and account menu"},{"h":"Sidebar","a":"sidebar","t":"The Dashboard sits at the top. Everything else is in collapsible groups: Sales, Inventory, Tax, Pricing, Purchasing, Expenses, Branches, People, Reports, Help and System. You only see items your role can open and your plan includes. See the table in the Overview. Use the menu button in the header (Toggle sidebar) to collapse or expand it. The group containing the page you are on stays open."},{"h":"Header tools","a":"header-tools","t":"Tool What it does Search box \"Search products, customers, sales...\" finds products, customers and sales, and also lists sidebar pages. Support Opens the Support page. Open to every member. Notifications (bell) A count and a list of what needs attention: products low or out of stock, batches expired or expiring soon, and customers with dues older than 30 days. Each links to the matching report or customer list when you have access. View all notifications opens the full page. Not shown on the POS terminal. Business switch Appears only if your account belongs to more than one business. Branch switch Appears only if you can work in more than one branch. The panel shows data for the branch you pick. Language Appears when more than one language is active. Colour palette Pick an accent colour (Black, Amethyst, Ocean, Rose). Hidden when the owner fixed an accent colour in Settings. Account menu Shows your name, email, business and branch. Contains Profile, the Theme switch (Light, Dark, System) and Logout."},{"h":"Quick page search","a":"quick-page-search","t":"Press Ctrl+K (Cmd+K on Mac) to open Search pages.... Type to filter the sidebar pages, use the arrow keys to move, Enter to open and Esc to close."},{"h":"Banners you may see","a":"banners-you-may-see","t":"Free trial reminder with days left, and a link to Billing (you can dismiss it for the session). Payment overdue (grace period) and subscription not active (read-only) notices. Verify your email, shown to the owner when the platform requires verification. A maintenance notice or announcements set by the platform administrator."},{"h":"The guided tour","a":"the-guided-tour","t":"Select Take a tour at the bottom of the sidebar. The tour walks through the Dashboard, the menu groups and how to add a product, and only shows steps you have access to. Use Next, Back or Skip tour; you can resume later from the same button. The owner can turn the tour off under Settings > Appearance (\"Show the system tour to new users\")."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Dashboard Profile Notifications Languages Branches Previous Setup Wizard Next Dashboard Sidebar Header toolsQuick page search Banners you may see The guided tour Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/getting-started/setup-wizard/","ti":"Setup Wizard","c":"Getting Started","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The Setup Wizard is a four-step guide that appears for a brand-new business. It gets the essentials in place so you can start selling. Where to find it: it opens automatically the first time the owner reaches the Dashboard. Later, reopen it from System > Settings > Appearance > Setup guide > Run setup again. Requires settings.manage. Setup wizard showing the Business details step"},{"h":"How it works","a":"how-it-works","t":"The wizard opens once per session while it is pending, then the rest of the panel stays reachable. Each step has Save and continue (the last one says Finish) and Skip. Every step after the first also has Back. Close setup dismisses the guide. You can run it again from Settings. You only see the steps you have permission for."},{"h":"Step 1: Business details","a":"step-1-business-details","t":"Needs settings.manage. Field What it does Currency The currency for prices and reports. Choosing one fills in a matching symbol. Symbol The currency symbol shown next to amounts (up to 6 characters). Default tax rate (%) The shop-wide tax rate, 0 to 100. Price type Exclusive (tax added on top) or Inclusive (tax included in the price). Business time zone Shown only if you have loyalty.manage. Decides the business day, for example when loyalty points expire. These use the same rules as the Settings page."},{"h":"Step 2: Your first branch","a":"step-2-your-first-branch","t":"Needs settings.manage. Rename the default branch to your shop's real name and edit its Branch code. Use Add branch to open the new-branch form for more. See Branches."},{"h":"Step 3: Your first products","a":"step-3-your-first-products","t":"Needs products.create. A product needs a category and a unit; a brand is optional. A General category and common units are already added. The step lists them with a Manage button each. You can: Add a product by hand. Import from a spreadsheet, after Download the template. Save and continue appears once you have at least one product. If you have none, you must add one or press Skip."},{"h":"Step 4: Invite your team","a":"step-4-invite-your-team","t":"Needs users.manage. Select Invite a team member to open the invitation form. If the owner's email is not verified yet, the step explains that and offers Resend link instead. See Team."},{"h":"When the wizard is finished","a":"when-the-wizard-is-finished","t":"Finishing or skipping the last step shows \"Your business is set up.\" and returns you to the Dashboard."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Sign Up and Onboarding Products Team Previous Sign Up and Onboarding Next Navigating the Panel How it works Step 1: Business details Step 2: Your first branch Step 3: Your first products Step 4: Invite your team When the wizard is finished Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/getting-started/signup-and-onboarding/","ti":"Sign Up and Onboarding","c":"Getting Started","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"A new business starts by creating an account on the Register page. After that, a short onboarding flow lets you pick a plan or free trial and enter your business details. Where to find it: /register on your site. Sign-up must be open (a platform setting); otherwise the page sends you to Sign in with the message \"Sign-up is currently closed.\" Create your account form"},{"h":"Create your account","a":"create-your-account","t":"Open the Register page. Enter your Full name, Email and Password, then confirm the password. Accept the Terms of Service and Privacy Policy. Select Create account. The password must meet the minimum length shown under the field. Some email domains can be blocked by the platform; you will see \"Email addresses from this domain cannot be used.\" You become the business Owner. The account starts with: A default branch called Main (code MAIN). The built-in roles, default payment methods and expense categories. Nine common units (Piece, Pack, Box, Dozen, Kilogram, Gram, Litre, Millilitre, Metre) and a General category, so your first product can be saved straight away. Five refund reasons: Changed mind, Damaged or faulty, Wrong item, Expired, Other. A free trial subscription. Your currency and time zone, taken from the platform defaults and your browser. You can change or remove all of these later."},{"h":"The onboarding steps","a":"the-onboarding-steps","t":"After registering you land in onboarding. The steps are Create account, Select plan, Business setup and, if you chose a paid plan, Payment."},{"h":"Select plan","a":"select-plan","t":"Choose Start your N-day free trial (full access, no credit card), or pick one of the paid plans. For paid plans, switch between Monthly and Yearly billing. Prices and limits come from the plans your platform administrator published. Select Continue, or Skip for now to continue on the trial. If you came from a pricing page link with a plan in it, that plan is preselected."},{"h":"Business setup","a":"business-setup","t":"Field What it does Business name Required. Names your business everywhere. Defaults to \"your name's business\". Business type Required. Pick from the list. Phone Required. Country Required. State Optional. Address Optional. Select Continue (or Skip for now). You can edit all of this later in General Settings."},{"h":"Payment","a":"payment","t":"This step appears only when you chose a paid plan and at least one online payment gateway is available for the plan's currency. You pay on the gateway's secure page. Choose Pay later, continue with the free trial to skip it. If the payment is still being confirmed you stay on the free trial until it goes through."},{"h":"Done","a":"done","t":"The final screen says \"Welcome to ...!\" and offers Go to Dashboard plus next steps: Add your first product, Set up your store settings and Invite your team. note You can change plan any time from System > Billing. See Billing & Plans."},{"h":"Verify your email","a":"verify-your-email","t":"If the platform requires email verification, a banner asks you to verify your address. Until the owner verifies, nobody in the business can invite team members or take online gateway payments. Select Resend link on the banner if the email did not arrive."},{"h":"Sign in later","a":"sign-in-later","t":"Use the Sign in page. If you forget your password, use the forgot password link to receive a reset email. If you send a form after your session has ended, nothing is saved: you are asked to sign in again and then return to the page you were on. On a demo site the Sign in page also has one-click demo buttons; see Demo mode. People you invite do not register; they accept an invitation. See Team."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Setup Wizard Navigating the Panel Billing & Plans First Login Previous Shop Panel Overview Next Setup Wizard Create your account The onboarding stepsSelect plan Business setup Payment Done Verify your email Sign in later Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/overview/","ti":"Shop Panel Overview","c":"","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The shop panel is where a business runs its day: selling at the POS terminal, managing products and stock, buying from suppliers, tracking expenses, and reading reports. Each business has its own isolated data, branches, team and settings. Shop panel dashboard with the sidebar menu on the left"},{"h":"What the panel manages","a":"what-the-panel-manages","t":"Selling: POS terminal, sales history, refunds, cash register shifts and quotations. Catalogue and stock: products, variants, categories, brands, units, stock levels, adjustments, transfers and stock takes. Tax and pricing: tax rates and groups, price lists, customer groups, discount rules, coupons and gift cards. Purchasing: suppliers, purchase orders, reorder suggestions and purchase returns. Expenses, branches and people: expense records, multiple branches, customers, loyalty points, your team and their roles. Reports and system: sales, payment, purchase, inventory, expiry and profit reports, plus settings, billing and the audit log."},{"h":"The sidebar menu","a":"the-sidebar-menu","t":"The menu is built from config/menu.php. You only see an item when your role has its permission and your plan includes its feature. The Dashboard sits above the groups. Group Items Permission needed Sales POS Terminal, Sales, Refunds, Refund Reasons, Shifts, Quotations sales.create, sales.view, sales.return, shifts.view, quotations.view Inventory (Catalogue) Products, Categories, Brands, Units, Attributes, Print Labels products.view, categories.view, brands.view, units.view, attributes.view Inventory (Stock) Stock levels, Stock Adjustments, Stock Transfers, Stock Takes inventory.view Tax Tax Rates, Tax Groups tax-rates.view, tax-groups.view Pricing Price Lists, Customer Groups, Discount Rules, Coupons, Gift cards price-lists.view, customer-groups.view, discount-rules.view, coupons.view, gift-cards.view Purchasing Suppliers, Purchase Orders, Reorder Suggestions, Purchase returns suppliers.view, purchase-orders.view, purchase-orders.create Expenses Expenses, Expense categories expenses.view Branches Branches settings.manage People Customers, Team, Roles & Permissions customers.view, users.manage Reports Sales Report, Payments Report, Purchases Report, Inventory Report, Expiry Report, Profit Report, Coupons report, Gift cards report reports.sales, reports.financial, reports.inventory Help Support Open to every member System Audit log, Billing, Settings audit.view, billing.manage, settings.manage"},{"h":"Access and permissions","a":"access-and-permissions","t":"Every action is controlled by a permission such as products.view or sales.create. Permissions are grouped into roles; each team member has one role and a set of branches they can work in. Six roles come built in (Owner, Admin, Manager, Cashier, Inventory Manager, Purchase Manager), and you can create your own. See Roles & Permissions and Team."},{"h":"Plan features","a":"plan-features","t":"Your plan sets limits on branches, team members and products, and switches some features on or off. Pages for a feature your plan does not include are hidden from the menu and refuse direct access. Feature Gates Quotations Sales > Quotations Stock take Inventory > Stock Takes Batch and expiry tracking Reports > Expiry Report, expiry pages Loyalty points Settings > Loyalty points, loyalty on customers Daily owner summary Settings > daily summary Coupons Pricing > Coupons, Coupons report Gift cards Pricing > Gift cards, Gift cards report SMS Settings > SMS settings and SMS templates Manage your plan under System > Billing. See Billing & Plans. note When your subscription is not active the panel becomes read-only: you can view and export your data and contact Support, but you cannot add or change anything. An overdue payment first gets a grace period with full access."},{"h":"Recommended setup path","a":"recommended-setup-path","t":"Sign up and finish onboarding: plan, business details. Run the Setup Wizard: currency, branch name, first products, team. Review General Settings and Payment Methods. Add categories, brands and units and your products. Put stock on your products with a stock adjustment. Set up tax and, if needed, price lists and discount rules. Invite your team and assign roles. Open a register and make your first sale on the POS Terminal."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Navigating the Panel Dashboard Billing & Plans Next Sign Up and Onboarding What the panel manages The sidebar menu Access and permissions Plan features Recommended setup path Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/people/customers/","ti":"Customers","c":"People","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The customer book holds the people and businesses you sell to. Attach a customer to a sale to apply their group pricing, sell on credit, earn loyalty points and keep a purchase history. Where to find it: People > Customers. Requires customers.view. Customers list with status tabs and an owing filter"},{"h":"Customer list","a":"customer-list","t":"Tabs filter by status: all, Active and Inactive. Search by name, phone, email or ID. Tick Customers who owe to show only those with an unpaid balance, and Sort by newest or highest balance. Switch between grid and list view."},{"h":"Add or edit a customer","a":"add-or-edit-a-customer","t":"Select New customer (needs customers.create). To change one, use Edit (needs customers.update). Field What it does First name Required. Last name, Company Optional. Phone / Email At least one is required, so you can reach the customer. Email must be unique in your business. A phone number that belongs to someone else shows a warning, and you tick the confirmation box to save anyway. Customer ID Unique code, generated for you. Change it if you use your own scheme. Customer group Groups can get their own price lists at checkout. See Customer Groups. Status Active or Inactive. Only active customers can be picked at the POS. Credit limit The most this customer can owe at one time. Empty means no limit. Tax ID For business customers who need it on their invoice. Birthday Lets you send a birthday offer. How they found you Walk-in, Referral, Online store, Social media or Other. Address, city, state, postal code, country Optional. Send offers and news Marketing opt-in. Only turn on if the customer agreed. Preferred channel SMS, Email or WhatsApp. Notes Only your team sees this. Cashiers can also add a customer quickly from the POS cart. See POS Terminal."},{"h":"Customer page","a":"customer-page","t":"Open a customer to see their profile and tabs: Tab Shows Overview Total spent, number of purchases, last purchase, amount owed and, with loyalty on, points. Choose a period: 7 days, 30 days, 90 days, 12 months or all time. Loyalty points Balance, next tier, points expiring soon, history, and an Adjust form. Only when the program is on or the customer has points. Purchase history The latest sales for this customer in your branches. Payments Unpaid sales and the payments you collected, each with a receipt. Credit & limits Credit limit, remaining credit and Set limit. Notes Add and edit notes. New sale opens the POS with this customer already attached."},{"h":"Credit sales and balances","a":"credit-sales-and-balances","t":"A customer's balance is what they still owe on open (credit) sales. Credit sales happen at the POS when: Allow credit sales (checkout with a balance due) is on in Settings > Cashier (POS), and the sale has a customer attached. If a sale would take the customer over their credit limit, checkout refuses it. A user who can edit the customer can raise the limit right from the till."},{"h":"Collect a payment","a":"collect-a-payment","t":"Needs customers.collect. Open the customer and select Collect payment. Enter the Amount. It settles their oldest unpaid sales first and cannot exceed what they owe. Choose the Method. Cash goes into your open register shift, so you need one open. Add an optional reference (a card slip or bank transfer number) and note. Submit. A receipt number is issued; you can open it later from the Payments tab. You can also collect on a single sale from its page. See Sales."},{"h":"Statement","a":"statement","t":"Select Statement on a customer to see every sale, payment and refund with a running balance. Pick a date range (leave empty for everything; the opening balance is what they owed before the first date) and Print statement."},{"h":"Alerts","a":"alerts","t":"The header bell warns about customers with dues older than 30 days and links to the list filtered to those who owe."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Loyalty Customer Groups Sales POS Terminal Previous Branches Next Loyalty Customer list Add or edit a customer Customer page Credit sales and balances Collect a payment Statement Alerts Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/people/loyalty/","ti":"Loyalty","c":"People","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Loyalty points reward customers who come back. They earn points on paid sales, spend them as money off a later sale, and unused points can expire. The program is switched off until you turn it on. Where to find it: System > Settings > Loyalty points (loyalty.manage). Points on customers and at the POS appear once the program is on. Requires the Loyalty points plan feature. Loyalty points settings with earning, spending and expiry rules"},{"h":"Turn it on and set the rules","a":"turn-it-on-and-set-the-rules","t":"Open Settings > Loyalty points. Turn on Loyalty program. Sales without a customer never earn. Fill in the rules below. An example panel shows what a sample sale earns and what the points are worth. Save."},{"h":"Earning","a":"earning","t":"Field What it does Points given How many points the customer gets each time they spend the amount in the next box. For every amount spent The spend that earns those points. Example: 1 point for every 10 spent. Amount counted Goods before tax (the price after any discount, tax left out) or Total including tax. Points are earned once a sale is fully paid. The part of a sale paid with points does not earn points. Fractions are kept behind the scenes and the customer sees whole points."},{"h":"Spending","a":"spending","t":"Field What it does Points in a reward How many points make one reward. Money off for those points How much comes off the bill for them. Example: 100 points = 1 off. Minimum balance to spend Customers can spend points once they have at least this many. Most of a sale points can pay A share of the sale total, 1 to 100 percent."},{"h":"Expiry","a":"expiry","t":"Field What it does Points expire after Months until earned points expire. Enter 0 for points that never expire. Warn customers Days before expiry to remind them. Remind customers before points expire Sends the \"Loyalty points expiring\" message by email and SMS where the customer has those details. Edit the wording under message templates. Business time zone The day points expire is counted in this zone. note Points are never spendable after their expiry date, but recording expiries and sending reminders run from the daily scheduler. Make sure the Laravel scheduler cron job is set up on your server. See Cron Jobs. Default values for a new business: earn 1 point per 10 spent on goods before tax, 100 points are worth 1, minimum balance 100, at most 50% of a sale, expiry after 12 months, warning 14 days before."},{"h":"Tiers","a":"tiers","t":"Tiers are levels such as Silver or Gold. Once a customer has earned enough points in total, they move up and earn points faster. Under Tiers, select Add tier. Enter a Tier name, Reached after earning (lifetime points earned) and Earns points (a multiplier, for example 1.5 times). Save. Each tier shows how many customers sit in it. You can add up to 10 tiers. Tiers are optional; without them everyone earns at the normal rate. A customer's tier is based on lifetime points earned, not on their current balance."},{"h":"At the POS","a":"at-the-pos","t":"With a customer attached, the cart shows their points balance, how many points the sale will earn and any points expiring soon. At payment, Use loyalty points lets the cashier enter Points to use or press Use max; the window shows what they are worth off the sale. Spending uses the points closest to expiry first. See POS Terminal."},{"h":"On the customer","a":"on-the-customer","t":"Open a customer's Loyalty points tab to see their balance, tier, next tier, points expiring and a history with types: Earned, Spent, Expired, Adjusted, Taken back (refund) and Returned (refund). With loyalty.manage you can select Adjust to add or remove points: enter the points (for example 50 or -20), a required reason and an optional expiry date. Adjustments are whole numbers."},{"h":"Refunds","a":"refunds","t":"When a sale with points is refunded, the share of points earned is taken back and the share paid with points is returned to the customer. See Refunds."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Customers POS Terminal Refunds Email Settings SMS Settings Previous Customers Next Team Turn it on and set the rulesEarning Spending Expiry Tiers At the POS On the customer Refunds Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/people/roles-and-permissions/","ti":"Roles and Permissions","c":"People","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Access in the panel is controlled by permissions. A role is a named set of permissions, and each team member has exactly one role. What a person sees in the menu and what buttons they get follows their role. Where to find it: People > Roles & Permissions. Requires users.manage. Role form with permissions grouped by module"},{"h":"Built-in roles","a":"built-in-roles","t":"Every business gets six roles. Their names cannot be changed or deleted, but you can adjust the permissions of all except Owner. Role Access Owner Everything, including billing and data export. Always has full access and cannot be edited. A business must keep at least one active Owner. Admin Everything except the two Owner-only permissions (data.export, billing.manage). Manager Everything except settings, team and audit log (settings.manage, users.manage, audit.view) and the Owner-only permissions. Cashier Sell and return: products, categories, brands and units (view), sales (view, create, return), customers (view, create), inventory (view) and quotations (view, create, update). Inventory Manager Products, categories, brands, units, attributes and inventory, without delete rights. Purchase Manager Products, suppliers, purchase orders, tax rates and tax groups, and inventory."},{"h":"All permissions","a":"all-permissions","t":"Owner has every permission. \"Yes\" means the role has it by default; blank means it does not. These defaults are given to each new business and can be changed per role. Permission Allows Admin, Manager Cashier Inventory Manager Purchase Manager products.view See products and print labels Yes Yes Yes Yes products.create Add products Yes Yes Yes products.update Edit products Yes Yes Yes products.delete Delete products Yes Yes categories.view See categories Yes Yes Yes categories.create Add categories Yes Yes categories.update Edit categories Yes Yes categories.delete Delete categories Yes brands.view See brands Yes Yes Yes brands.create Add brands Yes Yes brands.update Edit brands Yes Yes brands.delete Delete brands Yes units.view See units Yes Yes Yes units.create Add units Yes Yes units.update Edit units Yes Yes units.delete Delete units Yes suppliers.view See suppliers Yes Yes suppliers.create Add suppliers Yes Yes suppliers.update Edit suppliers Yes Yes suppliers.delete Delete suppliers Yes Yes attributes.view See attributes Yes Yes attributes.create Add attributes Yes Yes attributes.update Edit attributes Yes Yes tax-rates.view See tax rates Yes Yes tax-rates.create Add tax rates Yes Yes tax-rates.update Edit tax rates Yes Yes tax-groups.view See tax groups Yes Yes tax-groups.create Add tax groups Yes Yes tax-groups.update Edit tax groups Yes Yes customer-groups.view See customer groups Yes customer-groups.create Add customer groups Yes customer-groups.update Edit customer groups Yes price-lists.view See price lists Yes price-lists.create Add price lists Yes price-lists.update Edit price lists Yes price-lists.delete Delete price lists Yes discount-rules.view See discount rules Yes discount-rules.create Add discount rules Yes discount-rules.update Edit discount rules Yes coupons.view See coupons Yes coupons.create Add coupons Yes coupons.update Edit coupons and switch them on or off Yes coupons.delete Delete unused coupons Yes gift-cards.view See gift cards Yes Yes gift-cards.sell Sell gift cards and check balances at the POS Yes Yes gift-cards.manage Adjust, extend and disable gift cards, and gift card settings Yes purchase-orders.view See purchase orders, purchase returns Yes Yes purchase-orders.create Create purchase orders and use reorder suggestions Yes Yes purchase-orders.update Edit purchase orders Yes Yes inventory.view See stock levels, adjustments, transfers, stock takes Yes Yes Yes Yes inventory.adjust Make stock adjustments Yes Yes Yes inventory.transfer Transfer stock between branches Yes Yes Yes sales.view See sales and receipts Yes Yes sales.create Use the POS terminal, open registers, collect balances Yes Yes sales.cancel Cancel sales and held carts Yes sales.return Process refunds and manage refund reasons Yes Yes refunds.approve Refund above the refund limit Yes customers.view See customers Yes Yes customers.create Add customers Yes Yes customers.update Edit customers, notes and credit limits Yes customers.collect Collect customer payments Yes reports.sales Sales and Payments reports, dashboard takings Yes reports.inventory Inventory and Expiry reports Yes reports.financial Purchases and Profit reports, gross profit Yes shifts.view See all shifts Yes expenses.view See expenses and categories Yes expenses.create Add expenses Yes expenses.update Edit expenses Yes expenses.delete Delete expenses Yes quotations.view See quotations Yes Yes quotations.create Create quotations Yes Yes quotations.update Edit quotations, change status, convert Yes Yes quotations.delete Delete draft quotations Yes loyalty.manage Loyalty settings and manual point adjustments Yes stock-batches.override Choose a batch by hand at the till Yes stock-batches.edit Correct batch expiry dates Yes settings.manage Settings, branches, setup wizard, payment methods Admin only users.manage Team, invitations, roles Admin only audit.view See the audit log Admin only data.export Export business data Owner only billing.manage Billing and plans Owner only note Pages for features your plan does not include stay hidden even if the role has the permission: Quotations, Stock Takes, expiry, loyalty, owner summary and SMS. See the Overview."},{"h":"Create a role","a":"create-a-role","t":"Select Add role. Enter the Role name, which is shown when assigning the role. Optionally Start from a preset (Cashier, Manager, Inventory Manager or Purchase Manager) or use Copy permissions from a role to begin from an existing role. Tick permissions, module by module. Each module card has Select all. Standalone permissions (Manage settings, Manage team, View audit log, Manage billing, Export business data) are under Other permissions. Select Create role. Action names on the form map to permissions: View, Create, Update, Delete, Adjust, Transfer, Cancel, Return, Collect payment, Sales Report, Inventory Report, Financial Report, Choose batch manually (stock-batches.override) and Correct batch expiry dates (stock-batches.edit)."},{"h":"Edit or delete a role","a":"edit-or-delete-a-role","t":"Open a role from the list to edit its permissions. Built-in role names are fixed. Custom roles can be renamed and deleted. A role that is assigned to a team member cannot be deleted. The Owner role is shown read-only. Changes are written to the audit log."},{"h":"Limits on who can grant what","a":"limits-on-who-can-grant-what","t":"You can only give a role permissions you hold yourself. Only an Owner can give any permission. data.export and billing.manage are Owner-only; nobody else can hand them out. If you hold a role, you cannot add permissions to it. Ask an Owner. Only an Owner can assign the Owner role."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Team Audit Log Navigating the Panel Previous Team Next Reports Overview Built-in roles All permissions Create a role Edit or delete a role Limits on who can grant what Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/people/team/","ti":"Team","c":"People","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The Team page lists everyone who can sign in to your business. You invite people by email, give each one a role and the branches they can work in, and deactivate them when they leave. Where to find it: People > Team. Requires users.manage. Team list with member status tabs and pending invitations"},{"h":"The team list","a":"the-team-list","t":"Tabs show all, Active and Inactive members with counts. Search by name or email (\"Search team\"). Each row shows the member's role, branches and status, with Edit and activate/deactivate actions. Only an Owner can manage another Owner. Pending invitations appear below the list with the invited email, role, branches, who invited them and when the invitation was sent and expires. Each can be Resend or Revoked."},{"h":"Invite a team member","a":"invite-a-team-member","t":"Select Invite team member. The form opens in a dialog, and so does Edit. Enter their Email. They choose their own password. Pick a Role and one or more Branches (the branches they can switch to and work from). Select Send invitation. They receive an email with a link that works for 7 days. The button is disabled, with a reason on hover, when: the business owner's email is not verified yet (when the platform requires verification), your own email is not verified (\"Verify your own email address before inviting others.\"), or your plan's user limit is reached. Members and pending invitations both count."},{"h":"Rules that apply","a":"rules-that-apply","t":"You can only give a role whose permissions you hold yourself. Only an Owner can hand out the Owner role. You can only give branches you can reach yourself. You cannot invite someone who is already a member, or whose invitation is still pending (use Resend instead). Sending is rate limited per business and per person, and an invitation can be resent a limited number of times a day. Limits are set in config/invitations.php and can be raised through environment variables."},{"h":"If the email cannot be sent","a":"if-the-email-cannot-be-sent","t":"The page shows Share this invitation link once. Copy it and send it to the person privately. It works for 7 days and is not shown again; Resend creates a new one."},{"h":"Accepting an invitation","a":"accepting-an-invitation","t":"The invitee opens the link and sees \"Join business\" with the role they were invited as. A new person enters a Name, a password and confirmation, and accepts the Terms of Service and Privacy Policy. Someone who already has an account with that email enters that account's password to join. If they are signed in as a different user they are asked to sign out first. The link stops working when it is used, revoked, replaced by a resend, or expired. The business must still have a free seat on its plan when it is accepted."},{"h":"Edit a member","a":"edit-a-member","t":"Select Edit on a row. Change the Name, Profile photo (JPG, PNG or WebP, up to 2 MB), Role or Branches. At least one branch is required. The email is their login and cannot be changed here. Save. Things to know: If someone works for more than one business, only they can change their name and photo, on their Profile. You cannot change your own role or widen your own branches. Changing a member's role to one without users.manage revokes the invitations they sent."},{"h":"Activate and deactivate","a":"activate-and-deactivate","t":"Deactivating blocks sign-in to your business and revokes invitations the person sent. Reactivating needs a free user seat on your plan. You cannot deactivate yourself, and the business must always keep at least one active Owner."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Roles & Permissions Branches Billing & Plans Profile Previous Loyalty Next Roles and Permissions The team list Invite a team memberRules that apply If the email cannot be sent Accepting an invitation Edit a member Activate and deactivate Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/pricing/coupons/","ti":"Coupons","c":"Tax & Pricing","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"A coupon is a code the cashier enters at the POS for a discount on the whole sale. Unlike a discount rule, it applies only when the code is entered. Where to find it: Pricing > Coupons. Permissions: coupons.view, coupons.create, coupons.update, coupons.delete. Your plan must include Coupons. Coupons list with code, value and uses"},{"h":"Create a coupon","a":"create-a-coupon","t":"Click New coupon and choose one of: One coupon: you choose the code, for example WELCOME10. Letters, numbers, dashes and underscores, up to 40 characters. Many coupons: enter a prefix and how many codes to make (up to 500 at a time). Codes look like SUMMER-K7M2QX and share the same settings. Field What it does Name For your own reference Type, Value Percentage (up to 100) or Fixed amount Branch One branch, or All branches Customer Group One customer group, or Any customer Min. sale amount The basket needed before the code works Start date, End date When the code is valid Total uses How often the code can be used in all Uses per customer Needs a customer on the sale Can be combined with automatic sale discounts Whether it can be used together with a sale-level discount rule Status Inactive switches the code off"},{"h":"Use a coupon at the POS","a":"use-a-coupon-at-the-pos","t":"Select Coupon in the POS bottom bar (Alt+K), type the code and select Apply. The till says why when a code is refused: expired, used up, basket too small, wrong branch or customer, or a customer is needed. Remove takes it off. One coupon can be used per sale. A sale with a coupon that is waiting for payment holds one use until it is completed or cancelled. Gift cards in the basket are not discounted. A coupon that has been used cannot be deleted. Switch it off instead."},{"h":"Coupons report","a":"coupons-report","t":"Reports > Coupons report (reports.financial) shows each code's uses, total discount and last use, with Export CSV."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Discount rules POS terminal Previous Discount Rules Next Gift cards Create a coupon Use a coupon at the POS Coupons report Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/pricing/customer-groups/","ti":"Customer Groups","c":"Tax & Pricing","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"A customer group segments your customers. Assign price lists to a group and its customers get those prices automatically at the POS. Discount rules can also be limited to a group. Where to find it: Tax & Pricing > Customer Groups. Permissions: customer-groups.view, customer-groups.create, customer-groups.update. Customer group form with price lists"},{"h":"Create a group","a":"create-a-group","t":"Click New Customer Group. Enter a Name (unique). Set Status. Inactive stops new customers from being assigned to the group. Under Price Lists for this Group, tick the active price lists that apply. Click Save Customer Group. Use the toggle in the list to activate or deactivate a group. Groups cannot be deleted."},{"h":"Put customers in a group","a":"put-customers-in-a-group","t":"Edit a customer and choose the Customer Group (see Customers). When that customer is on a sale, the group's price lists and group-specific discount rules apply."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Price lists Discount rules Customers Previous Price Lists Next Discount Rules Create a group Put customers in a group Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/pricing/discount-rules/","ti":"Discount Rules","c":"Tax & Pricing","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"A discount rule gives an automatic discount at the POS when its conditions are met. No code or manual entry is needed. For a code the cashier enters, use coupons. Where to find it: Tax & Pricing > Discount Rules. Permissions: discount-rules.view, discount-rules.create, discount-rules.update. Discount rule form"},{"h":"Create a rule","a":"create-a-rule","t":"Click New Discount Rule. Fill in the fields below. Click Save Discount Rule. Field What it does Name Shown in reports and the list. Unique. Type Percentage (up to 100) or Fixed (a flat amount off). Value The percentage or amount. At least 0.01, two decimals. Scope Product, Variant or Sale. Branch Limit to one branch, or All branches. Customer Group Limit to one customer group, or Any customer. Status Inactive stops the rule applying, without deleting it. Start date / End date Optional. The rule only applies between them. The end must be after the start. Min. quantity Optional. Quantity of the item in the cart needed (Product and Variant scope). Min. sale amount Optional. Sale subtotal needed (Sale scope). Products / Variants Required for Product and Variant scope. Search, Select all or Clear all."},{"h":"How rules are applied","a":"how-rules-are-applied","t":"Product and Variant rules discount each matching line. The price they discount is the price list price if one applies, otherwise the product's price. If several rules match a line, only the single best one (largest amount) is used; they do not stack. A rule never takes a line below zero. Sale rules discount the whole basket once the subtotal reaches Min. sale amount. Again the best single rule wins, and the discount is shared across the lines. A fixed amount is capped to the basket. Tax is calculated on the amount after the discount. See Tax rates and groups. note A product's own Discounted price (set on the product) is separate from discount rules. It becomes the starting price that rules then discount."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Price lists Customer groups POS terminal Previous Customer Groups Next Coupons Create a rule How rules are applied Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/pricing/gift-cards/","ti":"Gift cards","c":"Tax & Pricing","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Sell gift cards at the till and accept them as payment. Every card keeps a full history of its balance. Where to find it: Pricing > Gift cards. Permissions: gift-cards.view (see), gift-cards.sell (sell), gift-cards.manage (adjust, extend, disable, settings). Your plan must include Gift cards. Gift cards list with balance and expiry"},{"h":"Sell a gift card","a":"sell-a-gift-card","t":"On the POS select Gift card in the bottom bar (Alt+G). Enter the amount, and optionally the recipient and a note. Select Add to sale and take payment. The card becomes active, and its code is printed, once the sale is paid in full. Until then it is Pending. A gift card cannot be bought with another gift card."},{"h":"Pay with a gift card","a":"pay-with-a-gift-card","t":"In the payment window open Pay with a gift card, enter the code, select Check balance, set the amount and select Apply. Several cards can be used, and the rest is paid another way. Too many wrong codes lock the lookup for a short time."},{"h":"Manage a card","a":"manage-a-card","t":"Search by code or recipient, and filter by status and expiry. Staff without gift-cards.manage do not see full codes. Open a card for its History and: Action What it does Adjust balance Adds an amount, or takes off with a minus, with a reason. Larger changes may need a manager Extend expiry Sets a new expiry date Disable / Enable Stops the card being spent, or allows it again Statuses: Pending, Active, Used up, Expired, Disabled. A card cancelled by a refund or a cancelled sale cannot be enabled again."},{"h":"Settings","a":"settings","t":"Settings > Gift cards (gift-cards.manage): Field What it does Validity (months) How long new cards are valid, 0 to 600. 0 means they never expire Restrict to the selling branch When on, a card works only at the branch that sold it Adjustment limit without approval The largest balance change without approval rights Some countries set a minimum validity for gift cards, so check the rules where you trade. Expired cards are closed by a nightly job, which needs the cron job."},{"h":"Gift cards report","a":"gift-cards-report","t":"Reports > Gift cards report (reports.financial) shows cards sold, spent, refunded back, expired, cancelled and the outstanding balance. Selling a card is not counted as revenue; revenue is recorded when the card is spent."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"POS terminal Coupons Previous Coupons Next Suppliers Sell a gift card Pay with a gift card Manage a card Settings Gift cards report Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/pricing/price-lists/","ti":"Price Lists","c":"Tax & Pricing","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"A price list holds special prices for specific variants, optionally with a minimum quantity (tiers). It replaces a variant's normal price when it applies to a sale. Where to find it: Tax & Pricing > Price Lists. Permissions: price-lists.view, price-lists.create, price-lists.update, price-lists.delete. Price list form with tiered prices"},{"h":"Create a price list","a":"create-a-price-list","t":"Click New Price List. Enter a Name (unique). Choose a Type: Retail, Wholesale or Custom. This is only a label for your own organisation and does not change how prices apply. Choose a Branch, or leave All branches. Set Status. Under Prices in this List, click Add price for each line: pick the Variant, enter the Price and the Min. quantity (at least 1, or 0.001 for decimal units). Click Save Price List. On an existing list you can add or remove prices one at a time. A variant can have several tiers, but not two with the same minimum quantity."},{"h":"Which list applies","a":"which-list-applies","t":"The list is picked when an item is added to a sale: If the customer belongs to a customer group with active price lists assigned, those lists are used. A list for the current branch wins over an all-branches list, then the newest list wins. Otherwise the newest active list for the current branch that has no customer group, then the newest active all-branches list that has no customer group. A list assigned to a customer group is for that group only. Walk-in customers and customers in other groups never get it. Within the list, the tier with the highest Min. quantity that the sale quantity reaches is used. If the variant is not in the list, its normal price applies. Discount rules are then applied to the list price (see Discount rules)."},{"h":"Archive and delete","a":"archive-and-delete","t":"Use Archive to take a list out of pricing. Items and group links are kept, so Restore brings it back intact. Delete permanently is only for archived lists."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Customer groups Discount rules Products Previous Tax Rates and Groups Next Customer Groups Create a price list Which list applies Archive and delete Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/pricing/tax-rates-and-groups/","ti":"Tax Rates and Groups","c":"Tax & Pricing","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"A tax rate is a single tax such as VAT or GST. A tax group bundles one or more rates (for example CGST + SGST). You assign a tax group to a product or variant, and its rates are applied whenever that item is sold. Where to find it: Tax & Pricing > Tax Rates and Tax Groups. Permissions: tax-rates.* and tax-groups.* (view, create, update). Tax group form with its rates"},{"h":"Create a tax rate","a":"create-a-tax-rate","t":"Open Tax Rates and click New Tax Rate. Enter a Name. It must be unique. Enter the Rate (up to 4 decimals) and choose the Type. Set Status and click Save Tax Rate. Type What it does Percentage A share of the price. 0 to 100. Fixed A flat amount charged per unit sold, regardless of price. Setting a rate to Inactive hides it from new tax groups without deleting it."},{"h":"Create a tax group","a":"create-a-tax-group","t":"Open Tax Groups and click New Tax Group. Enter a Name (unique). Under Rates in this Group, tick the rates that apply together. Set Status and click Save Tax Group. Inactive groups no longer appear in the product form's tax group list."},{"h":"Assign a group to a product","a":"assign-a-group-to-a-product","t":"On the product form, pick the Tax Group. For variable products each variant row has its own Tax Group. No tax means no tax is charged."},{"h":"How tax is calculated","a":"how-tax-is-calculated","t":"Price type: in Settings, the Tax card has Price type. Exclusive (tax added on top) adds tax at checkout. Inclusive (tax included in the price) treats the price as already containing the percentage rates. Percentage rates are worked out on the line amount after discounts. In an inclusive setup, the tax is the part of the price that is tax, shared between the group's rates. Fixed rates are always added on top, per unit, even in an inclusive setup. Each rate is rounded to cents on its own, and the total is the sum of those amounts, so receipts always add up. The product form shows a live preview of the tax for the chosen group."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Products Discount rules Price lists Previous Stock Takes Next Price Lists Create a tax rate Create a tax group Assign a group to a product How tax is calculated Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/purchasing/purchase-orders/","ti":"Purchase Orders","c":"Purchasing","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"A purchase order (PO) records what you ordered from a supplier. Receiving it adds the stock to a branch, and you can record payments and returns against it. Where to find it: Purchasing > Purchase Orders. Permissions: purchase-orders.view, purchase-orders.create, purchase-orders.update. Purchase orders list with status tabs and payment status"},{"h":"The list","a":"the-list","t":"Tabs: All, Draft, Ordered, Received, Closed, Cancelled. Filter by supplier, branch, payment status (Unpaid, Partially paid, Paid) and date range, or search by PO number or supplier. Columns include Order total, Paid, Due and Payment Status. You only see branches you have access to."},{"h":"Create a PO","a":"create-a-po","t":"Click New Purchase Order. Under Purchase Order Details choose the Supplier and the Branch the stock will be received into. Optionally set Expected Date and Notes (internal). Under Items, click Add Item and choose the Product (variant), Qty Ordered and Unit Cost. The line total and Total update as you type. Click Save. The PO is saved as a Draft with a number like PO-0001. Only active suppliers and active variants can be ordered. If you have no suppliers yet, the form tells you and links to New supplier."},{"h":"Order lifecycle","a":"order-lifecycle","t":"Status Meaning Draft Editable. Not sent. Ordered Placed with the supplier. Partially received An Ordered PO where some stock has arrived. Received Every item has arrived in full. Closed Finished. Cancelled Cancelled. Mark as Ordered (from Draft): the supplier is emailed. The order date is set to today. The PO needs at least one item. Edit is available on a Draft, or an Ordered PO that has no receipts and no payments. Cancel Order works on Draft or Ordered POs, but is refused if stock has been received (and not returned) or money has been paid. Close Order is available once the PO is Received."},{"h":"Receive stock","a":"receive-stock","t":"On an Ordered PO, use the Receive Stock card. Set Received On (not in the future) and optional Notes. For each item enter Receive now (up to the remaining quantity), or click Receive all remaining. For products that track batches or expiry, enter the Quantity, Batch / lot number and Expiry date of each lot. Click Add another lot if the delivery came in several. Lot quantities must add up to what you receive. A batch number is required for batch-tracked products. Click Receive Stock. Stock is added to the PO's branch. When every item has been received in full the PO becomes Received. Receiving history is listed at the bottom, and Send received notification sends a received email for the quantities received so far."},{"h":"Record payments","a":"record-payments","t":"Use the Payments card on an Ordered, Received or Closed PO that still has a balance. Enter Amount, choose a Payment Method, set the Date and an optional Reference. Click Add payment. You cannot pay more than is Due. Gateway, credit and loyalty methods are not offered. If you pay cash and have an open register shift, a cash-out is added to that shift so your drawer count stays correct. The summary shows Order total, Returned, Paid, Due, Supplier credit and the payment status."},{"h":"Return goods","a":"return-goods","t":"Use the Purchase returns card on the PO. See Purchase returns."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Suppliers Reorder suggestions Purchase returns Batches and expiry Shifts and cash Previous Suppliers Next Reorder Suggestions The list Create a PO Order lifecycle Receive stock Record payments Return goods Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/purchasing/purchase-returns/","ti":"Purchase Returns","c":"Purchasing","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"A purchase return records goods you send back to a supplier. It removes the stock from the branch and reduces what you owe on the purchase order. Where to find it: Purchasing > Purchase Returns. Needs purchase-orders.view to see the list and purchase-orders.update to record a return. Purchase returns list"},{"h":"The list","a":"the-list","t":"Every return, newest first. Search by return number, PO number or supplier. Columns: Return no. (starting PRT-), PO Number, Supplier, Branch, Return date, items, Returned amount, Reason and By."},{"h":"Record a return","a":"record-a-return","t":"Click New purchase return. Search and find the purchase order the goods came from. Only orders with received items still to return are shown. Click Return items. This opens the Purchase returns card on that PO. Set the Return date (not in the future) and an optional Reason. For each item enter Return qty. Can return shows the maximum (received minus already returned). Lines left at 0 are ignored, and at least one line is needed. For tracked products, optionally pick the Batch. The default is Auto (earliest expiry). Click Return to supplier. The PO must be Ordered, Received or Closed. What happens: The quantity is taken out of the PO's branch stock, from the chosen lot or earliest expiry first. Expired lots can be returned. The returned value is quantity times the PO's unit cost. The PO shows the returned amount, and Due and Supplier credit are updated."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Purchase orders Batches and expiry Suppliers Previous Reorder Suggestions Next Expenses The list Record a return Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/purchasing/reorder-suggestions/","ti":"Reorder Suggestions","c":"Purchasing","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Reorder Suggestions lists items at or below their alert level in your current branch, grouped by the supplier you last bought them from, and creates a draft purchase order from them. Where to find it: Purchasing > Reorder Suggestions. Needs purchase-orders.create. Reorder suggestions grouped by supplier"},{"h":"How suggestions are worked out","a":"how-suggestions-are-worked-out","t":"Only active products and variants are considered, in the branch you are working in. An item is listed when its stock is at or below its Alert quantity, or the default low-stock threshold from Settings if it has none. The suggested quantity brings stock up to twice the alert level, less what is already on open Draft or Ordered orders. Whole-number units are rounded up. The unit cost is the cost on the last order that included the variant, otherwise the variant's cost price. Items are grouped under the supplier of that last order. Items never ordered before appear under No supplier yet. If nothing qualifies, the page says Nothing to reorder. Every item is above its alert level or already on order."},{"h":"Create a draft PO","a":"create-a-draft-po","t":"For each group, review the In stock, Alert level, On order, Order and Unit cost columns. Change any Order quantity or Unit cost. Set a quantity to 0 to leave an item out. Under Choose a supplier, pick the supplier (it is preselected for groups with a known supplier). Click Create draft PO. A draft PO opens for the current branch. At least one item must have a quantity above zero. Then follow the normal flow in Purchase orders."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Purchase orders Stock levels Products Previous Purchase Orders Next Purchase Returns How suggestions are worked out Create a draft PO Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/purchasing/suppliers/","ti":"Suppliers","c":"Purchasing","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Suppliers are the people and businesses you buy stock from. You pick one on every purchase order. Where to find it: Purchasing > Suppliers. Permissions: suppliers.view, suppliers.create, suppliers.update, suppliers.delete. Suppliers list with amount owed"},{"h":"The suppliers list","a":"the-suppliers-list","t":"Tabs filter by status. Search by name. Columns: Name, Code, Contact person, We owe this supplier (the unpaid balance on their orders) and Status."},{"h":"Add a supplier","a":"add-a-supplier","t":"Click New supplier. Fill in the form and click Save supplier. Field What it does Active Off hides the supplier from the purchase order form without deleting it. Name Display name. Required and unique among active suppliers. Code Optional short reference, unique. Leave blank to auto-generate. Business name Optional registered or trading name. Contact person, Phone, Email All required. Address line 1, City, Country Required. Address line 2, State / region and Postal code are optional. Tax registration number Optional. Used on purchase invoices. Notes Internal notes, visible to staff only. When you edit a supplier, a Purchasing section shows We owe this supplier, the number of Purchase Orders and their recent orders."},{"h":"Import suppliers","a":"import-suppliers","t":"Click Import suppliers and Download template, fill it in, then upload it (comma-separated, up to 2 MB). Only name is required. Other columns: code, business_name, contact_person, phone, email, status, address_1, address_2, city, state, postal_code, country (2-letter code such as US), tax_reg_no, notes. Skipped rows are listed with the reason."},{"h":"Archive and delete","a":"archive-and-delete","t":"A supplier with purchase orders cannot be archived or deleted. Otherwise use Archive, then Restore or Delete permanently from the archived tab. Archived and inactive suppliers take no new orders."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Purchase orders Reorder suggestions Previous Gift cards Next Purchase Orders The suppliers list Add a supplier Import suppliers Archive and delete Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/reports/inventory-and-expiry/","ti":"Inventory and Expiry Reports","c":"Reports","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The Inventory Report shows what you hold and what it is worth at cost. The Expiry Report lists batches that have expired or will soon. Where to find it: sidebar > Reports > Inventory Report and Expiry Report. Both need reports.inventory. The Expiry Report also needs the plan feature Batch and expiry tracking."},{"h":"Inventory Report","a":"inventory-report","t":"Inventory report with stock value cards Shows current stock for every variant of every product, per branch. It has a Branch filter and no date range. Card What it shows Stock Value Sum of quantity times cost price across the rows. SKU Count Number of variants. Low stock Variants at or below their alert quantity (or the default threshold). Out of stock Variants with zero or less stock. Columns: Product, SKU, Branch, Quantity, Cost Price, Stock Value. The CSV is inventory-report.csv. The default low-stock threshold is set in General Settings."},{"h":"Expiry Report","a":"expiry-report","t":"Expiry report listing batches with days left Lists batches that still have stock. Days are counted from today in the business time zone. \"Expiring\" means within the Expiry warning (days) setting."},{"h":"Filters","a":"filters","t":"Field What it does Branch One branch or All branches. Status All batches with stock, Expired, or expiring within the warning days. Category Limits to one product category (All by default). Apply Reloads the list."},{"h":"Summary and columns","a":"summary-and-columns","t":"Cards show the number Expired, the number expiring within the warning days, and the Value at cost of the filtered batches. Columns: Product, Variant, Batch, Branch, Expiry date, Days left, Quantity, unit cost, Value at cost, status (Expired, Expiring soon or OK). The CSV is expiry-report.csv and is streamed, so large lists export without trouble. note The header bell also warns about low stock and expiring batches. See Notifications."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Reports Overview Stock Levels Batches & Expiry General Settings Previous Sales and Payments Reports Next Purchases and Profit Reports Inventory Report Expiry ReportFilters Summary and columns Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/reports/overview/","ti":"Reports Overview","c":"Reports","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Reports turn your sales, payments, purchases, stock and expenses into totals you can filter by date and branch. Every report can be exported to CSV. Where to find it: sidebar > Reports. Each report needs its own permission (see below). Sales report with date and branch filters and summary cards"},{"h":"The reports","a":"the-reports","t":"Report Permission Question it answers Sales Report reports.sales How much did we sell, and how much was refunded? Payments Report reports.sales How much money came in, and by which method? Purchases Report reports.financial How much did we spend with suppliers? Profit Report reports.financial What is the gross and net profit? Inventory Report reports.inventory What stock do we hold and what is it worth? Expiry Report reports.inventory + plan feature Batch and expiry tracking Which batches have expired or are about to? Coupons report reports.financial + plan feature Coupons How often was each coupon used? Gift cards report reports.financial + plan feature Gift cards What did we sell, and what is still open on gift cards? A menu item only shows if you hold the permission. The Expiry Report is also hidden when your plan does not include batch and expiry tracking. See Roles & Permissions to grant access."},{"h":"Shared filters","a":"shared-filters","t":"The Sales, Payments, Purchases and Profit reports use the same filter bar. Field What it does From / To Limits the report to a date range. Leave both empty for all time. Branch Limits the report to one branch. All branches covers every branch you may access. Apply Reloads the report with your choices. Dates are read in your business time zone. A shop's \"9 October\" starts at the shop's midnight, not UTC midnight. If From is after To, the two are swapped and a notice tells you. An invalid date is ignored and a notice names it. You only ever see branches you are assigned to. Asking for a branch you cannot access shows all of your branches instead. The Inventory and Expiry reports show stock as it is now, so they have no date range, only a Branch filter."},{"h":"Summary cards and table","a":"summary-cards-and-table","t":"Each report starts with summary cards for the whole filtered period, followed by a table that shows 15 rows per page. The cards cover every matching row, not just the page you are on. The table headings stay in view while you scroll."},{"h":"Export CSV","a":"export-csv","t":"Click Export CSV to download the filtered report. The file contains every matching row, not only the current page, and respects your filters. Report File name Sales sales-report.csv Payments payments-report.csv Purchases purchases-report.csv Profit profit-report.csv Inventory inventory-report.csv Expiry expiry-report.csv note In read-only mode (an expired subscription) reports and exports still work. See Billing & Plans."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Sales & Payments reports Inventory & Expiry reports Purchases & Profit reports Roles & Permissions Previous Roles and Permissions Next Sales and Payments Reports The reports Shared filters Summary cards and table Export CSV Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/reports/purchases-and-profit/","ti":"Purchases and Profit Reports","c":"Reports","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The Purchases Report totals your supplier spend. The Profit Report works out gross and net profit from sales, cost of goods and expenses. Where to find it: sidebar > Reports > Purchases Report and Profit Report. Both require reports.financial. Both use the shared date and branch filters."},{"h":"Purchases Report","a":"purchases-report","t":"Purchases report with spend cards Lists purchase orders by order date. Draft and cancelled orders are left out. Totals are net of returns, the same figure used for supplier dues. Card What it shows Total Spend Sum of the orders in the period. Purchase Orders Number of orders. Avg. order value Total spend divided by the number of orders. Pending Receipt Orders that are ordered but not yet received. Columns: Date, PO #, Supplier, Status, Items, Total Cost. The CSV is purchases-report.csv."},{"h":"Profit Report","a":"profit-report","t":"Profit report with gross and net profit cards Built from completed sales in the period. Card How it is worked out Revenue Sale totals minus the tax collected. Tax is owed to the tax authority, so it is not counted as income. Refunds Refunds issued in the period, shown beside revenue. Revenue and profit are before refunds. COGS Cost of the goods sold: each line's unit cost times quantity. Gross Profit Revenue minus COGS. Margin Gross profit as a percentage of revenue. Expenses Expenses dated in the period (branch-filtered if you pick a branch). Net profit Gross profit minus expenses. Net margin Net profit as a percentage of revenue. Columns: Date, Sale #, Revenue, COGS, Gross Profit, Margin. The CSV (profit-report.csv) ends with an Expenses row and a Net profit row. tip Profit is only as accurate as your cost prices. Keep product costs and purchase receipts up to date."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Reports Overview Purchase Orders Expenses Products Previous Inventory and Expiry Reports Next General Settings Purchases Report Profit Report Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/reports/sales-and-payments/","ti":"Sales and Payments Reports","c":"Reports","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The Sales Report totals what you sold. The Payments Report totals what you actually collected and splits it by payment method. Where to find it: sidebar > Reports > Sales Report and Payments Report. Requires reports.sales."},{"h":"Sales Report","a":"sales-report","t":"Sales report summary cards Only completed sales are counted. Use the shared date and branch filters."},{"h":"Summary cards","a":"summary-cards","t":"Card What it shows Revenue Total of completed sales in the period, before refunds, including tax. Sales Number of completed sales. Avg Sale Value Revenue divided by the number of sales. Items sold Total quantity of items on those sales. Refunds Issued Refunds counted by the date the refund was issued, whichever day the sale was made. Net revenue Revenue minus refunds."},{"h":"Table columns","a":"table-columns","t":"Date, Sale #, Customer (shows Walk-in customer when none was chosen), Items, Subtotal, Discount, Tax, Total, Status. The CSV (sales-report.csv) has the same columns."},{"h":"Payments Report","a":"payments-report","t":"Payments report with totals by method Counts only payments with status paid, on completed sales, by the date the payment was made. Card What it shows Total Collected Sum of paid payments in the period. Payment Count Number of payments. By method Amount and percentage share for each payment Method. Table columns: Date, Sale #, Method, Amount, Reference. The CSV is payments-report.csv. tip Revenue and Total Collected can differ. Credit sales add to revenue but only add to collected money when the customer pays later."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Reports Overview Sales Refunds Payment Methods Previous Reports Overview Next Inventory and Expiry Reports Sales ReportSummary cards Table columns Payments Report Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/selling/pos-terminal/","ti":"POS Terminal","c":"Selling","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The POS Terminal is the till. You open a register with starting cash, add products to a cart, take payment and print or send a receipt. Where to find it: Sales > POS Terminal. Requires sales.create. POS terminal with product tiles on the left and the cart on the right"},{"h":"Open the register","a":"open-the-register","t":"Each cashier opens their own register (shift) in the branch they are working in. Until you do, the terminal shows Open Register. Enter the Starting cash amount. This is the opening balance for your sales session. Select Open Register. Each cashier can have one open register per branch, so several cashiers can sell at the same time. Check the branch in the header first if you work in several."},{"h":"The screen at a glance","a":"the-screen-at-a-glance","t":"Header: the scan box, the customer box, Cash in/out, Close Register, a full-screen button and your account menu. Full screen hides the browser bars; press it again or Esc to leave. It is not offered on iPhones. Bottom bar: the sale actions (Hold, Held Sales, Note, Coupon, Gift card, Return and Cancel sale), whether the browser is online, when the register was opened, the layout buttons, the calculator and a keyboard button that shows or hides the key hints on the buttons. Cart: the lines, the customer, the totals and Pay Now."},{"h":"Add products to the cart","a":"add-products-to-the-cart","t":"Scan or type a barcode / SKU in the box at the top, then Add to cart. Tap a product tile. Tiles show stock status (in stock, low stock, out of stock), a New badge and any percentage discount. Use the + and - buttons on a tile to change its quantity. Products with variants show Choose options. Select the variant you need. Weighed or measured products ask for the amount first (for example 1.25 kg). Filter by category (drag the category row sideways if it does not fit), by In stock, Low stock or Out of stock, and by brand; sort by name or price; and switch between grid and list view. A number on Choose options shows how many variants the product has. Products appear 60 at a time and more load as you scroll. Search always covers the whole catalogue. Sold-out products are hidden while browsing but still found by search. Type a count and * before a code to add several, for example 3*CODE. A barcode scanner works wherever the cursor is, not only in the scan box. If a window such as payment or a note is open, the till asks you to close it first. Scanning on the Sale completed! screen starts the next sale with that item. The cart shows each line, the Subtotal, the discounts (Item discounts and Order discount are shown separately when they apply), Tax and the Grand Total. A discounted line shows its unit price struck through. The keyboard icon at the top of the cart lists the keys for working on cart lines. Discounts come from your discount rules; prices follow the customer's price list when one applies. note You cannot sell more than the stock on hand unless Allow stock to go negative is switched on in Settings. Products tracked by batch never go below zero."},{"h":"Batches","a":"batches","t":"For batch-tracked products the cart uses the earliest-expiry batch automatically. If you hold stock-batches.override, you can pick a different batch on the line. Expired batches cannot be chosen when Block sales of expired stock is on."},{"h":"Customer and notes","a":"customer-and-notes","t":"Select the Customer box (F3), type a name or phone number, and choose from the list with the mouse or with the arrow keys and Enter. Leave it as Walk-in customer for anonymous sales. Select New to add a customer on the spot: first name, last name (optional), phone, and group. Needs customers.create. Add and use saves and attaches the customer. Add with all details opens the full form in a new tab. Attaching a customer applies their group pricing, and enables credit sales and loyalty points. Note in the bottom bar (Alt+O) attaches a note to the sale. When loyalty is on, the cart shows the customer's points balance and how many points the sale will earn."},{"h":"Cart and scrolling","a":"cart-and-scrolling","t":"On a computer the cart stays pinned under the header while the products scroll. A long cart scrolls on its own, and the customer, totals and Pay Now stay in view. On small screens the cart is below the products, with a bar at the bottom for the total and payment."},{"h":"Coupons and gift cards","a":"coupons-and-gift-cards","t":"Select Coupon in the bottom bar to apply a coupon and Gift card to sell a gift card with the sale."},{"h":"Hold, resume and cancel","a":"hold-resume-and-cancel","t":"Action What it does Hold Parks the current cart and starts a fresh one. Held Sales Shows the number of parked carts for this branch and opens the list. Select Resume to bring one back. Clear all Removes every item from the cart after you confirm. Cancel sale Discards the cart. Needs sales.cancel. A held sale can be cancelled from the list the same way. These actions do not reload the page: only the cart, held sales, prices and stock change. Your category, search and scroll position stay, and the cursor returns to the scan box. Something scanned while a sale is being held goes to the next sale."},{"h":"Take payment","a":"take-payment","t":"Select Pay Now. The Take Payment window opens, showing the items and total. For one payment method, choose it and enter the Received Amount, or tap Exact or one of the suggested round amounts under the box. Change Due is calculated for you. For several methods, select Split, then Add payment for each one. The last row can fill in whatever is Still to pay. The window shows when the sale is Fully covered or Overpaid by an amount. If a method is set to require a reference (a slip or UPI number), enter it in the Reference field. Select Pay & Complete Sale. Payment methods come from Payment Methods. Online gateways that are switched on (Stripe, Razorpay, Flutterwave, PayPal) also appear. Choosing one sends the customer to the gateway's page, and the sale completes when the payment is confirmed. Online payments wait until the owner's email is verified."},{"h":"Credit sales","a":"credit-sales","t":"If the received amount is less than the total, the remainder can go on the customer's account. This needs both: Allow credit sales (checkout with a balance due) switched on in Settings > Cashier (POS), and a customer attached to the sale. A customer's credit limit is enforced. If a sale would go over it, the till offers Increase limit to raise the limit and continue. Collect the balance later from the customer's page. See Customers."},{"h":"Loyalty points","a":"loyalty-points","t":"With a customer who has spendable points, the payment window shows Use loyalty points. Enter Points to use or select Use max. The points are worth an amount off the sale, limited by your loyalty rules."},{"h":"After the sale","a":"after-the-sale","t":"The window shows Sale completed! with the sale number and change due. From here you can Print the receipt, Send Receipt (SMS/Email) or start a New Sale, which opens at once with fresh stock. The receipt is also available later from Sales."},{"h":"Returns from the till","a":"returns-from-the-till","t":"You can take a return without leaving the POS. Your current cart stays as it is. Needs sales.return. Select Return in the bottom bar (Alt+T). Scan the barcode or QR code on the customer's receipt, or search by sale number, customer name or phone. With an empty box, recent sales are listed. Select the sale. Choose the items, quantities, condition, reason and payout, the same as on the Refunds page, and select Process return. The window shows the amount and refund number. Print receipt prints the updated receipt, and Back to sale returns you to the cart. Resellable items go back into stock and the product tiles update at once."},{"h":"Cash in/out and closing the register","a":"cash-inout-and-closing-the-register","t":"Cash in/out records money added to or taken from the drawer. Choose Cash in or Cash out, an amount, a reason (Float top-up for cash in; Supplier payment, Safe drop or Expense for cash out; Other for either) and a note, which is required for cash out. The dialog closes when it is saved and the till stays as it was. Cash out cannot exceed the cash expected in the drawer. Close Register asks for the Counted cash and an optional note, then ends your shift and opens its report. See Shifts and Cash."},{"h":"Keyboard shortcuts","a":"keyboard-shortcuts","t":"Key Action F2 Product search F3 Customer list F4 Hold Sale F6 Pay. In the payment window, complete the sale (also Ctrl+Enter). On the success screen, New Sale F8 or Alt+C Calculator F9 Held Sales. On the success screen, print (also Alt+P) Alt+N New customer Alt+O Add note Alt+K Coupon code Alt+G Sell gift card Alt+T Return Alt+X Cancel sale Alt+I Cash in/out Alt+R Close Register Alt+1, Alt+2, ... Choose a payment method Alt+Up, Alt+Down Select a cart line Alt+Plus, Alt+Minus Change the selected line's quantity Alt+Q Type the selected line's quantity Alt+Backspace Remove the selected line On a Mac, Alt is the Option key. The keys are shown on the buttons; the keyboard button in the bottom bar hides or shows them, and the till remembers your choice. The layout buttons in the bottom bar switch between cart on the right, cart on the left, or a category list on the left, for this visit only."},{"h":"Settings that change the terminal","a":"settings-that-change-the-terminal","t":"Under Settings > Cashier (POS): cart position (right or left), tile size (Compact, Comfortable, Spacious), default category, \"New\" badge duration, show the tax line in the cart, show \"from $X\" on tiles with several prices, and play a sound when an item is added."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Sales Coupons Gift cards Refunds Shifts and Cash Customers General Settings Previous Dashboard Next Sales Open the register The screen at a glance Add products to the cartBatches Customer and notesCart and scrolling Coupons and gift cards Hold, resume and cancel Take paymentCredit sales Loyalty points After the sale Returns from the till Cash in/out and closing the register Keyboard shortcuts Settings that change the terminal Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/selling/quotations/","ti":"Quotations","c":"Selling","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"A quotation is a formal offer with the same prices and taxes a sale would use. It does not reserve or deduct stock. When the customer agrees you convert it into a draft sale at the POS. Where to find it: Sales > Quotations. Requires quotations.view and a plan that includes the Quotations feature. Creating needs quotations.create, editing and status changes quotations.update, deleting quotations.delete, and converting also needs sales.create. Quotation form with customer details, items and summary"},{"h":"Statuses","a":"statuses","t":"Status Meaning Draft Saved, not yet given to the customer. Can be edited and deleted. Sent You marked it as given to the customer. Can still be edited. Accepted The customer agreed. Can be converted. Rejected The customer declined. Expired Past its Valid until date while Draft or Sent. Cannot be sent, accepted or converted until you extend the date. A refusal can still be recorded. Converted Turned into a sale. Locked. The list has a tab for each status, a date range and branch filter, and search by quotation number, prospect name or customer name."},{"h":"Create a quotation","a":"create-a-quotation","t":"Go to Sales > Quotations and select New quotation. Fill in the details: Field What it does Branch The store the quotation is for. Converting needs an open shift on this branch. Existing customer Search by name, code or phone. Uses that customer's pricing group. Prospect name, email, phone For someone who is not a customer yet. A name is required when no customer is chosen. Billing address / Shipping address Printed on the quotation. Issue date The date written on it. Valid until Last day the offer stands. Cannot be before the issue date. Expected delivery date Optional promised date. Terms and conditions Payment, delivery or warranty terms. Printed. Customer notes A message for the customer. Printed. Internal notes Visible only to staff. Never printed. Under Items, search for products by name, SKU or barcode and set quantities. Prices and taxes are filled in automatically and cannot be typed. You can add up to 200 lines. Check the Quotation summary. Totals are calculated by the server with the customer's pricing and current tax rules. Sale-wide discounts apply at checkout. Select Save draft."},{"h":"Work the quotation","a":"work-the-quotation","t":"Open it from the list. Available actions depend on status: Edit (Draft or Sent). Mark as sent: records that you gave it to the customer. It does not email anything. Accept or Reject (from Sent). Print: a printable copy for the customer. Delete: drafts only."},{"h":"Convert to a sale","a":"convert-to-a-sale","t":"Open an accepted, sent or draft quotation that has not expired. Select Convert to sale. You need an open shift on the quotation's branch, and you must be working in that branch. The app creates a draft sale in the POS with the same products and quantities, at today's prices. Stock is checked now, not when the quote was written. It shows Please check before taking payment notes for anything that changed: an item no longer available, a price that changed, or low stock. Continue in the POS with Open sale in POS, take payment, and the quotation shows Converted. The customer for the sale is the chosen customer. For a prospect, a customer is created from their details (or linked to an existing one with the same email). With no contact details it becomes a walk-in sale."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"POS Terminal Customers Shifts and Cash Billing & Plans Previous Shifts and Cash Next Products Statuses Create a quotation Work the quotation Convert to a sale Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/selling/refunds/","ti":"Refunds","c":"Selling","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"A refund (return) is recorded against a completed sale. You choose which items come back and in what condition, pay the customer out, and the app updates stock, loyalty points and the sale's refunded total. Where to find it: Sales > Refunds (history and new returns) and Sales > Refund Reasons. Requires sales.return. Return builder with item quantities, condition and payout"},{"h":"Before you start","a":"before-you-start","t":"Open your register. The money leaves your till, so you need an open shift. Otherwise you are sent to the POS with \"Open your register before processing a return.\" Be in the sale's branch. If the sale was made in another branch, switch to it first. Only Completed sales can be returned."},{"h":"Process a return","a":"process-a-return","t":"Go to Sales > Refunds and select New return, or open a completed sale and select New return. At the till, use Return in the bottom bar instead (see below). If you started from the list, enter the sale number (for example SAL-000123) or scan the barcode or QR code on the receipt, and select Find sale. Searching suggests matching sales as you type, by sale number or by the customer's name or phone. For each item, enter the Return qty. The page shows how much is still returnable. Weighed or measured products accept decimals. Set the Condition: Resellable puts the items back into stock; Damaged does not. Pick a Reason (optional) from your active refund reasons. Under Refund payout, choose how to pay the customer back: a single method, or Split between methods. The total must match the refund exactly; the page shows what is Left to pay out. Select Process return. You land on the sale's receipt, which now shows the refund."},{"h":"Returns from the POS","a":"returns-from-the-pos","t":"Cashiers can take a return without leaving the till. Select Return in the POS bottom bar (Alt+T), scan the receipt or search the sale (recent sales are listed), and fill in the same form as above. The cart in progress is kept. When it is done, the window shows the amount and refund number, with Print receipt and Back to sale. See POS Terminal."},{"h":"How the amount is worked out","a":"how-the-amount-is-worked-out","t":"The refund per item is the customer's actual paid share of that line, including its tax and any discount. Returning every unit of a line refunds exactly what was paid for it. A refund can never exceed what the customer actually paid on the sale."},{"h":"Loyalty points","a":"loyalty-points","t":"If part of the sale was paid with points, that share is paid back as points (\"Paid back as points\") and the points earned on the refunded part are taken back. See Loyalty. warning There is no gateway refund integration. For a sale paid through Stripe, Razorpay, Flutterwave or PayPal the refund is only recorded here. Return the money from your payment gateway dashboard."},{"h":"Refund limit and approval","a":"refund-limit-and-approval","t":"Under Settings > Cashier (POS) you can set a Refund limit: the most a user without refund approval can refund in total on one sale. Leave it empty or 0 for no limit. Users with the refunds.approve permission are not restricted. Others see \"Ask a manager to approve it.\""},{"h":"Refund history","a":"refund-history","t":"Sales > Refunds lists every return, newest first, with its refund number, sale, amount and payout methods. Search by refund number or sale number."},{"h":"Refund Reasons","a":"refund-reasons","t":"Reasons are the choices cashiers pick when processing a return. New businesses start with Changed mind, Damaged or faulty, Wrong item, Expired and Other. Open Sales > Refund Reasons. Select Add refund reason, enter a name (names must be unique) and save. Use the edit, activate/deactivate or delete actions on a row to manage existing reasons. Only active reasons appear in the return form."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Sales Shifts and Cash Roles & Permissions Payment Methods Previous Sales Next Shifts and Cash Before you start Process a return Returns from the POSHow the amount is worked out Loyalty points Refund limit and approval Refund history Refund Reasons Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/selling/sales/","ti":"Sales","c":"Selling","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The Sales page lists every sale made in the branches you work in. Open a sale to see its items, payments and timeline, print its receipt, collect a balance, cancel it or start a return. Where to find it: Sales > Sales. Requires sales.view. Sales list with status tabs and filters"},{"h":"Sale statuses","a":"sale-statuses","t":"Status Meaning Completed Fully paid and finalised. Open A credit sale that still has a balance due. Cancelled Cancelled before any payment. Its stock went back to the shelf. Carts that are still being built or are on hold at the POS do not appear here."},{"h":"Find a sale","a":"find-a-sale","t":"Use the tabs: All, Completed, Open, Cancelled. Type in the search box: \"Search by sale number, customer or phone\". Narrow down with the filters: payment status (Paid, Due, Partially refunded, Fully refunded), branch, cashier, payment method and a date range. The list only includes branches you have access to."},{"h":"Open a sale","a":"open-a-sale","t":"Select a sale to see: Sale Summary: sale number, date, branch, cashier, customer, and totals (subtotal, discount, tax, grand total). Items with SKU, quantity, unit price and tax. Payments, each with method, status, reference and time. Failed payments are struck through and not counted. Sale Timeline and any refunds against the sale."},{"h":"Actions on a sale","a":"actions-on-a-sale","t":"Action When it shows Permission Receipt Completed and cancelled sales sales.view New return Completed sale that is not fully refunded sales.return Cancel sale Open sale with no payment received yet sales.cancel Collect Payment Open sale with a balance due sales.create Check payment status A pending online payment on an open sale sales.create"},{"h":"Collect a balance","a":"collect-a-balance","t":"On an open sale, use the Collect Payment card: choose the payment method, enter the amount (and a reference if the method needs one) and submit. When the balance reaches zero the sale becomes Completed. You can also collect against a customer's whole account from Customers."},{"h":"Cancel an open sale","a":"cancel-an-open-sale","t":"Cancel sale returns the items to stock and removes the amount owed. A sale that already has a payment cannot be cancelled; use a refund instead."},{"h":"Receipts","a":"receipts","t":"The receipt page prints or shows the sale for the customer. Its layout comes from Settings > Receipt template: paper size (58mm, 80mm or A4), optional logo, customer, cashier, SKU, tax breakdown, barcode, QR code and batch, plus header text, return policy and footer. It also shows loyalty points earned, used and the balance when loyalty is on."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"POS Terminal Refunds Customers General Settings Previous POS Terminal Next Refunds Sale statuses Find a sale Open a sale Actions on a saleCollect a balance Cancel an open sale Receipts Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/selling/shifts-and-cash/","ti":"Shifts and Cash","c":"Selling","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"A shift is one cashier's register session in one branch, from opening cash to the final cash count. Shifts tie every sale, refund and cash movement to a cashier and show whether the drawer balances. Where to find it: Sales > Shifts. Requires shifts.view. Opening and closing a register happens on the POS Terminal (sales.create). Anyone can open the report of their own shift. Shift report with payment breakdown and cash reconciliation"},{"h":"The shift life cycle","a":"the-shift-life-cycle","t":"Open: on the POS Terminal enter the Starting cash amount and select Open Register. Sell: sales, cash refunds and cash movements are recorded against the shift. Move cash: use Cash in/out for money added to or removed from the drawer. Close: select Close Register, enter the Counted cash and an optional note, and confirm. A cashier has one open shift per branch at a time. A held sale resumed later is attached to the shift that is open then."},{"h":"Cash in/out","a":"cash-inout","t":"Field What it does Cash in / Cash out Cash in is money you add to the drawer. Cash out is money you take from it. Amount A positive number. Cash out cannot exceed the cash expected in the drawer. Reason Float top-up (cash in), Supplier payment, Safe drop, Expense (cash out) or Other (either). Shown on the shift report. Note Detail such as who was paid. Required for cash out. Cash paid for an expense or to a supplier from a register is recorded as an automatic cash out on that shift. See Expenses."},{"h":"Expected cash and difference","a":"expected-cash-and-difference","t":"The drawer should hold: opening cash + cash sales - cash refunds + cash in - cash out Card, wallet and other non-cash payments are not in the drawer, so they are left out. When you close, the Difference is the counted cash minus the expected cash. Zero is perfect; negative means the drawer is short, positive means it is over. After closing you see \"Register closed. Cash difference: ...\" and land on the shift report."},{"h":"Shifts list","a":"shifts-list","t":"Sales > Shifts shows all shifts in your branches. Filter by date range, branch and cashier, and tick Only shifts with a difference to see closed shifts where the count did not match. The Per cashier summary shows shifts, sales total and net difference for each cashier. Select Export CSV to download the list."},{"h":"Shift report (Z-report)","a":"shift-report-z-report","t":"Open a shift to see: Opening cash, Expected cash, Counted cash and Difference. Payment breakdown: everything received by payment method, including non-cash. Cash sales, Cash refunds, Cash in and Cash out. The cash movements with reasons, the sales made in the shift and the refunds issued. Print Z-report for a paper copy. Closed shifts show the figures stored at closing. Open shifts show live figures. The Dashboard also lists open shifts. See Dashboard."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"POS Terminal Refunds Expenses Roles & Permissions Previous Refunds Next Quotations The shift life cycle Cash in/out Expected cash and difference Shifts list Shift report (Z-report) Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/settings/backups/","ti":"Backups","c":"Settings","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Your business has no backup screen of its own. Backups are whole-database dumps taken by the platform administrator for every business together. Where to find it: not in the shop panel. Backups are managed in the platform panel under Settings, and need the platform permission backups.manage."},{"h":"What this means for you","a":"what-this-means-for-you","t":"Nightly database backups are scheduled at 02:00 by the platform, when automatic backup is on. The platform decides how many recent copies to keep (14 by default; it is adjustable between 3 and 90). You cannot download or restore a backup from the shop panel. Ask your platform administrator if you need a restore. note The plan feature labelled Daily owner summary (internally feature.backups) controls the Owner Summary, not backups."},{"h":"Keep your own copy","a":"keep-your-own-copy","t":"Owners can download all of their business records at any time with Data Export. It produces a zip of CSV files and uploaded pictures, and it keeps working even when your subscription is read-only. If you host this application yourself, see Cron Jobs so the nightly backup runs,."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Data Export Owner Summary Cron Jobs Previous Owner Summary Next Languages What this means for you Keep your own copy Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/settings/data-export/","ti":"Data Export","c":"Settings","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Data export gives the owner a zip file with every record of the business as CSV files, plus your uploaded pictures and receipts. Where to find it: sidebar > System > Settings, Your data card at the bottom. Requires settings.manage and data.export, which only the Owner has. Your data card with Include pictures and receipts option"},{"h":"Export your data","a":"export-your-data","t":"Open Settings. In Your data, tick or untick Include pictures and receipts. Click Export my data. The browser downloads <business code>-data-<date>.zip. It is built while you wait, so a large business can take a while. Leave the page open."},{"h":"What is in the zip","a":"what-is-in-the-zip","t":"Item Contents tables/*.csv One CSV per kind of record: products, sales, customers, stock movements, purchases, expenses, settings, team and more. UTF-8, opens in Excel or Sheets. files/ Product pictures, logos and member avatars, when pictures are included. manifest.json Business name, time generated, row count per table, and which columns were left out. Passwords, gateway secrets and tokens are never included. Gateway and SMTP secret settings are left out. If your files total more than 1 GB they are omitted and the manifest says so."},{"h":"Limits","a":"limits","t":"Up to 3 exports per hour per business. Only one export can run at a time. A business with more than 2,000,000 rows cannot be exported this way. Ask your platform administrator. Each export is written to the Audit Log as data_exported. Export still works when your subscription is read-only."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Backups Audit Log Billing & Plans Previous Languages Next Billing and Plans Export your data What is in the zip Limits Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/settings/email-settings/","ti":"Email Settings","c":"Settings","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Email settings choose the mail account your business sends from. Email templates let you edit the wording of every email the system sends. Where to find it: sidebar > System > Settings > Messaging > Email settings and Email templates. Requires settings.manage. Email settings form with SMTP server fields and test email box"},{"h":"SMTP server","a":"smtp-server","t":"Leave SMTP host empty to use the system's default mail setup. Fill it in to send from your own mail account. Field What it does SMTP host Your mail server, for example smtp.yourdomain.com. Port Required when a host is set. 1 to 65535. Username Mail account login. Password Stored encrypted. When one is saved, leave the field blank to keep it. Encryption TLS, SSL or None. From email Required when a host is set. The address your emails come from. From name Name shown to the recipient. Click Save."},{"h":"Send a test email","a":"send-a-test-email","t":"Enter an address in the test box. Click Send test email. The test uses the details currently on the form, even before you save, so you can check they work. It needs your own SMTP host: with no host the test is refused. The host must be a public mail server, not this server or a private network address. Test sending is limited to 5 per minute."},{"h":"Email templates","a":"email-templates","t":"Open Email templates to see every email the system can send, grouped as Emails to suppliers, Emails to customers and Emails to the owner. Email Sent when Purchase order placed A purchase order is marked as ordered (to the supplier). Purchase items received Stock is received against an order (to the supplier). Purchase return recorded Goods are returned to the supplier. Sale receipt After a sale at the POS (to the customer). Refund confirmation A refund is recorded (to the customer). Payment received A payment is collected on an open sale (to the customer). Loyalty points expiring A few days before some of a customer's points expire. Daily summary Each evening, to the owner. See Owner Summary. The list shows each email's Status (On or Off), the languages it is Customized in, or Default wording. Use Deactivate / Activate to switch an email off or on."},{"h":"Edit a template","a":"edit-a-template","t":"Click Edit on an email. Pick the language to edit. Each language has its own wording. Change the Subject and Message. Add optional CC and BCC addresses. Insert Placeholders from the list where you want real values, for example the customer name or sale number. They are replaced when the email is sent. Click Save. Reset to default wording removes your customisation for that language."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"SMS Settings Owner Summary General Settings Previous Payment Methods Next SMS Settings SMTP server Send a test email Email templatesEdit a template Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/settings/general-settings/","ti":"General Settings","c":"Settings","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Settings is where you describe your business and tune how the panel and the POS behave. One page holds most sections as tabs, and a few other pages (payment methods, email, SMS, daily summary) open from the same menu. Where to find it: sidebar > System > Settings. Requires settings.manage. Settings page with the section list on the left"},{"h":"How the page works","a":"how-the-page-works","t":"The section list on the left is grouped: General (Appearance, Business, Brand, Money & tax), Sales (Receipt template, Cashier (POS), Payments, Payment Methods, Loyalty), Messaging (Email settings, Email templates, SMS settings, SMS templates) and Alerts & backups (Daily summary). The tabs on this page share one form. Click Save settings to save every tab at once. A bar shows Unsaved changes and nothing is applied until you save. A red ! badge on a section marks a field that needs attention after a failed save. Loyalty only shows if you hold loyalty.manage. See Loyalty. Sections your plan does not include (for example Loyalty, Gift cards, SMS settings, SMS templates or Daily summary) are hidden from the list. See Billing and plans."},{"h":"Appearance","a":"appearance","t":"Choose how the admin looks. Changes apply to everyone in the business once you save, and you can preview them first. Field What it does Accent color Colour of buttons, links, toggles and charts. Pick a suggested swatch, choose Custom, or type a 6-digit hex value. Reset returns to the built-in palette. Text on accent Colour of labels on accent-filled buttons: Auto, White or Dark. A badge warns when the contrast is Hard to read. Default theme What people see until they choose their own: Light, Dark or System. Font One of the curated fonts, used across the whole admin. Guided tour Switch for showing the system tour to users. Setup guide Reopen brings back the setup checklist. See Setup Wizard."},{"h":"Business","a":"business","t":"Identity and contact details printed on receipts and reports. Field What it does Business name Required. Legal name Fill in if it differs from the trading name. Tax registration no. Your tax or VAT number. Phone, Email, Website Contact details. Street, Unit / suite, City, State / region, Postal code Your address. Country Required. United States, United Kingdom, India, Canada, Australia, Germany, France, United Arab Emirates, Singapore or Other."},{"h":"Brand","a":"brand","t":"Your name and logos. PNG, JPG or WebP up to 1 MB each (the favicon also accepts ICO, up to 512 KB). Field What it does App name Shown in the sidebar and browser tab. Blank uses the default. Logo Main logo. Logo for dark mode Logo used on the dark theme. Icon Compact icon. Favicon Browser tab icon."},{"h":"Money & tax","a":"money--tax","t":"How prices are written and the tax added at checkout. Field What it does Regional presets One click fills the currency format for US, Euro, UK or India. You can adjust anything afterwards. Currency USD, EUR, GBP or INR. Symbol The currency symbol shown with amounts (up to 6 characters). Thousands separator Comma (1,234), Dot (1.234), Space (1 234) or None (1234). Decimal separator Dot (12.50) or Comma (12,50). Put the symbol before the amount Places the symbol before or after the number. Default tax rate (%) Charged on taxable products at checkout. 0 to 100. Price type Exclusive (tax added on top) or Inclusive (tax included in the price). Date format 2026-10-07 (year-month-day), 07/10/2026 (day/month/year), 10/07/2026 (month/day/year) or 07 Oct 2026. Time format 24-hour (22:20) or 12-hour (10:20 PM). warning Changing the currency does not convert existing product prices. A notice appears after saving with a Review product prices link. Past sales and refunds keep the currency they were made in. For tax rates and groups beyond the default rate, see Tax Rates & Groups."},{"h":"Receipt template","a":"receipt-template","t":"Controls what prints on the customer receipt. Field What it does Paper size 58 mm thermal roll, 80 mm thermal roll or A4 sheet. Sets width and column layout. On a roll the print page is exactly as long as the receipt, so nothing is cut off and no blank paper is fed. A4 sheet prints an invoice layout with a Billed to box and a list of payments. Text size Small, Normal (default), Large or Extra large. A sample below the field shows the result. Text thickness Normal or Bold (darker). Choose Bold if the printed text looks too light, which is common on thermal printers. Print logo at the top Includes your logo. Print customer name + phone Includes the customer. Print cashier name Includes the cashier. Print SKU under each item Adds the SKU line. Print tax breakdown Shows tax per rate. Print sale barcode Adds a barcode of the sale number. Print QR code Adds a QR code of the sale number. Scanning it into a search box, for example when taking a return, finds the sale. Print batch and expiry under tracked items For batch-tracked products. Header text Up to 500 characters, printed above the items. Usually shop name, address and tax number. Footer text Up to 200 characters, printed below the totals. A thank-you note or social handle. Return policy Up to 500 characters, printed at the very bottom in fine print."},{"h":"Cashier (POS)","a":"cashier-pos","t":"Tunes the checkout screen. See POS Terminal. Field What it does Cart position Beam puts the cart on the right (default). Lane puts it on the left. Tile size Compact fits more per row, Comfortable is balanced (default), Spacious is easier to tap. Default category The category tab selected when the screen opens. All categories by default. \"New\" badge duration (days) Products added within this many days show a \"New\" badge. 0 turns it off. Show the tax line in the cart Toggle. Show \"from $X\" on tiles with multiple prices Toggle. Play a sound when an item is added to the cart Toggle."},{"h":"Inventory","a":"inventory","t":"Field What it does Default low stock threshold Used for products with no alert quantity of their own. Products at or below it in the current branch show a Low badge. Allow stock to go negative Lets sales continue at zero stock. Batch-tracked products never go below zero. Block sales of expired stock Expired batches are skipped at the till and in transfers. Write-offs and supplier returns can still take them. Expiry warning (days) Batches expiring within this many days are flagged in the cart and in the Expiry Report. 0 to 365."},{"h":"Sales","a":"sales","t":"Field What it does Allow credit sales (checkout with a balance due) Lets a customer leave with an unpaid balance. Refund limit The most a user without refund approval can refund in total on one sale. Empty or 0 means no limit."},{"h":"Payments","a":"payments","t":"Lets customers pay by card or UPI at checkout through an online gateway. Choose Stripe, Razorpay, Flutterwave or PayPal from the Gateways list. A coloured dot shows whether it is off, configured, or missing credentials. Payments tab with gateway list and Test/Live switch Field What it does Enabled Turns the gateway on. It is active only when the credentials for the selected mode are saved. Mode Live uses live credentials and takes real payments. Test uses the separate test credentials and moves no real money. Credentials Stripe: Publishable key, Secret key, Signing secret. Razorpay: Key ID, Key Secret, Webhook secret. Flutterwave: Public key, Secret key, Secret hash. PayPal: Client ID, Client secret, Webhook ID. Webhook URL Copy it into the gateway's dashboard so payments confirm even if the customer's browser never returns. Secret values are stored encrypted and shown as Saved. Click Replace to change one; leave it blank to keep it. Live and test credentials are kept separately, so you can switch modes without retyping. PayPal only appears at checkout when it supports your currency. A gateway in Test mode is labelled Test mode at checkout. For cash, card terminal, UPI and other manual methods, see Payment Methods."},{"h":"Your data","a":"your-data","t":"Owners also see a Your data card at the bottom of Settings. See Data Export."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Payment Methods Email Settings Owner Summary Data Export Setup Wizard Previous Purchases and Profit Reports Next Payment Methods How the page works Appearance Business Brand Money & tax Receipt template Cashier (POS)Inventory Sales Payments Your data Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/settings/languages/","ti":"Languages","c":"Settings","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The panel can be shown in any language the platform has switched on. Each person picks their own language from the header. Where to find it: the globe button in the top bar. No permission needed. The button only appears when more than one language is active. Language dropdown in the top bar"},{"h":"Switch your language","a":"switch-your-language","t":"Click the globe button in the header. It shows the current language code. Under Select language, choose a language by its native name. The page reloads in that language and the choice is remembered for your session. It affects only you, not other team members. The same switcher is on the login pages and public pages."},{"h":"Included languages","a":"included-languages","t":"The application ships with English (en), Hindi (hi), Arabic (ar) and French (fr) translation files. Which of them appear in the menu depends on what the platform administrator has enabled. Languages written right to left, such as Arabic, switch the whole panel to a right-to-left layout."},{"h":"Add or edit a language","a":"add-or-edit-a-language","t":"Adding a language, editing its translations, disabling it, setting the default and marking it right-to-left are done by the platform administrator, not from the shop panel. A new language starts as a copy of English, so nothing shows blank until it is translated. note Email and SMS templates keep separate wording per language. See Email Settings."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Email Settings Profile Navigating the Panel Previous Backups Next Data Export Switch your language Included languages Add or edit a language Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/settings/owner-summary/","ti":"Owner Summary","c":"Settings","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The daily summary is a short report of the day, emailed to the owner each evening and optionally sent as a text message. Where to find it: sidebar > System > Settings > Alerts & backups > Daily summary. Requires settings.manage and the plan feature Daily owner summary. Daily summary settings with send time and recipients"},{"h":"What the summary contains","a":"what-the-summary-contains","t":"Number of sales and sales total for the day. Refunds total and net total. Payments split by method. Low-stock count and items. Count of expiring batches. Top sellers (the five best by quantity)."},{"h":"Settings","a":"settings","t":"Field What it does Send the daily summary Master switch. Send at (business time) Time of day, in your business time zone, from 00:00 to 23:50. A time before 06:00 reports the day that just ended, for shops that close after midnight. Send to Email address of the recipient. Only the Owner can change it. Others see it read-only. Also send a short text message Adds an SMS version. Only shows once an SMS gateway is active; otherwise a link to SMS settings appears. Phone number for the text Number that receives the text. Owner-only. Click Save changes."},{"h":"Send a test now","a":"send-a-test-now","t":"Click Send a test now to send today's report immediately. A message confirms \"A test summary was sent.\" or tells you to check the email address and the email settings."},{"h":"How it is sent","a":"how-it-is-sent","t":"The server checks every 10 minutes and sends each business its report once the local send time has passed. This relies on the scheduler cron job. See Cron Jobs. The email uses your Email Settings if you set an SMTP host, and the Daily summary email template can be edited or switched off."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Email Settings SMS Settings Dashboard Previous SMS Settings Next Backups What the summary contains Settings Send a test now How it is sent Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/settings/payment-methods/","ti":"Payment Methods","c":"Settings","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Payment methods are the tiles your cashier sees when taking payment. Custom methods record a reference the customer gives you and never contact a gateway. Where to find it: sidebar > System > Settings > Payment Methods. Requires settings.manage. Manual payment methods list with Add payment method button"},{"h":"Built-in methods","a":"built-in-methods","t":"New businesses start with these: Method Type Can be deleted? Cash Cash No Card Card No UPI Digital Yes Bank Transfer Digital Yes Cheque Other Yes Loyalty points Loyalty No Cash, Card and Loyalty points are protected because checkout and refunds rely on them. Turn a protected method off instead of deleting it."},{"h":"Add a method","a":"add-a-method","t":"Click Add payment method. Enter a Name (up to 64 characters). Pick a Type: Cash, Card, Digital or Other. Tick Requires reference if the cashier must type a reference (for example a transaction ID) for each payment. Click Add payment method."},{"h":"Manage a method","a":"manage-a-method","t":"The list shows Method, Type, Requires reference and Status. Use the Active switch to turn a method on or off. Inactive methods disappear from checkout. Click Remove to delete a custom method."},{"h":"UPI settings","a":"upi-settings","t":"The UPI row has UPI Settings with two fields: Field What it does UPI VPA Your UPI ID (Virtual Payment Address) that customers pay into, for example merchant@okbank. UPI Payee Name The name shown in the customer's UPI app. Click Save UPI settings to save. note Online gateways (Stripe, Razorpay, Flutterwave, PayPal) are configured separately under the Payments tab. See General Settings."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"General Settings POS Terminal Payments report Previous General Settings Next Email Settings Built-in methods Add a method Manage a method UPI settings Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/settings/sms-settings/","ti":"SMS Settings","c":"Settings","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"SMS settings connect your business to an SMS gateway. SMS templates control the wording of each text message. Where to find it: sidebar > System > Settings > Messaging > SMS settings and SMS templates. Requires settings.manage and the plan feature SMS. If your plan does not include it, the pages show \"This feature is not included in your plan.\" SMS settings with gateway selector and test SMS box"},{"h":"Choose a gateway","a":"choose-a-gateway","t":"Supported gateways: MSG91, 2Factor and Fast2SMS. Only one is active at a time. Under Active gateway, pick the gateway, or SMS off to send no texts. Enter that gateway's key (MSG91 calls it Auth key, the others API key) and Sender ID. Keys are stored encrypted; leave blank to keep a saved one. Set Default country code, added to phone numbers saved without one (for example 91 for India). Click Save. Save the key first, then select the gateway. Each gateway card has an Open dashboard link to the provider's site."},{"h":"Send a test SMS","a":"send-a-test-sms","t":"Enter a phone number. Add a Template ID / name (if required). MSG91 and 2Factor need one. Click Send test SMS. The test uses the details on the form, even before you save."},{"h":"SMS templates","a":"sms-templates","t":"Open SMS templates for the list of messages. They mirror the email types, except the backup-failure message, and use shorter wording without multi-line item lists. Field What it does Message The text. Keep it short. For DLT gateways it must match the wording you had approved. Gateway template IDs The approved (DLT) template each gateway needs for this message in this language. Only the active gateway's ID is used. Placeholders Replaced with real values when sent, and passed to the gateway as variables in the order they appear. Use Activate / Deactivate on the list to switch a message off, and Reset to default wording to undo your edits. When no gateway is active, a warning says no SMS will be sent."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Email Settings Owner Summary Billing & Plans Previous Email Settings Next Owner Summary Choose a gateway Send a test SMS SMS templates Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/stock/batches-and-expiry/","ti":"Batches and Expiry","c":"Stock","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Batch tracking keeps a product's stock per lot, so you know which delivery it came from. Expiry tracking adds a date to each lot. The system sells the earliest expiry first and, by default, refuses to sell expired stock. Where to find it: switch tracking on per product in Inventory > Catalogue > Products. Lots appear on the product page (Inventory tab, Batches card) and in Reports > Expiry Report. The expiry report and expiry correction require the Batch and expiry tracking feature on your plan. Expiry report with expired and expiring lots"},{"h":"Turn tracking on","a":"turn-tracking-on","t":"Edit a product and open Batches & expiry: Track batches / lot numbers: stock is kept per lot. Track expiry dates: each lot has an expiry date. You can also set a Default expiry date, pre-filled when receiving stock. Existing stock moves into an Opening batch. See Products for the limits on switching tracking off."},{"h":"How lots are created","a":"how-lots-are-created","t":"Lots are created whenever stock comes in on a tracked product: Receiving a purchase order: enter a batch number and expiry per lot. A batch number is required for batch-tracked products. A stock adjustment that adds stock: enter Batch / lot number and Expiry date, or leave the number blank for an automatic batch. A product's Starting quantity or a CSV import row (batch_number, expiry_date). A transfer: each lot arrives with the same number and expiry. Adding stock with the same batch number and expiry date to the same branch tops up the existing lot. An expiry date in the past is refused."},{"h":"How lots are used","a":"how-lots-are-used","t":"When you sell, transfer or remove stock, lots are taken earliest expiry first, then lots with no expiry, then the oldest receipt. Expired lots are skipped. Users with stock-batches.override can pick a specific lot in the POS cart, on adjustments and on transfers."},{"h":"Settings","a":"settings","t":"In Settings, the Inventory card has: Setting What it does Block sales of expired stock Expired batches are skipped at the till and in transfers. Write-offs and supplier returns can still take them. Expiry warning (days) Batches expiring within this many days are flagged in the cart and counted as expiring in the report. Allow stock to go negative Does not apply to batch-tracked products, which never go below zero. Days are counted on the business time zone from the loyalty settings."},{"h":"Batches card","a":"batches-card","t":"On a tracked product's page, the Batches card lists lots that hold stock in your branches: Batch, Branch, Expiry date, Days left and Quantity, earliest expiry first. If you have stock-batches.edit you can correct a lot's expiry date with New expiry date. Only the date changes, never the quantity, and the correction is written to the audit log. It is refused when the lot is empty or another lot with the same number already has that date."},{"h":"Expiry report","a":"expiry-report","t":"Reports > Expiry Report (reports.inventory) lists every lot with stock. Filters: Branch, Status (All batches with stock, Expired, Expiring within N days) and Category. Click Apply. Summary: Expired, Expiring and Value at cost. Columns: Product, Variant, Batch, Branch, Expiry date, Days left, Quantity, Value at cost. Export CSV downloads the list."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Products Stock adjustments Purchase orders Previous Stock Levels Next Stock Adjustments Turn tracking on How lots are created How lots are used Settings Batches card Expiry report Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/stock/stock-adjustments/","ti":"Stock Adjustments","c":"Stock","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"A stock adjustment adds or removes a quantity of one product in one branch, with a reason. The list is the history of all manual changes. Where to find it: Inventory > Stock > Stock adjustments. Needs inventory.view to see the history and inventory.adjust to add one. Stock adjustments history"},{"h":"History","a":"history","t":"The list shows Date, Product, Branch, Change, Balance After, Reason and By. Filter by branch, type (Add stock or Remove stock), user and date range, or search by product, SKU or reason. You only see the branches you have access to."},{"h":"Add an adjustment","a":"add-an-adjustment","t":"Click Add Stock Adjustment. The form opens in a dialog over the list. Choose the Branch. Search for the Product by name, SKU or barcode (type at least 2 characters). The current stock in that branch is shown. Enter Change: a positive number to add, a negative one to remove (for example 10 or -3). This is the amount to add or remove, not the new total. Enter a Reason, or click a common one: Opening stock, Restock, Stock count, Damaged, Expired. Click Add Stock Adjustment. Fields that appear only for tracked products: Field When it shows Batch / lot number Adding stock to a batch-tracked product. Leave blank for an automatic batch. Expiry date Adding stock to an expiry-tracked product. Required unless the product has a default expiry date. It cannot be in the past. Batch Removing stock, only if you have stock-batches.override. The default is Auto (earliest expiry). Rules: Change cannot be zero. Whole numbers only, unless the product's unit allows decimals. Archived products cannot be adjusted. Removing more than a tracked product holds is refused. tip For a full recount of a shelf or branch, use a stock take instead of many adjustments."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Stock levels Batches and expiry Stock takes Previous Batches and Expiry Next Stock Transfers History Add an adjustment Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/stock/stock-levels/","ti":"Stock Levels","c":"Stock","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Stock Levels lists every product and variant with its quantity in the branch you are working in, and lets you correct a quantity on the spot. Where to find it: Inventory > Stock > Stock levels. Needs inventory.view; the Adjust button needs inventory.adjust. Stock levels list with All stock, Low and Out tabs"},{"h":"Read the list","a":"read-the-list","t":"The page header names the branch you are viewing. To see another branch, switch branch first (see Branches). Tabs, each with a count: All stock, Low and Out. Search by product name or SKU, and filter by category, brand and unit. Column What it shows Product Product name and, for variable products, the option such as Size: L. SKU The variant's SKU. Current stock Quantity in this branch. Status Out (zero or less), Low (above zero and at or below the threshold) or Healthy."},{"h":"What counts as low stock","a":"what-counts-as-low-stock","t":"A product is Low when its quantity is at or below its own Alert quantity (set on the product). Products without one use the Default low stock threshold in Settings, in the Inventory card."},{"h":"Adjust stock from the list","a":"adjust-stock-from-the-list","t":"Click Adjust on a row. Choose Add stock or Remove stock and enter How many?. The Set stock to 0 shortcut fills in the full quantity to remove. For products that track expiry, enter an Expiry date when adding stock. Enter a Reason (required) and click Adjust stock. The change is recorded in Stock adjustments."},{"h":"Allow negative stock","a":"allow-negative-stock","t":"In Settings, the Inventory card has Allow stock to go negative. Products tracked by batch never go below zero, whatever this says."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Stock adjustments Stock transfers Batches and expiry Reorder suggestions Previous Print Labels Next Batches and Expiry Read the listWhat counts as low stock Adjust stock from the list Allow negative stock Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/stock/stock-takes/","ti":"Stock Takes","c":"Stock","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"A stock take is a guided physical count of a branch or one category. You enter what you counted, review shortages and surpluses, then approve to update stock. Where to find it: Inventory > Stock > Stock takes. Needs inventory.view to see takes and inventory.adjust to start, count, approve or cancel. This page requires the stock take feature on your plan. Stock take counting sheet"},{"h":"Start a count","a":"start-a-count","t":"Click New stock take. Choose the Branch. Under What to count, choose The whole branch or One category (and pick the Category; its sub categories are included). Add Notes if you like, then click Start counting. The sheet gets one row per active product variant in scope. For lot-tracked products there is one row per lot that holds stock. Only one count can be open per branch at a time. Codes start with ST-."},{"h":"Count","a":"count","t":"The system quantity is hidden while you count. Type the quantity in each Counted box and click Save counts. A row you do not save is left alone, and emptying a box and saving marks it as not counted. Use Scan or type a code (SKU, barcode or lot number) and Find to jump to a row. Enter moves to the next row, Esc returns to the scan box. Not counted yet shows only the rows you have not counted. The search box filters by product, SKU, barcode or lot. Found a lot that is not on the sheet? Use Add lot: choose the Product, then enter the Batch / lot number, Expiry date and Counted quantity. You can leave and return; counts you saved are kept."},{"h":"Review and approve","a":"review-and-approve","t":"Click Review differences. You see the Shortage and Surplus values at cost, the number of rows not counted, and each difference by product and lot. Click Approve and update stock to apply the differences. Rows you did not count are left unchanged. Or click Cancel stock take to discard the counts. No stock changes. Each difference is applied as a stock adjustment with the reason Stock take ST-0001. If a row cannot be applied, approval stops and lists the affected products. After approval the take shows as a read-only result with the differences. The list shows Status, counted rows and the value at cost of the approved take."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Stock adjustments Batches and expiry Stock levels Previous Stock Transfers Next Tax Rates and Groups Start a count Count Review and approve Related"}]},{"u":"docs/shop/stock/stock-transfers/","ti":"Stock Transfers","c":"Stock","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"A stock transfer moves products from one branch to another in a single step. Stock leaves the source branch and arrives at the destination immediately. Where to find it: Inventory > Stock > Stock transfers. Needs inventory.view to see transfers and inventory.transfer to create one. Stock transfers list"},{"h":"Create a transfer","a":"create-a-transfer","t":"Click Add Stock Transfer. Choose From branch (it defaults to your current branch) and To branch. They must be different, and both must be branches you have access to. Optionally add Notes. Click Add Item for each product: choose the Product (and variant) and enter the Quantity. Each product can appear only once. If you have stock-batches.override, you can pick a specific Batch. The default is Auto (earliest expiry). Click Save. Each transfer gets a code starting with TRF-. If any line cannot leave the source branch (not enough stock, only expired lots, a bad batch), the whole transfer is cancelled and nothing moves. For tracked products, each lot taken from the source arrives as the same lot (same number and expiry date) at the destination. Expired lots are left behind when Block sales of expired stock is on."},{"h":"Transfer list and details","a":"transfer-list-and-details","t":"Columns: Code, From branch, To branch, Items, Date and By. Filter by from branch, to branch, user and date, or search by code, product or note. Open a transfer to see its notes, products, batch / lot numbers and quantities. You see a transfer if you have access to either of its branches. note A transfer cannot be edited or undone. To correct a mistake, create a transfer in the opposite direction."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Branches Stock levels Batches and expiry Previous Stock Adjustments Next Stock Takes Create a transfer Transfer list and details Related"}]},{"u":"docs/support/","ti":"Support","c":"","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"Before contacting support, check the FAQs and the relevant page of this documentation."},{"h":"Contact","a":"contact","t":"Topic Who Contact When to use ✉️ General Support Team support@wrteam.in Anything else. Replies within 1 working day. 🛠️ Technical Developer vipul.wrteam@gmail.com · Chat on Microsoft Teams Installation, setup, errors and other technical issues."},{"h":"What to include","a":"what-to-include","t":"Your application version (see the changelog) and PHP version. The PHP version is under Settings > System > System health in the Super admin panel. What you did, what you expected and what happened. Any message on screen, and the latest entries in storage/logs. Screenshots if they help."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"FAQs Installation overview Next FAQs Contact What to include Related"}]},{"u":"docs/third-party-costs/","ti":"Third-party costs","c":"","s":[{"h":"","a":"","t":"The application itself runs on your own hosting. Everything below is optional or depends on how you run the platform. Pricing is set by each provider, so check their sites."},{"h":"Hosting and domain","a":"hosting-and-domain","t":"Item Notes Web hosting or VPS Must meet the server requirements and allow a cron job. Domain name Required for a live site. The Super admin panel can use its own host through ADMIN_DOMAIN. SSL certificate Needed for HTTPS. Many hosts provide one for free. MySQL database Usually included with hosting."},{"h":"Payment gateways","a":"payment-gateways","t":"Businesses pay for their subscription through a gateway you connect in the Super admin panel. The supported gateways are: Stripe Razorpay PayPal Flutterwave Each gateway charges its own transaction fees. You can also record payments manually. See Payment gateways. Shops can also take online payments from their own customers at the POS using their own gateway accounts; fees are billed by the gateway to the shop."},{"h":"Email (SMTP)","a":"email-smtp","t":"Verification, password reset, invitation and billing emails need a mail server. Enter your SMTP details in the Super admin panel under Settings > System email. Many email providers have a free tier. Each business can also set its own mail account in its email settings."},{"h":"SMS","a":"sms","t":"SMS is optional and set up per business in SMS settings. The supported providers are MSG91, 2Factor and Fast2SMS. Each provider bills per message."},{"h":"Purchase code validation","a":"purchase-code-validation","t":"The web installer checks your purchase code against the WRTeam validator. This needs your server to reach it over outbound HTTPS (port 443)."},{"h":"Related","a":"related","t":"Introduction Payment gateways Previous Introduction Hosting and domain Payment gateways Email (SMTP) SMS Purchase code validation Related"}]}];
